	quest.0089B6C20C45DDCA.quest_desc: ["The smeltery applies Fortune IV when smelting ores! "]
	quest.0089B6C20C45DDCA.quest_subtitle: "Fortune IV"
	quest.00A3AD4BD4EE0FC7.quest_desc: [
		"The Guard Tower will employ and house one Guard to protect your colony. Your citizens will appreciate a well guarded colony. A general rule of thumb is two guards for every three citizens."
		""
		"Guards sleep in guard dowers, freeing up the bed they previously occupied in a residence or tavern allowing you to recruit new colonists. "
		""
		"Tip: You can expand your colony border by building and leveling up guard towers."
	]
	quest.00A3AD4BD4EE0FC7.quest_subtitle: "Build a Guard Tower and Hire a Guard"
	quest.00B0676CC76BDDC4.title: "To Dusk"
	quest.00B6C41B39C403E9.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat chac-7.5.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"The CHAC-7.5 Advanced Chainsword utilizes serated blades in its attacks, reducing the target's total health. Subsequent attacks reduce this even further. In addition, the blade's extraterrestrial steel material makes it deal extra damage to technoflesh creatures."
		"Being that it is a machine in nature, it must have a constant source of energy."
	]
	quest.00B6C41B39C403E9.title: "CHAC-7.5 \"Advanced Chainsword\""
	quest.0148D140EF1045FA.quest_desc: ["The airship is a fairly simple vehicle. Opening its inventory, you'll see a slot on the left for fuel. You'll also see some for various upgrades, but they'll have their own moment. For now, just know that fuel can be anything you can use in a furnace."]
	quest.0148D140EF1045FA.title: "Henri's Handiwork"
	quest.01994F72AF7D412B.quest_desc: [
		"To kill The Leviathan is to combat the Abyss itself. You would best prepare yourself for combat in the water, and carry with you Blessed Amethyst Crab Meat, gained by &6&oslaying an Amethyst Crab in Lush Caves and blessing its meat at the Sunken City's Amethyst Altar&r."
		"Knowledge of one's surroundings is key in this battle, as The Leviathan's maw and tentacles will strike as you avoid making contact with the Abyssal Mines floating throughout the arena. &6&oDodge its strikes, projectiles, and mines, and victory may be yours.&r"
	]
	quest.01994F72AF7D412B.title: "Silence Once More"
	quest.019E4643C7FA74EF.quest_desc: [
		"Ivy Oleander is a trader known for her reserved demeanor, extensive travels, and unusually deep understanding of dragon behavior, particularly regarding the Raevyx species. Though outwardly calm and approachable, Ivy is widely associated with the disappearance of numerous Pillager groups and raider encampments across distant regions."
		"Despite maintaining the appearance of an ordinary merchant, rumors surrounding Ivy often describe her as relentless, emotionally detached, and dangerously patient toward those connected to raider activity."
	]
	quest.019E4643C7FA74EF.quest_subtitle: "Meet Ivy Oleander"
	quest.019E4643C7FA74EF.title: "The Lone Dragon Trader"
	quest.01C8FAA27461B5EB.quest_desc: ["An Afrit Miner will not only dig up normal ores, but it will also mine the deepslate variants of ores. Despite its immense power, an Afrit Miner's lamp will deteriorate at a much slower pace, making them excellent helpers."]
	quest.01C8FAA27461B5EB.title: "Afrit Miner"
	quest.01DF52F555D662F0.quest_desc: ["Upon death, A familiar will leave behind a shard of its soul. This shard, when powered by Otherworld Essence, can be used to revive the familiar."]
	quest.01FD933F1E52DA53.title: "16x Coal"
	quest.0200624FDF3F2367.quest_desc: ["Now that you've hopefully gotten some experience with basic fishing, it's time to take things up a notch. &6&oAt a smithing table, you can use string and various materials to upgrade your rod.&r For now, let's get your fishing rod to iron tier."]
	quest.0200624FDF3F2367.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade to an iron fishing rod"
	quest.0200624FDF3F2367.title: "Taking things to the next level"
	quest.020511479F5F4E92.quest_subtitle: "Lava Eater"
	quest.020AD3C5960386EB.quest_desc: ["You can upgrade your chests by surrounding it in material, the first step is usually copper or iron, copper is cheaper though. As you upgrade it, it can be filled with more and more shit, and you can even make further upgrades, like being able to put multiple stacks in a single slot."]
	quest.020AD3C5960386EB.quest_subtitle: "Does not Oxodize"
	quest.020AD3C5960386EB.title: "And A Little Bit of Copper."
	quest.025FD7C068AD4C7E.title: "time 3"
	quest.0272168A10CD6E01.quest_desc: ["Once you've become a lord, you can get a minion. &oYou can only have a number of minions equal to your lord level.&r To recruit a minion, find a weak vampire npc and interact with them holding a Vampire Minion Binding. Moon charms are received as rewards for completing the task, &o\"Minion Control.\"&r"]
	quest.02CD43D7360146B2.quest_desc: ["In a controlled village, there will be a representative of the controlling faction. They will offer you tasks or missions to complete. Once at max level, you can talk to them about becoming a Lord."]
	quest.02CD43D7360146B2.title: "Represent Wolf"
	quest.02E941103844339B.quest_desc: ["Use thes sabbath ritual to summon the Apostle, a boss that won't be easy."]
	quest.02E941103844339B.title: "Sabbath'"
	quest.0348441116732FB4.quest_desc: ["Do the sabbath ritual to fight and kill the apostle"]
	quest.034DBB22E2907A5E.quest_desc: [
		"The werewolf menu shows you options for changing appearance, but more importantly, shows &oyour skill tree.&r"
		"With every level you get, you earn 2 skill points. Now that you've gotten them, it's time to become more in tune and unlock partial transformation. "
		"While in this form, you'll gain some light armor and armor toughness, as well as a boost to speed and damage. You will also gain the ability to &obite&r an enemy. Doing so penetrates some of their armor"
	]
	quest.034DBB22E2907A5E.title: "Become a werewolf (kinda)"
	quest.03C1FFF0D39BAEE5.title: "16x Andesite"
	quest.03D00E8C22516D8B.title: "The Dragon Merchant"
	quest.03D9CFFF0388FBE2.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat crys_gen.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"After numerous failed attempts, researchers succeeded in cryogenically creating a renewable source of the energy crystals required to create many of the newer creations. The area around the machine was deathly cold, however, and required careful extraction. This has opened up a new realm of possibilities."
	]
	quest.03D9CFFF0388FBE2.title: "crs_gen.jv"
	quest.04EE6076E25E4491.quest_desc: [
		"&n&4Your dragon's happiness&r decreases slowly over time, as well as when your dragon takes damage, or when scales are forcibly plucked out. Like hunger, happiness will slowly drain your dragon's stats when reaching below 60, making them slower as it drains. At 30% and below, they will not let you ride them at all."
		"Feeding your dragon their preferred foods will increase their happiness, but the primary method is by brushing them."
		"Dragons are special creatures who require specialized brushes. Of these, there are two variants: a normal brush and a golden brush. &4&nUsing the normal brush on your dragon will increase its happiness by 10 points and the golden brush by 20.&r"
		"In addition to increasing happiness, a brush can be used to obtain scales if used when the brush icon in the Draconic Codex is lit up at 100%. This value increases steadily over time."
	]
	quest.04EE6076E25E4491.title: "Dragon Care 102"
	quest.04FF0DDDE96513F2.quest_desc: [
		"Rotorcraft such as the airship can hover in place and move much like a boat in many cases, using the left and right keys to turn around. Holding &o&6The Space Bar&r will lift you into the air, while holding shift lowers you. Unlike many vehicles and mounts, &o&6exiting the aircraft is done via a keybind (Default: R)&r."
		"The vehicles will require time to take off. You can view this via the meter above your hotbar."
	]
	quest.053F1DAB52A4FACE.title: "Weaponized Toxicity"
	quest.0551FA703A26C8C1.quest_desc: ["In a controlled village, there will be a representative of the controlling faction. They will offer you tasks or missions to complete. Once at max level, you can talk to them about becoming a Lord."]
	quest.0551FA703A26C8C1.title: "Represent Vamp"
	quest.056C6D7E2CDF2E85.quest_desc: ["Like gems, the rune can be added to your weapon in a smithing table. Doing so will cause it to deal 33% more damage in cold biomes"]
	quest.056C6D7E2CDF2E85.title: "Not Quite a Gem"
	quest.059DDAA627A824B9.quest_desc: [
		"You will find the door to Maledictus's chamber guarded by powerful draugr known as &6&oAptgangr&r. These colossal foes are capable of sending shockwaves by slamming the ground with its axe, and charging at their enemies with a death grip."
		"If you manage to kill one, you will obtain the key to the Maledictus's chamber. Make your final preparations, for the time has nearly come."
	]
	quest.059DDAA627A824B9.title: "Master Key"
	quest.05B83606164A1853.quest_desc: [
		"Have you found a place to settle down? Even if temporary, a home is not a home without &6&oa bed to set your spawn and sleep through the night&r. Do note that &6&osleep is not always possible, whether from an event occuring that prevents it, or from nightmares,&r though that second one is easily combatted with a proper home and some light, maybe even a pet or two."
		"Regardless, I, Professor Larch, am certain you will find your way through these harsh nights, and emerge from them even stronger than before."
		"If you're struggling to find wool, I suggest you look for &6&owild flax or industrial hemp seeds&r. Both make for a plentiful supply of string."
	]
	quest.05B83606164A1853.quest_subtitle: "Make a bed to sleep the night away."
	quest.05B83606164A1853.title: "Cozy and Comfortable"
	quest.0626E825BC0B0B77.quest_desc: [
		"&o&6Eterna&r is the most basic attribute. &6&oIt determines the max enchanting level&r. Think of it like regular enchanting. The more Eterna you have, the higher level your enchantments will be. Eterna is mostly increased by using stronger bookshelves, but some items such as magical crystals can also increase it when placed nearby."
		"There are several different bookshelves, but for now, let's just use the basic wooden ones."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/eterna.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0626E825BC0B0B77.title: "Eterna"
	quest.065CC7543DCDC9FC.quest_desc: ["Iron lets you hold EVEN MORE shit. And so on and so forth up to Netherite Teir, it's kinda pretty damn simple after this, each teir gives you some more space, and an extra upgrade slot to do whatever you please."]
	quest.065CC7543DCDC9FC.quest_subtitle: "Reinforced"
	quest.07337A0A95423EB2.quest_desc: ["Once you've obtained a Dimensional Storage Actuator, you can set up a Djinni to operate machines such as furnaces. Using the book of calling, you can set the machine, along with an optional extraction side, useful for blocks like furnaces, alongside the Storage Actuator to take from. Once that's done,"]
	quest.07337A0A95423EB2.title: "Feed The Machine"
	quest.0762152EEDB62151.quest_desc: ["The Tome of Superior Scrapping is an upgraded form of the Tome of Scrapping. &6&oIt does the same as the Tome of Scrapping, but takes all the enchantments instead of just half.&r"]
	quest.0762152EEDB62151.title: "Better Scraps"
	quest.07A6C9A92D352300.quest_desc: ["The Beholder familiar highlights nearby mobs and attacks enemies with lasers. It can also eat Shub Niggurath's babies to gain a boost in speed. When upgraded, it can make its owner immune to blindness."]
	quest.07A6C9A92D352300.title: "Beholder Familiar"
	quest.07C26C046CDE2507.quest_desc: ["The Crusher’s Hut is where the Crusher will take items and crush them into other blocks. Most notably cobblestone = gravel, gravel = sand, sand = clay. One important factor to know is that the crusher has a daily limit based on the hut level. Level 1 has a daily max of 16, level 2 has 64. At level 5 it’s daily max is 999. "]
	quest.07C26C046CDE2507.quest_subtitle: "Build a Crusher's Hut"
	quest.083FB6BC2C2D9609.quest_desc: [
		"Bundles are fantastic, but they can only do so much. At some point, you'll want more than they provide, perhaps an entirely new inventory? Well, I, Professor Larch, know of a way to achieve this. The solution you're looking for is &o&6A Backpack.&r"
		"While more costly than a bundle, a basic backpack is like a chest you can carry around. Wait, those exist, don't they? In that other dimension? Well, not matter. Unlike said boxes, your backpack can be carried on, well, your back via the curios slot. You can quickly deposit an item by hovering the backpack over it and right clicking."
		"Backpacks are capable of so much, but that isn't my subject to teach."
	]
	quest.083FB6BC2C2D9609.title: "Bags Of Holding"
	quest.0846198E310D721E.quest_desc: [
		"The Cindervane is a highly migratory draconic species known for its exceptional endurance and long-distance flight capability. Unlike territorial apex predators, Cindervanes prioritize survival, mobility, and environmental adaptation over prolonged combat engagement. Historically, many ancient civilizations are believed to have relied on established Cindervane migratory routes when constructing trade paths, evacuation corridors, and long-range messenger networks. Cindervanes are also domesticated for the purpose of transportation rather than combat mounts on a daily basis. Their tendency to disperse eggs across wide regions rather than defend centralized nesting grounds has led many researchers to classify the species as ecological carriers rather than territorial rulers. Although not specialized for sustained combat, Cindervanes remain highly dangerous when cornered. &n&4Wild Cindervanes are not hostile unless provoked.&r"
		"Similarly to domesticated wolves and cats, Cindervanes can be tamed through &4&ndirect feeding with preferred foods such as raw chicken, cod, salmon, and Hearty Dragon Meal.&r"
		"Due to their naturally cautious behavior, taming attempts may require multiple feedings before successful domestication occurs."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/cindervane.png width:300 height:180 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0846198E310D721E.quest_subtitle: "Tame a Cindervane"
	quest.0846198E310D721E.title: "Destruction Commence"
	quest.085A943345602261.quest_desc: ["Find a shipwreck and kill its captain (Pillager inside captain's quarters) to obtain the shell horn"]
	quest.085BF7B7C082C75D.quest_desc: ["An Iron Line increases the size of the bar during the fishing minigame, lowering difficulty."]
	quest.085BF7B7C082C75D.quest_subtitle: "Craft an Iron Fishing Line"
	quest.085BF7B7C082C75D.title: "Your Bit of String in Your Hand"
	quest.085F473094778DCD.quest_desc: [
		"The resource scroll is an easy way to tell what one of your Builder needs. Sneak + right-click on a Builder’s Hut to register the resource scroll to the builder."
		""
		"Now when you right-click while holding the resource scroll, you will see all the needed materials for the Builder’s Hut you clicked on."
	]
	quest.085F473094778DCD.quest_subtitle: "Micromanagement at it's finest"
	quest.08B2F084D5F15438.title: "Potion Serum"
	quest.08BE7B461CC437CA.quest_desc: ["The Melter is a Tinker's Best Freind in forging their first tools! The heater is placed underneath the melter and provided with solid fuel, which then melts any item (That's Meltable) Within, it can be taken out with a faucet and a casting basin."]
	quest.08BE7B461CC437CA.quest_subtitle: "Melter Skelter"
	quest.08BE7B461CC437CA.title: "Now your putting the Black in Smith"
	quest.08DB736B07836F38.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat bat-sml.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Using the energy crystals recovered from fallen meteorites and extraterrestrial steel, technicians have put together a special type of battery capable of charging devices made with these extraterrestrial materials."
	]
	quest.08DB736B07836F38.title: "bat-sml.jv"
	quest.08E9141026F7F288.quest_desc: [
		"As I said before, there are two components we will want to acquire. The second of these are &6&ofabrics&r. Made from lapis and some string, a variety of different fabrics can be created by adding one addition ingredient. These all have their purposes, but for ours, we will want &o&6magic fabric&r, made by adding gold to the recipe."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/fabrics.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.08E9141026F7F288.title: "The Fabrics That Bind Us"
	quest.09274D26D87B7EEE.quest_desc: ["The permafrost hook cools down the temperature of the water, making it good for when you're not in the coldest of areas."]
	quest.09274D26D87B7EEE.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Permafrost Hook"
	quest.09274D26D87B7EEE.title: "Water Cooler"
	quest.09A68ADF45EC8501.quest_desc: [
		"You wish to harness the dark arts you've witnessed from those around you? Or perhaps you've found a scroll that piqued your interest. Either way, I welcome you into my dark embrace."
		"&6Goety: The Dark Arts&r is a magic mod with a focus on dark or black magic. You as the caster utilize &6&osoul energy&r and wield &6&ofocuses&r to cast a variety of different spells."
		"Now then, follow me, my new apprentice. We have much to learn."
	]
	quest.09A68ADF45EC8501.title: "Introduction to The Dark Arts"
	quest.09D3034F4376724E.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat chah-06.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"The CHAH-06 Advanced Hand Drill is capable of breaking through rock and metal at extreme speeds compared to that of a traditional pickaxe. Being that it is an advanced machine in nature, &lit lacks a traditional durability&r, and must instead rely on a consistent stream of energy."
	]
	quest.09D3034F4376724E.title: "CHAH-06 \"Advanced Hand Drill\""
	quest.0A02AC6534B3BE3F.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat bat-bld.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Created as part of the Techointegration Project, the informally known \"Bloody Battery\" charges in response to physical trauma. While in posession of it, the user is made more vulnerable as the battery takes in the organic energy that triggered it and spreads it out amongst the various advanced tools and machinery on the wearer, &lturning damage into energy&r."
	]
	quest.0A02AC6534B3BE3F.title: "bat-bld.jv"
	quest.0A064317CD8AE591.quest_desc: ["I... won't ask &owhy&r so many raids have been triggered, but I will congratulate you for fending off each and every one of them... I hope."]
	quest.0A064317CD8AE591.title: "A True Hero of Green"
	quest.0A6C0D80401D7D17.quest_desc: ["A more powerful and intelligent spirit, the Djinni Miner discards most useless blocks, only bringing back the more valuable materials. While it is faster than a Foliot, due to its stronger presence, the lamp housing it will also degrade faster."]
	quest.0A6C0D80401D7D17.title: "Djinni Miner"
	quest.0A73874C00D2C311.quest_desc: [
		"Grout is nessary for constructing both the Melter and Smelter Multiblocks, your most powerful bulk smelter (For Now)."
		""
		"Gather plenty of Sand, Gravel, and Clay in preperation of making your first soild fuel melter."
	]
	quest.0A73874C00D2C311.quest_subtitle: "The Forge Awaits"
	quest.0A73874C00D2C311.title: "The River Provides"
	quest.0A8BB0E2C6DB515A.quest_desc: ["There are two possible \"upgrades\" for the furnace, each pertaining to a certain function. The &6&oBlast Furnace&r is one of these upgrades, pertaining to smelting down ores and metals. With the Blast Furnace, &6&oany raw metals or ores you put in will be processed much quicker than a typical furnace&r, but you will not be able to put any other items in, such as food. For that, you need the other option."]
	quest.0A8BB0E2C6DB515A.title: "What a Blast!"
	quest.0A91740322B9BEC2.quest_desc: ["An enhanced version of the Gem Case, this can store much more."]
	quest.0AB1E6FBCB9E81EC.quest_desc: [
		"The oceans aren't exactly safe, and the last thing you want is to be left defenseless under attack. For this, I'd recommend adding a cannon or two. It's as simple as right clicking your ship with the cannon in hand. With that done and dusted, you simply need to add some cannon balls to your ship's cargo, then fire by pressing the keybind (Default Space) while looking in the cannon's direction."
		"Cannon's aren't light, though, and each one will lower your ship's speed by 2.5%. Fortunately, removal is as simple as hitting it with a pickaxe."
	]
	quest.0AB1E6FBCB9E81EC.title: "Cannons Armed and Ready"
	quest.0AD58CA90772F0B5.quest_desc: ["Due to them not being the brightest, Foliot Miners will mine almost anything found in the mineshaft, bringing back all their contents. Due to the spirit's weaker strength, this is a slow process, and the lamp housing it will also decay slowly."]
	quest.0AD58CA90772F0B5.title: "Foliot Miner"
	quest.0AEBCA228D3D7205.quest_desc: [
		"&o&4Faction controlled villages&r are protected and occupied by one of the three factions. While exploring, you may find a village already with a fragile totem. If not, you can make a base and head yourself."
		"When claimed by a faction, all workstations and beds will be claimed by that faction. Right clicking a village totem not belonging to you will start &oa raid&r wherein the attacking faction will begin spawning and must be fought off by the defending faction. Raids can also occur randomly, or by entering a village with the Bad Omen effect from another faction."
	]
	quest.0AEBCA228D3D7205.title: "Village of Werewolves"
	quest.0B009391E3F76D6E.quest_desc: [
		"The fisher is an excellent source of early game food for your citizens. Hopefully you have a decent resource for string. With any luck the fisherman will also get some some extra loot. "
		""
		"If your colony lacks a natural water source like an ocean or river, you can make do with a 6x6x1 area of water. "
	]
	quest.0B009391E3F76D6E.quest_subtitle: "Build the Fisher's Hut"
	quest.0B2C4ACAE75F106F.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to Tubumbu 42.04.4 LTS"
		"*** System restart required ***"
		"Last login: Fri May 25 1979 from 189.26.60.236"
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat clanging_howl.jv"
		"Project Clanging Howl"
		"-------------------"
		"Following a recent meteor shower, reports of strange sounds led to a throrough search of the report's location. Though most of the search resulted in nothing but pebbles and bits of an unknown metal, one living specimen was captured and taken into custody. Weather reports indicated that a similar event may occur &levery 15 days&r."
		"Subject ch-001 is believed to be the first step into the cosmos, and how we may better understand its workings."
	]
	quest.0B2C4ACAE75F106F.title: "clanging_howl.jv"
	quest.0B8F9662721646F8.quest_desc: ["The Fairy familiar aids other familiars with beneficial effects and can prevent familiar death. It also drains the life force of its owner's enemies."]
	quest.0B8F9662721646F8.title: "Fairy Familiar"
	quest.0BB8DE1AF9032136.quest_desc: [
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"While watc\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"hing the fles\"},{\"text\":\"h spread, did you come acr\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"oss an\"},{\"text\":\"y berries? \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"Bloomberries form near outer walls of flesh\"},{\"text\":\". They c\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"an be p\"},{\"text\":\"icked and then consumed for rando\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"m po\"},{\"text\":\"tion effects. Alternativ\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ely, y\"},{\"text\":\"ou can let a \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"fully grown bloo\"},{\"text\":\"mberry continue growing before it'\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"s lau\"},{\"text\":\"nched into the sky. \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"After tr\"},{\"text\":\"aveling a bit, \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"they'll explode into malignant veins\"},{\"text\":\", continuing t\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"he spre\"},{\"text\":\"ad of the flesh.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/bloomberry.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0BB8DE1AF9032136.title: "The Berry's Blowing Up"
	quest.0C1D96315B727F90.quest_desc: ["Obtained from The Nether Gauntlet"]
	quest.0C74A1D72E10D754.quest_desc: [
		"Possession rituals are rituals where the summoned demon takes control of a particular mob. Their main purpose is usually to obtain rarer or harder to obtain items through killing them."
		"Most advanced rituals you'll make will need purple chalk, requiring end stone, which can be obtained by killing a posessed endermite."
		"Draw Hedryn's Lure and &6&obegin the ritual by placing the book of binding in the golden bowl, then throwing an egg&r."
	]
	quest.0C74A1D72E10D754.title: "The Mite of The End"
	quest.0C901BEB8C3CACDD.quest_desc: ["You will no doubt find many pieces of dark metal dropped by mobs. They can be blasted into dark metal nuggets or packed into piles of dark metal."]
	quest.0C97DDE29130A92D.quest_desc: ["The Lifestealer was once a vampire lord that swore his loyalty to the Lord of Chaos so he might become even more powerful."]
	quest.0C97DDE29130A92D.title: "Steal Back What's Yours"
	quest.0CBA6857AD661F3C.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat chac-10.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"The CHAC-10 Advanced Chainsaw is capable of shredding through wood at extreme speeds compared to those of a traditional axe. Being that it is an advanced machine in nature, &lit lacks a traditional durability&r, and must instead rely on a consistent stream of energy."
	]
	quest.0CBA6857AD661F3C.title: "CHAC-10 \"Advanced Chainsaw\""
	quest.0CBBAA0351FD2EF2.quest_desc: [
		"At level 4, your skill tree opens up. To grow stronger than level 4, you need the altar, a multiblock structure "
		"The required structure depends on the level, you need a specific amount of \"structure points\". The actual value of the structure you build is calculated after the following rules:"
		"The points each pillar piece add depend on the block inside: Stone Brick: 1, Iron Block: 2, Gold Block: 3."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"List each level's requirements here"
		"To Level | Structure Points | Pure Blood | Human Hearts"
	]
	quest.0CC9087813E5F33E.quest_desc: ["Once you've hit max level at 14, you can start to increase your age rank. You can do this by killing mobs with your bite attack. To check your progress on increasing your rank, interact with a coffin. As your age increases, you get more health, less sun damage, less blood drain, the ability to drain blood from attacks, and faster resurrection. However, you will also take more damage from fire, garlic, holy water, and hunters, as well as having harsher prices from villagers."]
	quest.0D3DC90F66E544F7.quest_desc: [
		"Want to avoid the chance of taking damage all together? Or maybe you're wanting to build another stealth archer. Either way, bows are a great method to deal damage from afar."
		"In this pack, they've been upgraded to have &6&ocritical hits&r&r. Whenever you shoot an arrow that's been fully charged, there's a chance you'll deal &6&o50% more damage.&r&r Sneaking while firing an arrow also increases the chance of a critical hit."
		"Guess stealth archers really are strong."
	]
	quest.0D3DC90F66E544F7.quest_subtitle: "Bows and Arrows"
	quest.0D3DC90F66E544F7.title: "I was an adventurer like you once"
	quest.0D56E3C121A776DF.quest_subtitle: "Undertaker Revived a Dead Citizen"
	quest.0D6CFA422E84AD0D.quest_desc: ["By infusing a Dormant Deepshelf, you will obtain a Deepshelf. This can be used to reach Level 70."]
	quest.0D6CFA422E84AD0D.title: "Dormant Potential Unleashed"
	quest.0D6E099A1A242153.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBuild Tool&r is one of the most important tools in the mod. It's how you will place all building from now on. Right+click any solid item to open the build preview GUI. On the right are controls for moving, rotating, raising, and lowering your building. "
		""
		"Place your &bTown Hall&r block and register your colony. However, the first building to be constructed is the builders hut. Your Town Hall cannot be built until you have a completed builders hut."
		""
		""
		"{image:questinstaller:textures/quests/hc_build_tool.png width:190 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0D781DCA4118AF8A.quest_desc: [
		"This thing we made... You know what? I'm just going to leave it to you. Given its nature, &o&6you probably want to use it somewhere with a lot of space&r."
		"Who knows what will happen when it's activated. &oBest be prepared for a fight.&r"
	]
	quest.0D781DCA4118AF8A.title: "Are You Sure This Will Work?"
	quest.0DD280488B9BE843.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ch-002.jv"
		"Indentifier: ch-002 | Informal Name: Extraterrestrial Reaper"
		"-------------------------------------------"
		"Entering the lab, Dr. Carpenter was found slouched against the wall close by ch-001's containment. Further inspection revealed ch-001 had escaped and dug its way into Dr. Carpenter's chest. Fearing the worst, he requested he be contained until further tests could be performed."
		"Not long after his requested containment, Dr. Carpenter began convulsing. A matter of seconds later, he died as subject ch-002 emerged from within him."
		"Extra caution was taken during the following days. Testing revealed &lthe same resistant properties as ch-001&r."
		"The blade on the end of ch-002's arm appears highly sharp, much more so than the average sword. Test subjects attacked with it appeared to have large cuts that did not heal naturally, &las if it had temporarily lowered their maximum health&r."
		"Some are wondering if it may be possible to create something harnessable using the metal from subjects ch-001 and ch-002."
	]
	quest.0DD280488B9BE843.title: "ch-002 \"Extraterrestrial Reaper\""
	quest.0E8687627D0325DF.title: "Kill the bonescaller"
	quest.0EB209B2B41E6921.quest_desc: [
		"The Harbinger is a deadly machine, utilizing the full power of the Nether Star used to power it mixed with ancient technology. To fight one is to fight that which combats destruction incarnate. &6&oFire resistance can prove vital as its barrage of lasers set you ablaze, and the wither effect corrupts you from your very core.&r"
		"The Harbinger does not care for life, and targets whatever is in its vicinity, an important thing to note if fighting in a group. &6&oSwitching between lasers and missiles&r can quickly turn the tides of the battle if not prepared, as can the exploding Wither Howlitzers. The Harbinger's shield, brought up upon &6&otaking 50% damage, blocks projectiles&r, leading to a close quarters fight. It seems as if the creators knew its power, however, as several columns with &6&olever activated EMPs&r have been left for usage."
		"&6&oKeep aware of your surroundings, listen closely for the mechanical hiss of changing weaponry, and use the arena to your advantage, so that you may claim the Mechanical Eye.&r"
	]
	quest.0EB209B2B41E6921.title: "Self Destruct Sequence"
	quest.0EBB4E5195610A82.quest_desc: [
		"The Sawmill is where the Carpenter will craft any items made of at least 75% wood. This is the point where the colony really starts to feel like it’s running on its own. Be sure to set up important recipes for items your builder regularly needs. While the sawmill starts with a paltry 10 recipes, the number of recipes you can teach the Sawmill doubles per building level."
		""
		"Tip: Be sure to give your carpenter a &ebuild tool&r as some recipes require it. "
	]
	quest.0EBB4E5195610A82.quest_subtitle: "Build a Sawmill"
	quest.0EE6E21E6EDBC5B7.quest_desc: ["If you want to make sure you don't get a specific enchantment, you'll want to craft a Seashelf of Aquatic Filtration. This bookshelf does not provide any enchantment stats. &6&oInstead, by inserting enchanted books like with a chisled bookshelf, the enchantments on said books will not appear when enchanting&r."]
	quest.0F047E7D87DD19B9.quest_desc: ["Starting from here, you'll need to make sure you are creating the correct upgrade for your chest. If it's still basic, then a Basic to Iron upgrade is what you need, if it's copper, then you need a Copper to Iron upgrade instead."]
	quest.0F047E7D87DD19B9.quest_subtitle: "Iron Chests"
	quest.0F409DACBEB7BBF8.quest_desc: ["Depending on the pack style you choose, supply ships may need to be placed in water, or in the air. Clear an area large enough to fit your supply ship. This may include digging under water, depending on where you place your ship. The supply ship will not place if there are objects in the way. Right clicking the supply ship on the ground will show a 3D preview of the camp. Using the placement controls arrows, position the ship in your clearing, then click the green checkmark to finalize the placement. If it won’t place, then the terrain is in the way, and you may need to clear the area more. Red lines will appear showing you the areas that need to be cleared."]
	quest.0F649DD652FB7582.quest_desc: ["Nobody quite knows who created the Ancient Factory, only that it remains alive, guarded by dutiful Watchers, Prowlers, and the unfinished form of &o&6The Harbinger&r. Found deep underground, this factory holds many a treasure, but to one searching for &6&oThe Legendary Eyes&r, none is greather than that which is embedded in The Harbinger's metallic body."]
	quest.0F649DD652FB7582.title: "Mechanized Warfare"
	quest.10B025FE594CB756.quest_desc: ["The Divination Wand is used to find common Otherworld materials not visible to the human eye, such as otherstone that appears as andesite to a normal viewer. It's most useful application is finding Iesnium Ore disguised as ordinary Netherrack"]
	quest.10E83B5B468FEF3B.quest_desc: ["A terrible sword could strike her down quick"]
	quest.10E83B5B468FEF3B.title: "Dying Once More"
	quest.1121523438B3BF2B.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ch-001.jv"
		"Indentifier: ch-001 | Informal Name: Heart of Decay"
		"-------------------------------------------"
		"Subject ch-001 was delivered to the station hard frozen in ice until it could be moved to a secure lcoation."
		"Controlled durability tests showed thickened skin &lresistant to even diamond grade tools&r, though scans suggest it could be integrated technology."
		"In addition to its strong defense, one worker was spat at by a strange &lneurotoxin which seemed to slowly eat away at the his health. Active movement seemed to increase only its effect.&r"
	]
	quest.1121523438B3BF2B.title: "ch-001 \"Heart Of Decay\""
	quest.113D270E86B5A284.quest_subtitle: "Copper Chests"
	quest.11A99823249B4587.quest_desc: [
		"The potion effect &o&4\"Sanguinare Vampiris\"&r is what converts you. &oSaid effect comes from the fangs of a vampire, either from being attacked by one, or by using their dropped fangs on yourself.&r &o&4If not cured, the effect's duration reaching 0, will turn you.&r"
		"Being a vampire seems to have some nice advantages. It seems &o&4most undead will ignore you unless attacked&r. You no longer need to breathe underwater, but it weakens you."
	]
	quest.120152510AD4B59A.quest_desc: ["While you might think your builder needs glasses sometimes, these goggles won’t help them. The Builders googles are for you. When you put them on your head or in a curio head slot they allow you to preview your buildings at level 5 which is helpful when fitting one building next to another."]
	quest.120152510AD4B59A.quest_subtitle: "It’s A Samsquanch!"
	quest.124B54C326D8BCBD.quest_desc: [
		"Technically not a familiar, the Demonic Wife and Husband are bound to their partner through a marriage contract."
		"If given a raw food item, they will cook it. If given a potion, they will grant the effect to their partner for a greater period of time. In addition, they will fight alongside their partner."
	]
	quest.124B54C326D8BCBD.title: "Demonic Wife"
	quest.12630716213DB5CE.quest_desc: ["So apparently you can fish in The End? That's new, I'll admit. Though with how &o&3my friend&r is talking about \"Void Liquid,\" I suppose it's not &othat&r crazy to imagine."]
	quest.12630716213DB5CE.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Hook of The Depths"
	quest.12630716213DB5CE.title: "You Can Fish WHERE?!"
	quest.126E583A9A6E0B9F.quest_desc: [
		"An easy way to carry around a large amount of blood without filling your inventory is to craft a &o&4Blood Container&r. It acts like a fluid tank, allowing you to add blood to it by right clicking with a bottle, and doing the same to extract it."
		"In addition, one can drink straight from it if they have a feeding adapter, gained through doing a quest."
	]
	quest.126E583A9A6E0B9F.title: "That's a Lot of Blood"
	quest.128555C5E928F099.title: "Diggy Diggy Hole 1"
	quest.12ABF5CAD1BBD4ED.quest_desc: [
		"Crafted with some wood, copper, and string, the &o&6Angling Table&r is your main method of customizing and upgrading your fishing rod."
		"To the left is the slot to place your rod and to retrieve it once finished. To the right you'll find slots for &o&6fishing line, a bobber, and a hook&r."
	]
	quest.12ABF5CAD1BBD4ED.quest_subtitle: "Craft an Angling Table"
	quest.12ABF5CAD1BBD4ED.title: "Getting into the deep end."
	quest.12D2C0A03089FE7E.quest_desc: ["So you've tracked temperature, you've tracked depth, you've checked the time of day and the moon, even listened daily to the radio for the weather. That must be quite a lot of items to keep track of. Fortunately, they can all be combined into the one size fits all &o&6Fish Tracker&r. Simply holding it, or more conveniently, putting it in the Informational curios slot, you'll be shown all current conditions in the bottom left of the screen."]
	quest.130E8FC7479E4271.quest_desc: [
		"The Shepherd’s Hut is where the Shepherd will breed and butcher sheep for food and wool. You will have to capture and bring in two sheep to the Shepherd’s Hut, as the Shepherd will not catch and bring in any sheep."
		""
		"The Shepherd will only keep two sheep alive per hut level, so at level 5 they will have ten sheep in their holding pens."
	]
	quest.130E8FC7479E4271.quest_subtitle: "Build a Sheperd's Hut"
	quest.134225C47C55A718.quest_desc: ["Climate and temperature can play a big role in a fish's presence. From hot oceans to frozen lakes, it's never bad to have a &o&6Climate Gauge&r on hand. Alternatively, you can put it in the Informational curios slot. Regardless of how you hold it, the temperature becomes clear as day in the bottom left corner of the screen."]
	quest.13CB873C91B6BB8E.quest_desc: ["I get it. The sword you tore from your enemy's hands is nice, but you aren't particularly fond of its descriptive name, and would rather it not be there. That's where a Sigil of Unnaming comes into play. Putting it into an anvil with an Affixed item will removed the prefixes and suffixes of its name."]
	quest.13D002D731503C1F.quest_desc: ["Minons will have 4 attribute: Inventory Size, Health, Strength, Resource Efficiency. When you level up your minion, they gain a skill point that you can spend to increase one of these attributes."]
	quest.13D221AFA2707A46.quest_desc: ["The Cargo Airship works the same as its predecessor, only it requires more fuel to operate."]
	quest.13D221AFA2707A46.title: "Mobile Cargo Shipment"
	quest.13D99A6985631F9C.quest_desc: [
		"Once you've obtained some &o&6Infused Shelves&r, you can craft them into even more powerful variants. There are several, each with different pros and cons, but the simplest ones are the &o&6Glowing Hellshelf&r and &o&6Crystalline Seashelf&r."
		"With these upgraded shelves, you will be able to reach level 60."
	]
	quest.13D99A6985631F9C.title: "And This Is To Go Even Further Beyond"
	quest.141564E14017FEA6.quest_desc: ["The Bat Familiar gives night vision when nearby or in a familiar ring. If upgraded, it can give its owner a lifesteal effect"]
	quest.141564E14017FEA6.title: "Bat Familiar"
	quest.1428DFC072CD4426.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ch-003.jv"
		"Indentifier: ch-003 | Informal Name: Flesh Maiden"
		"-------------------------------------------"
		"When presented with a captured zombie, ch-002 showed an odd shift in behavior. Initially hostile, it showed no malice towards the zombie after its initial attacks. Scans showed an infection in the undead, and soon after, ch-003 emerged from it."
		"Initial durability tests confirmed the same durability as its predecessors."
		"Completely hostile, ch-003 attempted to attack the team members with its arms. When that had no visible result, Dr. Weaver attempted a better look through the glass, only for ch-003 to &lstrike with what resembled a long whip-like tongue&r."
	]
	quest.1428DFC072CD4426.title: "ch-003 \"Flesh Maiden\""
	quest.143F22ADA2229BF4.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.143F22ADA2229BF4.title: "reach lvl 14"
	quest.144A97870616A8AC.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat adv_elc.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"During the cleanup of Site Romulus, extraction team members found various electronics, fragile and of which the notes to recreate seem to have perished with its creators. It's possible &lmore may be found in other sites&r with connection to Romulus"
	]
	quest.144A97870616A8AC.title: "adv_elc.jv"
	quest.1467F080230DFEEE.quest_desc: [
		"{image:modpack:textures/frostmaw.png width:160 height:90 align:center}"
		"Cold? Let me tell you about cold. The Frostmaw is a hulking beast of the snow. You'll likely find him sleeping in your travels, but be wary. Waking one can quickly spell out a forever frozen fate. That said, play your cards right, and you can take down the behemoth, making the Cold Eye it guards all but yours."
		"PS: You might be able to snag the Ice Crystal it holds in its sleep, provided you're confident in your stealth."
		"HARD"
	]
	quest.1467F080230DFEEE.quest_subtitle: "The Yeti"
	quest.149BF56B98224AAF.quest_desc: ["You've truly found your footing now. I, Professor Larch, could not be more proud. With that said, you can only experience so much in one place. Yes, you will no doubt want to explore the world, finding structures big and small. Still, the length of travel may be intimidating, but that is where &o&6Waystones&r will come in handy. An elegant relic for a more civilized age, you will be able to &6&oquickly travel between any waystones you've discovered&r. Still, doing so will cost you, though the cost will lessen the further away you are from your destination. With that said, I may have one to spare, if you'd show that you're the type who would get good use out of it."]
	quest.149BF56B98224AAF.title: "Don't lose your way(stone)"
	quest.14A6246E24E675A9.quest_desc: [
		"&o&6Universal Bosses&r are ordinary mobs that spawn as an Apothic Boss. Unlike normal bosses, Universal Bosses don't have any special equipment, only increased stats and sometimes &6&oEntity Affixes&r."
		"When killed, Universal Bosses can drop gem dust, enchanted books, and on rare occasions, an Affix Scroll. These scrolls can be &6&ocombined with items in an anvil&r to give that item up to two scroll affixes or broken down at a Salvaging Table for rarity materials."
	]
	quest.14A6246E24E675A9.title: "Bosses Risen"
	quest.14B0868E99676875.quest_subtitle: "Four Stack"
	quest.14DA3DC7C0009A6A.quest_subtitle: "Reach 50 Citizens"
	quest.14DC4E0A7614FE76.quest_desc: [
		"While sitting in your ship, let down the sails with the necessary keybind (Default R). From there, you can increase the speed with W and decrease it with S."
		"For some extra personality, you can dye the sails of your ship."
	]
	quest.14DC4E0A7614FE76.title: "Sailing Strong"
	quest.14E521ADAD4C9D6E.quest_desc: [
		"At the top of the reforging hierchy is the &6&oFabled Reforging Table&r. Unlike the tables before it, the Fabled Reforging table is only able to reforge an item to Fabled rarity. In doing so, it also gives the item a &o&4Set Affix&r."
		"Set Affixes add on top of existing affixes and &6&ogrow stronger when multiple items within the same set are used&r."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/fabled.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.14E521ADAD4C9D6E.title: "Tales and Fables"
	quest.15324C27CC683196.quest_desc: [
		"Tell me, have you ever made the choice to insert one gem into an item only for you to later find a different gem, or perhaps just a better version of the one in your item? Well, don't worry."
		""
		"If you're ever in a situation where you'd like to &oremove&r a gem from one of your items, you can craft a &o&6Sigil of Withdrawal&r. &6&oPutting the sigil in a smithing table with your item will remove all the gems in its sockets.&r"
	]
	quest.15324C27CC683196.title: "Gem Removal Service"
	quest.15757B216B5D7237.title: "Waystone 1"
	quest.15ACD993630984F4.quest_desc: [
		"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Welcome, traveler. I do not know your name, but neither do you mine. What matters is that we've met, talked... understood one another.\",\"font\": \"alt\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Welcome, traveler. I do not know your name, but neither do you mine. What matters is that we've met, talked... understood one another.\"}},{\"text\":\"\\n\\n\",\"font\": \"alt\"},{\"text\":\"This world is full of wonders, but also danger. Many gears move in the clockwork of reality, and time is something nobody can escape. So the question is, what will you do with yours?\",\"font\": \"alt\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"This world is full of wonders, but also danger. Many gears move in the clockwork of reality, and time is something nobody can escape. So the question is, what will you do with yours?\"}},{\"text\":\"\\n\\n\",\"font\": \"alt\"},{\"text\":\"Within the contents of this book are a collection of people's notes, their journeys, and for some, their life's work. I'm certain it will prove useful to you.\",\"font\": \"alt\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Within the contents of this book are a collection of people's notes, their journeys, and for some, their life's work. I'm certain it will prove useful to you.\"}},{\"text\":\"\\n\\n\",\"font\": \"alt\"},{\"text\":\"Ah, but be not afraid if you lose this book. Its contents will always be accessible through your inventory.\",\"font\": \"alt\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Ah, but be not afraid if you lose this book. Its contents will always be accessible through your inventory.\"}}]"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/quest-book.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
		""
		"Now, go forth, and carve your tale."
	]
	quest.15ACD993630984F4.quest_subtitle: "Hovering Can Discern The Unreadable"
	quest.15ACD993630984F4.title: "A book?"
	quest.15B51FB56A64C303.quest_desc: [
		"Many new buildings and upgrades are locked behind university research so it is worth getting a university built as soon as possible. Researcher will research various upgrades to your colony, and each level unlocks an additional researcher for a total of 5 researchers. Each Researcher can start their own research, but more Researchers does not lower the amount of time each individual research takes."
		""
		"Note: Research time is real-world time spent in-game. However, after level 3, Researchers will sometimes use offline time to work on researches."
	]
	quest.15B51FB56A64C303.quest_subtitle: "Build a University"
	quest.15D59D975C84E266.quest_desc: [
		"&6&oThe Burning Arena,&r home to the immortal flame, &4Ignis&r. I cannot describe this coliseum with words alone. If you seek its challenge, &6&oprepare yourself for a fight you will never forget&r."
		"Ah, right. An &o&6Eye of Flame&r may be able to help locate this arena."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/burning-arena.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.15D59D975C84E266.title: "A Final Destination"
	quest.15E23B6FFCCBEFD2.quest_desc: [
		"Much like the transporter, a Foliot Janitor is a Foliot bound to a book of calling. Whereas the transporter moved items from one inventory to the next, janitors will pick up any items in their filters and deposit them in a designated container."
		"Shift Right Clicking the spirit will let you change its filter, which by default is set to only allow items added to its list, but that can be changed to the opposite if you desire. Right clicking with the book of calling will let you choose to either set the janitor's work position and radius that it will search, or choose the container for it to deposit items it picks up."
	]
	quest.15E23B6FFCCBEFD2.title: "Cleanup on Isle 13"
	quest.15EC5D720D4001E8.quest_desc: [
		"The eternal guardians of the Nether Fortress, Wither Skeletons are a semi-rare occurance. That's not to say you won't find your fair share of them. Be careful of their attacks, for the wither you away from the inside."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/wither-skeleton.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.15EC5D720D4001E8.title: "Off With Their Heads!"
	quest.15F03A5E7E14C022.quest_desc: ["The stonemason is another key profession in the colony. They craft items commonly required by the builder. The stonemason will craft 3x3 recipes made entirely out of cobblestone, stone, andesite, diorite, granite, quartz, purpur, nether bricks, prismarine, sandstones, blackstone, and basalt. They can also craft end stone from cobblestone and an ender pearl after you complete the research."]
	quest.15F03A5E7E14C022.quest_subtitle: "Build a Stonemason's Hut"
	quest.161435ADC63C307D.quest_desc: ["&6&oOne must venture into the Deep Dark if they are to obtain even greater power&r. Requiring materials only found within the dark, and even from venturing into the Ancient Cities of the past, two of the three upgraded forms of the Deepshelf are &6&oThe Echoing Deepshelf&r and &6&oThe Soul-Touched Deepshelf&r. Each focuses on a specific stat, but both can be used to &6&oreach level 75 enchantments&r."]
	quest.161435ADC63C307D.title: "This Isn't Even Its Final Form"
	quest.166C0CC10669A38E.title: "Hell's Greatest Tourist"
	quest.16F31CF0700E1CC8.quest_desc: ["Hearty Dragon Meal is a universally loved food for all dragons and often has stronger effects than other preferred food. &4&nIt can also be made with almost any fish and eggs.&r"]
	quest.16F672CB45B8DBAC.quest_desc: ["Dragon familiars give extra xp to their owner. If upgraded, they will attack enemies with swords"]
	quest.16F672CB45B8DBAC.title: "Dragon Familiar"
	quest.17171CE78EEE17E1.quest_desc: ["A Terrible Weapon, its cost of blood is often seen as fair for its high critical damage."]
	quest.1722CCBB8755EF0A.quest_desc: [
		"The Djinni Crusher is a stronger spirit than its Foliot counterpart, and can crush any raw ore into 3 of its corresponding dusts."
		"Create Ophyx' Calling and summon one to further your ore processing goals."
	]
	quest.1722CCBB8755EF0A.title: "Djinni to Win"
	quest.17DBF6E831690F59.quest_desc: ["Obtained from The Masquerader"]
	quest.1804F80D5B4FBD50.title: "16x Lapis Lazuli"
	quest.180555739861AF54.quest_desc: ["I have nothing to say to you. I guess it &odoes&r let you fish in lava with any hook."]
	quest.180555739861AF54.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Netherite Fishing Rod"
	quest.180555739861AF54.title: "Reel Dedication"
	quest.1844A99E435F6E8E.quest_desc: [
		"At the very end of your enchanting journey is The Draconic Endshelf. &6&oCrafted using the head of an Ender Dragon, only 1 shelf is required to bridge the gap from Level 90 to Level 100.&r"
		"At last, the pinacle of power is yours."
		"Or is it?"
	]
	quest.1844A99E435F6E8E.title: "The Shelf of Dreams"
	quest.18C4659AC9FEDFED.quest_desc: ["There are tales of an ancient material, older than the world itself. Found deep within the earth under immense pressure, it is known as &4&nWorld Root&r. I have found the material to be real, and very, very hard, requiring at least diamond tier tools to break, and can onl"]
	quest.18DC1665AD8C8EE9.quest_desc: ["You've ventured into the nether and returned with some spectacular materials. I believe it's time we upgrade our Reforging from a simple one to a proper one. While all functions remain the same, you'll now be capable of Reforging all the way up to &o&6Mythic&r tier."]
	quest.18DC1665AD8C8EE9.title: "Upgrading The Upgrader"
	quest.1908E5992649B221.quest_desc: ["Now, throw &o&6some andesite and oak saplings into the fire&r. The flames will alter them, and you will be given &oOtherstone and an Otherworld Sapling&r, though the latter may not look the part."]
	quest.1908E5992649B221.title: "Items From Beyond The Veil"
	quest.1935CFAC6173A06F.quest_desc: [
		"I've no doubt you've noticed your items aren't their normal colors. That, my dear friend, is from the item's &6&oRarity&r"
		"Rarity is important, as it determiens the strength of an item and what kinds of affixes it can have. A good example is that an uncommon and rare item can only have up to 1 gem socket, while higher rarities can have &6&oup to 3&r The rarities are &7Common&r, &2Uncommon&r, &9Rare&r, &5Epic&r, and &6Mythic&r."
		"To increase rarity or craft certain items, you will want to get your hands on some &6&oRarity Materials&r. To do this, you must use Gem Dust to craft a &6&oSalvaging Table&r. Putting an item into the GUI, you will see the amount of Rarity Materials you'll get from salvaging any item. In addition to salvaging items, you can also &o&6salvage gems&r for a much more elegant and efficient method of obtaining it. "
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/salvaging-table.png width:308 height:180 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1935CFAC6173A06F.title: "What is This, A Gatcha Game?"
	quest.193988E4791FC83A.quest_desc: [
		"When you were fighting wither skeletons, did you ever find one's head dropped from it? &o&6Wither Skeleton Skulls&r are a very rare and very important item. The ancient beings would quiver in fear of &4&othe monster that three of them could summon&r."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/wither-skeleton-skull.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.193988E4791FC83A.title: "The Heads of The Dead"
	quest.19CDC61F17EC887C.quest_desc: [
		"The Atroxiia is an ancient cryomancy-adapted lindworm species inhabiting frozen mountain ranges, glacial valleys, and polar frontiers. Rather than overwhelming prey through relentless pursuit, Atroxiia establish dominance by exerting precise control over the terrain itself, reshaping the battlefield through specialized cryomantic abilities channeled primarily through the tail. Their composed temperament, territorial discipline, and unusually regal demeanor have inspired countless legends depicting them as forgotten monarchs or divine guardians of winter, though such accounts remain unverified. Despite their measured behavior, an Atroxiia becomes exceptionally dangerous once provoked, relying on calculated force rather than prolonged aggression. &4&nAny meetings will likely be hostile.&r"
		"Before an Atroxiia can be tamed, &4&nit must first be subdued in combat&r. Wild Atroxiia become vulnerable only after their health is &4&nreduced to approximately 60 HP&r, causing the dragon to enter a stunned state. Once stunned, the dragon may be fed preferred foods such as &n&4raw cod, salmon, beef, porkchops, mutton, chicken, and Hearty Dragon Meal&r."
		"Feeding an Atroxiia does not guarantee successful taming. Failed attempts will restore a portion of the dragon's health, immediately ending its stunned state and forcing the player to subdue it again."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/atroxiia.png width:481 height:113 align:center}"
	]
	quest.19CDC61F17EC887C.quest_subtitle: "Tame an Atroxiia"
	quest.19CDC61F17EC887C.title: "The False Pharaoh"
	quest.19D03831EB5EED02.quest_desc: ["The Blacksmith is a 3x3 crafter and can make any vanilla tools, armor, swords, and shields (no bows or redstone items). You will need to teach the Blacksmith the recipes of the items you want them to create. "]
	quest.19D03831EB5EED02.quest_subtitle: "Build a Blacksmith Hut"
	quest.19DC21F62A5164A3.quest_desc: [
		"As most sockets have tiers, you'll find that eventually, your gems may outstrengthen your gear. But do not be afraid, for there is always a solution."
		"A &o&6Sigil of Elevation&r is crafted with only the best materials, and when placed into a smithing table with your gear, will increase the tier of all present sockets."
	]
	quest.19DC21F62A5164A3.title: "Climbing The Tiered Ladder"
	quest.1A4D57B6CA4E5128.quest_desc: ["Make a butchers knife and kill large animals like pigs and cows to get tallow for special candles"]
	quest.1AA91D7D090A9404.quest_desc: ["Like a regular sheep, these guys "]
	quest.1AAD393EC8CA5294.quest_desc: ["A limited Barrel is made to hold a single type of item, Just- A Damn lot, of that one item, useful for filtering. or all your thousands of cobble."]
	quest.1AAD393EC8CA5294.quest_subtitle: "One Stack"
	quest.1BA8589B69D3D94E.quest_desc: [
		"Once you make a tool, it's parts can be replaced and swapped out. You made a flint pick earlier, try adding the new iron head to it now."
		""
		""
		"Sand Casts are the cheapest way to make casts, place the cast into the Casting Table, and then a stone or wooden part onto the sand cast, then remove the part, this makes a cast of whatever part you used. Permanent Casts can be made by pouring liquid gold onto a part (Hint: Try an Ingot!)"
	]
	quest.1BA8589B69D3D94E.quest_subtitle: "Hot Swapping"
	quest.1BA8589B69D3D94E.title: "Tier 2 Tools"
	quest.1BB571557F74D3A1.quest_desc: ["As you have explored, you may have encountered abandoned colonies. If you like, you can take over an abandoned colony and repair it. This can be a good way to jumpstart your colony. However, if you want the full colony experience, then it’s recommended that you find a good place to settle your colony and start the old fashioned way. Blood, sweat and tears. "]
	quest.1BC30C22E89D0830.quest_desc: ["After reaching max level, you can talk to the werewolf representative and accept a task to become a Werewolf Lord. One of the requirements are werewolf teeth, which only drop from Alpha werewolves in The Werewolf Heaven biome."]
	quest.1BC30C22E89D0830.title: "Become Werewolf Lord"
	quest.1BC55DD4CCAA97C0.quest_desc: [
		"Each enchantment has its own rarity. &6&oArcana is the stat that changes your chances of getting each rarity.&r In addition to this, higher Arcana also increases the amount of enchantments your item will receive, going from only 1 to a max of always getting 3 enchantments."
		"Like other stats, Arcana is primarily increased by using bookshelves, however, &6&ocandles are another way to raise it&r."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/arcana.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1BC55DD4CCAA97C0.title: "Arcana"
	quest.1C15A3A4E31745DE.quest_desc: [
		"With the sacrifice of a parrot, tamed or otherwise, one can summon a Drikwing. Like with the parrot, a drikwing can be summoned either as a familiar or an untamed spirit depending on whether string or an egg is used."
		"Drikwings grant their owner partial flight, allowing multiple high jumps and slow falling."
	]
	quest.1C15A3A4E31745DE.title: "Drikwing Familiar"
	quest.1C16AEE8E29FB5A0.quest_desc: [
		"The rallying banner will summon your Guards to you when used. It’s especially useful in raids, as Guards don’t automatically know where to find the raiders. You must shift + right-click the banner on a Guard tower or Barracks Tower to assigns the Guards in that tower to the rallying banner."
		""
		"Note: Your Guards will not follow you outside the colony border. To bring Guards outside the border, set them to Follow you on the second page of their tower GUI."
	]
	quest.1C4A96F5309C4A07.quest_desc: [
		"That's it, Not a lot to teach."
		""
		""
		"Now get outta my face."
	]
	quest.1C4A96F5309C4A07.quest_subtitle: "Damn, that's Expensive"
	quest.1C7B5C5AA9263D78.quest_desc: ["Once you've become a lord, you can get a minion. &oYou can only have a number of minions equal to your lord level.&r To recruit a minion, find a weak werewolf npc and interact with them holding a Moon Charm. Moon charms are received as rewards for completing the task, &o\"Minion Control.\"&r"]
	quest.1CFAF1433C2BE3AC.quest_desc: [
		"While you grow stronger, you'll come across options with two choosable skills. These skills are &oexclusive&r and you can only choose one."
		"At level 4, your skill tree opens up to 3 paths, these being &oBeast, Survivalist, and Human, focusing on combat, movement, and utilities respectively. While not exclusive, later skills such as forms cost more points, so be sure to think over your choices. &oYou cannot easily reset your perks.&r"
	]
	quest.1CFAF1433C2BE3AC.title: "reach lvl 4"
	quest.1D0A5E343CD7689A.quest_desc: ["These guys are jerks. They'll attack you, villagers, and any other animals that's not a pig. What's more, if you feed it raw porkchops, it'll enter a &ofrenzy&r and will start attacking quite literally anyhting."]
	quest.1D1BDE3EC94B4722.quest_desc: [
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/dead-king.png width:160 height:90 align:center}"
		"The Dead King was once a powerful necromancer. Now his body sits atop his throne, waiting with the eye it guards hidden away. Dark magic can bind this king's soul to a compass, leading you to his catacombs. Take care of yourself and your surroundings, and this lord of the dead will fall before you."
		"PS: Don't think you've won after killing him once. The dead always come back."
	]
	quest.1D1BDE3EC94B4722.quest_subtitle: "The Lord of Death"
	quest.1D75D3EE37934DAE.quest_desc: ["The Chimera Familiar fights its owner's enemies, and when fed meat, grows in size and strength. At its max size, it can be ridden by the player until it shrinks over time, requiring it to be fed once more."]
	quest.1D75D3EE37934DAE.title: "Chimera Familiar"
	quest.1DDD484C05B10A38.quest_desc: ["With a Foliot Crusher, you'll be able to have raw ores and ingots crushed down into dusts, which can then be smelted into ingots. Crushing an ingot will only give an ingot's worth of dust, but raw materials can give double what normally smelting would give you."]
	quest.1DDD484C05B10A38.title: "Let's Get Crushing"
	quest.1E0F68CE39E46A81.quest_desc: ["With the pentacle Eziveus's Spectral Repulsion, some silver, and a bit of gold, your glass lenses can be bound to a foliot, allowing you to then craft otherworld goggles. While these goggles allow one to &osee&r otherworld materials, they are unable to &omine&r the materials. For that, a special pickaxe is required."]
	quest.1E1870FAD295DEDE.quest_desc: [
		"Clear and flatten an area about 20×20 blocks to make space for your camp. The camp cannot be placed if objects block the area. Right-click the supply camp on the ground to see a 3D preview. Use the arrow controls to position the camp within your cleared space, then click the green checkmark to place it. "
		""
		"If placement fails, the terrain is still in the way, remove obstacles until it fits. Red lines will mark spots that need further clearing."
	]
	quest.1E2054693E1C12A1.quest_desc: ["Scattered and Buried throughout the hellscape are parts of the distant past, just waiting to be melted down for your own use. Netherite is useful sure. but what else can be made from the old scrap?"]
	quest.1E2054693E1C12A1.quest_subtitle: "I Wonder Who Left It?"
	quest.1E2054693E1C12A1.title: "Forgotten Treasures"
	quest.1E77333D8A12F3E6.quest_desc: ["For whatever reason, there are some fish that only come out during a certain phase of the moon. You could keep track of this yourself, or you can get yourself a &o&6Lunar Calendar&r to show you. Once hung up on a wall, standing nearby will tell you the moon's current phase."]
	quest.1E85DF6B80F62A89.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ext_stl_nug.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Researchers have begun trialing new ways to use the extraterrestrial steel. In this pursuit, they have carved away at the ingots forged to make more use out of it."
	]
	quest.1E85DF6B80F62A89.title: "ext_stl_nug.jv"
	quest.1F64A9564AC6EC77.quest_desc: [
		"Earlier, you'll recall that I, Professor Larch, talked about a wise man's quote, \"It all started with a tree, then an upgrade.\""
		"Well, by now you've crafted a crafting table, and you've likely crafted a wooden pickaxe. But that's only going to get you so far, so now it is time for that upgrade. Three stones and two sticks will give you a stone pickaxe, capable of mining much more."
		"Indeed, this is the progression of tiers. You'll find many cases of upgrades in forms such as this. Your next upgrade will likely be Iron, but that isn't for certain. After all, the beauty of this world comes from its freedom."
	]
	quest.1F64A9564AC6EC77.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Stone pickaxe"
	quest.1F64A9564AC6EC77.title: "Tree Finished, Now An Upgrade"
	quest.1F92B2332221508F.quest_desc: [
		"I hope you haven't tried sleeping in a bed. That doesn't really work in The Nether. That being said, there &ois&r a way to set your spawnpoint. With some crying obsidian and glowstone, you can craft a &o&6Respawn Anchor&r."
		"It's worth noting that a Respawn Anchor's power is not unlimited. &6&oIt must be given glowstone to gain a charge&r. Up to 4 charges can be stored at once, and one charge is expended upon respawning."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/respawn-anchor.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1F92B2332221508F.title: "Otherworldly Undeath"
	quest.1FED017AF22E96E9.quest_desc: [
		"Placeholder"
		"By having a werewolf attack you and infect you with &oLupus Sanguinem, then sleeping while infected. When you wake up, you will be a werewolf.&r"
		"Werewolves are unique in that they only show their true strength at night and that they are only treated as a werewolf while transformed. In human form, you are treated like you aren't in any faction."
		"As a werewolf, you'll take reduced damage and can pierce armor with your attacks. Different forms gained later on will increase your abilities."
	]
	quest.1FED017AF22E96E9.title: "Lupus"
	quest.200D96871A6421D8.quest_desc: ["This nifty little scroll requires you bind the scroll to a waystone first, but then you can warp back there any time you want. I'd say it's quite useful after a long day's travel."]
	quest.200D96871A6421D8.title: "1x Bound Scroll"
	quest.201741943D9BE0ED.quest_desc: ["Fused bones drop from siamese skeletons"]
	quest.201CB898A399F1D5.quest_desc: [
		"The Swineherd’s Hut is where the Swineherd will breed and butcher pigs for food. You will have to capture and bring in two pigs to the Swineherd’s Hut, as the Swineherd will not catch and bring in any pigs."
		""
		"The Swineherd will only keep two pigs alive per hut level, so at level 5 they will have ten pigs in their holding pens."
	]
	quest.201CB898A399F1D5.quest_subtitle: "Build a Swineherd's Hut"
	quest.2053246F6CA30BC6.quest_desc: [
		"Wow, you've really gotten far, huh? With everything you've done, we can get into Bio-Alchemy, the creation of serums with varrying effects. To start, you'll uh, want to make a &o&6Bio-Lab&r."
		"{\"extra\":[{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"TEST\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
	]
	quest.205582225EA06E0E.quest_desc: ["Carve one to get the evil carved pumpkin"]
	quest.206159A3C7A78447.quest_desc: [
		"The Mystical Site is a simple building that increase a colony's overall happiness level. It has no worker and increases colonists' happiness just by existing."
		""
		"The Mystical Site also gives a bonus to the maximum resurrection chance of the Undertaker."
		""
		"Before you get too excited. No, there is no benefit or bonus from building multiple mystical sites. "
	]
	quest.206159A3C7A78447.quest_subtitle: "Build a Mystical Site"
	quest.209788EC74A463B8.quest_desc: [
		"Manyullyn is one of the strongest metals known to blacksmiths, forged with a mix of Cobalt and Ancient Debris. At one point. It was the stongest metal a mortal could ever hope to forge."
		""
		"Nowadays, though it remains strong, other metals have taken it's place on top. It's up to you to find them..."
	]
	quest.209788EC74A463B8.quest_subtitle: "Deep Purple"
	quest.209788EC74A463B8.title: "Bound Tight"
	quest.20B7F6A62F064817.quest_desc: [
		"Tales talk of a grand fortress built long ago by ancient beings that no longer walk these realms. Made from netherbrick, The Nether Fortress is a towering construction. Finding one may not be easy, but it's best to start looking."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/nether-fortress.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.20B7F6A62F064817.title: "The Fortress of The Damned"
	quest.20BC0B93A0B52388.quest_desc: [
		"Great, Now To make sure you continue to have room to put shit until... I dunno, you have enough cobblestone to create a black hole, Make an upgrade base."
		""
		"It's pretty easy, just use some of those levers I gave ya and combine them with a basic chest in a crafting grid."
	]
	quest.20BC0B93A0B52388.quest_subtitle: "Just a Small Change"
	quest.20BC0B93A0B52388.title: "A Little Bit of Redstone...."
	quest.21026D8552F0AAC5.quest_desc: [
		"Like the name, this barrel can hold two item stacks, unless you can't read. But then you couldn't read this either."
		""
		""
		"Just remember, now that it holds two different items, the amount of those items the barrel can store is now halfed."
	]
	quest.21026D8552F0AAC5.quest_subtitle: "Two Stack"
	quest.2132D9E3E29FB05D.quest_desc: ["To cure yourself of being a werewolf, use a syringe on another werewolf to acquire a &oStrange Injection&r then inject yourself by right clicking an injection chair."]
	quest.2170DDB920E2E543.quest_desc: [
		"Exploring the world, you may notice a gold trim around Spawners. Indeed, these are Multiplayer Spawners, and they have some interesting effects. You will find that breaking it removes the trim, but not the block itself. In doing so, you have &o&6de-activated the spawner&r for yourself. It will no longer activate when you are around, but will still do so for others until they, too, deactivate it for themselves."
		"I, Professor Larch, would also like to tell you that &o&6torches you place near spawners will extinguish after 10 minutes.&r Also, if you'd like to truly break the block for any reason, break it a second time and use the prompt in Chat."
	]
	quest.21AC049A964823A0.quest_desc: [
		"The Tongue is not unlike a mechanical chute. &6&oWhen connected to a container, it will slowly extract all items within it, placing them on the ground as if dropped.&r"
		"Oddly, it does not appear to work with &6&oFleshkin Chests&r."
	]
	quest.21AFB6E4BAD5EC6B.title: "Spiritual Storage Solutions"
	quest.221F955B1421EC0C.quest_desc: ["Ah, that catch your eye? Yes, soul gems may be somewhat plentiful to those practicing the arts, but it takes a... special touch to imbue one as I have. If you want one, I'll gladly sell it to you. Perhaps it can be useful next time you die."]
	quest.221F955B1421EC0C.title: "1x Enchanted Soul Gem"
	quest.222203F2D4CF537C.quest_desc: [
		"It's time to make the Smeltery!"
		""
		"You will need quite a bit of Grout to make a forge large enough to be of use. The Multiblock is created by building a 3x3 base, and building up the walls around it, you do not need corners. You can place the Controller and the Fuel Tank wherever you please within the walls. But I recommend they're easily accssesable. "
		""
		""
		"(Tip: You're going to need Lava to Fuel the Smeltery, It's a good idea to have some sort of generator to keep it running!)"
	]
	quest.222203F2D4CF537C.quest_subtitle: "Apprentice Blacksmith"
	quest.222203F2D4CF537C.title: "The Heart of Copper"
	quest.226176A1C73431B5.quest_desc: ["Assign 5 fields to a single worker."]
	quest.226176A1C73431B5.quest_subtitle: "Get To Work!"
	quest.226E685EBF424C80.title: "Final Chalk"
	quest.2270E70D4E4E6E86.quest_desc: [
		"Exploring the vast ocean is a long an arduous journey. It's for this reason that a proper ship becomes a necessity. Whether it be a Cog for simple traversal, particularly in cold waters, a Brigg for transportation of many items and passengers, a Galley for naval warfare, or a Drakkar for the true Norse experience."
		"All ships have their uses, and all use the sails, let down with the necessary keybind (Default R). From there, speed is increased with W and decreased with S."
		"For some extra personality, you can dye the sails of your ship."
	]
	quest.2270E70D4E4E6E86.title: "To Sail The Seas"
	quest.227108006BB0F89B.quest_desc: ["Vampire clothing is armor that does not hinder your speed or strength while being fully enchantable."]
	quest.227108006BB0F89B.title: "Vampiric Outfitter"
	quest.22D0DB7D7F40A723.title: "Chalk It Up to Spirits"
	quest.22F4C38E79DEFF1E.quest_desc: ["When placing any building, including your supply camp or ship. You will have the option to change your colony style. Click the “Switch Pack” button to open a menu with many styles to choose from. If you want to get an idea of the styles before you build, go to youtube and search \"&eMineColonies Build Styles&r\". Note: This pack includes a number of additional styles not shown in the video."]
	quest.22F4C38E79DEFF1E.quest_subtitle: "TODO: Improve Language"
	quest.23012F6C4C522CEB.quest_desc: ["The Forester is an essential worker in your colony. They will chop down trees and replant a sapling in the tree’s place. Foresters will chop any tree in the immediate area. However, this area can be restricted using a &ezoning tool&r available in the hut block. "]
	quest.23012F6C4C522CEB.quest_subtitle: "Build the Forester's Hut"
	quest.236A8CD55E52C733.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ful-blz_cyl.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Chemists and Technicians were able to convert Blaze Fuel into a more malleable and transportable source of thermal energy. The casing requires plating coated in Netherrack to contain such energy."
	]
	quest.236A8CD55E52C733.title: "ful-blz_cyl.jv"
	quest.2396C57A6CDEC65A.quest_desc: [
		"They say the Nightmare Stalker is one of the most dangerous spirits to invade the Overworld, but I've seen it, the transformation all those years ago."
		"If you become its target, be alert, for you will see nothing of its presence through your vision alone, save for its two glowing eyes."
		""
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/nightmare-stalker.png width:114 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.23F1B575238D5D9F.quest_desc: [
		"\"So, we've got a vial and a lab, what next?\" I hear you ask. Well, this is where we begin to use the lab."
		"When you use the bio-lab, you'll be met with the following screen. Like all other machines, the bio-lab requires &onutrients&r, found through the bar on the left. The top four slots are your &o&6ingredients&r and the center is your &o&6base&r. Much like regular potions, you use a base item when creating compounds and serums."
		"&o&6The Organic Compound&r serves as your basis for all future alchemy. Every single serum starts off as this. Try making some."
	]
	quest.2426440F227E7101.title: "Dragon Slayer"
	quest.2444BC79553C5720.title: "Path of nether"
	quest.2458D0D81AE5F2B1.quest_desc: ["Made with the power of the &oMidas Fish&r, this rod can catch golden items alongside fish."]
	quest.24A3D813751D0FBD.quest_desc: [
		"&6&oAugments&r are a tier above gems that are inserted into &oCrest Slots&r. Using an Augment can grant various general bonuses, such as &6&ostrengthening the power of gems or affixes&r in a piece of gear."
		"Sigils of Ascension are an infused version of Sigils of Socketing, used to convert an &oUntiered Gem Socket&r to an &6&oAugment Socket&r."
	]
	quest.24A3D813751D0FBD.title: "Ascended Augmentation"
	quest.24D211740DD41A5D.quest_desc: ["An ancient civilization that still thrives, Deeplings inhabit what can only be called the Sunken City. A gargantuan structure found in Deep Oceans and completely submerged in water, it houses the brother of Scylla, &o&6The Leviathan&r. If you wish to lay claim to The Legendary Eyes, this will be one of your key destinations. Best not make it your last."]
	quest.24D211740DD41A5D.title: "The Abyss Calls Back"
	quest.25117DDCB87D0502.quest_desc: [
		"Dragons have two special stats besides health: Hunger and Happiness. With the &4&nDraconic Codex&r, you can see all your tamed dragons and their needs. In addition, you can view their health, armor value, gender, and location."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/draconic-codex.png width:180 height:100 align:center}"
		"Hunger decreases slowly over time, but drains much faster when riding your dragon, about 4 times as quickly. At 60 hunger and below, they will progressively become weaker until their hunger is less than 30."
		"To increase hunger, feed your dragon their preferred foods or Hearty Dragon Meals. You can view their preferred foods by clicking the green tab on the side of the codex screen."
	]
	quest.25117DDCB87D0502.title: "Dragon Care 101"
	quest.253503BACB844886.quest_desc: ["Umbrellas negate the sun's effect on you in exchange for lowering your speed. They can be equipped in either hand or a designated curios slot."]
	quest.2538D770008B1CD4.title: "Diggy Diggy Hole 3"
	quest.257AD50176950053.quest_desc: ["A crafting table is an excellent and vital block for sure, but you can only do so much with a 3x3 grid. Many times, you'll find you need something heated. That's where &o&6The Furnace&r comes into play. You'll want to have mined a ring of stone to craft it, and an entire world of possibilities will open for you. Will you cook? Smelt? Perhaps do more? I, Professor Larch, am excited to find out, even if this is a book I've pre-written for you."]
	quest.257AD50176950053.title: "Smeltery? Not Quite"
	quest.25927B5C8F23FCEA.quest_desc: [
		"Not all mobs are made equal. For some, power has been grasped in some way. These are &o&6Bosses&r. Stronger variants of mobs wielding special equipment unique to them."
		"Most often, you'll come across these variants when one &o&6invades your world&r, shown through a sound playing alongside text notifying you and a beacon of light illuminating them from afar. "
		"You may also come across &o&6Mini Bosses&r while exploring, rare wandering mobs who have tapped into the power of Affixes."
		"Finally, they speak of &6&odungeons&r hidden under the dirt and rock of the world, treasure and knowledge stored away, guarded by a Boss."
		"When slain, a Boss will always drop &6&oits unique Affixed item&r. These are typically stronger than most other affixed items you'll come across. And as a memento of the one who held it before you, the boss's name with be added to the item."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/bosses.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.25927B5C8F23FCEA.title: "Promotion"
	quest.25B20970F2E51E30.quest_desc: [
		"Howdy! You can call be the Quartermaster! I am fluent in all things storage- well maybe not all things, there are some wizard's an' shit that can do the same... but if it's made out of wood, it's my specialty!"
		""
		""
		"First, Just make a chest to toss yer shit."
	]
	quest.25B20970F2E51E30.quest_subtitle: "Standard Chest"
	quest.25B20970F2E51E30.title: "It's a Box!"
	quest.25D54E863A28A0AF.quest_desc: [
		"The Ignivorus is a colossal fire-adapted dragon species known for its overwhelming physical presence and extreme thermal output. Native primarily to the Nether, Ignivoruses are capable of drastically altering their surroundings through prolonged exposure alone, often rendering occupied regions permanently hostile to other lifeforms. The Ignivorus relies on sustained pressure, environmental dominance, and absolute escalation once engaged in combat. Its immense resilience and refusal to retreat have made it one of the most feared apex predators documented. &4&nAny meetings will likely be hostile.&r"
		"Before an Ignivorus can be tamed, &4&nit must first be subdued in combat&r. Wild Ignivoruses become vulnerable only after their health is &4&nreduced to approximately 100 HP&r, causing the dragon to enter a stunned state. Once stunned, the dragon may be fed preferred foods such as &n&4raw cod, salmon, beef, and Hearty Dragon Meal&r."
		"Feeding an Ignivorus does not guarantee successful taming. Failed attempts will restore a portion of the dragon's health, immediately ending its stunned state and forcing the player to subdue it again."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/ignivorus.png width:300 height:199 align:center}"
	]
	quest.25D54E863A28A0AF.quest_subtitle: "Tame an Ignivorus"
	quest.25D54E863A28A0AF.title: "Scorched Earth"
	quest.25E290F19A2CCAF7.quest_desc: [
		"Deep underground lie the &6&oCatacombs&r, burial sites of an ancient necromancer and his army. A wayward compass may show you the way to one of these locations, and exploration will reward you with treasures of arcane power. It also remains home of &6&oThe Dead King, holder of The Undead Eye&r."
		"A powerful necromancer indeed, The Dead King will cast a variety of deadly spells, &o&6from slashes of blood to to poison arrows, and even raising the dead to fight under it&r. And do not fool yourself into thinking it is weak in close quarters, for it still holds its staff, a powerful bludgeoning tool."
		"&6&oBe quick on your feet, bring plenty of potions, and The Undead Eye may be yours to claim.&r"
	]
	quest.25E290F19A2CCAF7.title: "Stay Dead"
	quest.26391C42E91CA9F7.quest_desc: [
		"You have reached Tier 3 tools, equivalant, and often surpassing, Diamond. Congrats! This is the maximum teir you can acheive without defeating the Gatekeeper to the Nether, and making a portal."
		""
		"Go forth my Apprentice! You are well on your way to becoming a Master Smith!"
	]
	quest.26391C42E91CA9F7.quest_subtitle: "Good Student!"
	quest.26391C42E91CA9F7.title: "Tier 3 Tools"
	quest.265ADD6A31E72A87.quest_desc: ["At level 4, you become a proper vampire, and your skill tree opens up"]
	quest.265ADD6A31E72A87.title: "No longer a child"
	quest.2767F0ACA0E05A29.quest_desc: ["This little scroll of mine's simple but powerful. It'll instantly teleport you to the closest known waystone available. Pretty useful for a quick escape, no?"]
	quest.2767F0ACA0E05A29.title: "1x Return Scroll"
	quest.27BE86C707B9A681.quest_desc: [
		"The &o&6Heart-Forged Seashelf&r is an upgraded Seashelf that &6&ooffers higher stats in exchange for lowering your Rectification&r."
		"This can be rectified by using the Shelf of Seabound Rectification."
	]
	quest.28458B14A9335A52.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.28458B14A9335A52.title: "Obtain a Cave Tablet"
	quest.28751771BB33158E.quest_desc: ["When first turned, you will be rather weak. At this stage, sunlight will not yet hurt you, and you'll gain a blood bar. The primary way to fill the bar is by drinking blood from mobs, holding the keybind (Default V) while looking at a mob. The symbol over the crosshair can show how much blood a mob has. Exhausting this supply can be fatal to the one drank from. If your blood bar is full, having a blood bottle in your hotbar will fill it when drinking"]
	quest.28751771BB33158E.title: "Blood Soaked Fangs"
	quest.289249EDEB1AF17E.quest_desc: ["&6&oThe Hellshelf of Masterful Sight&r is an upgraded form of the Hellshelf of Sight &6&othat increases the visible clues by 2 instead of 1&r."]
	quest.2909AA079114656F.quest_desc: ["The quickest and most powerful miner spirit, a Marid Miner is not only able to mine common and uncommon ores, but even the rarest ores like Iesnium and Ancient Debris are obtainable through this spirit's work."]
	quest.2909AA079114656F.title: "Marid Miner"
	quest.29213AC500A39A04.quest_desc: ["The Devil Familiar grants its master fire resistance while attacking hostile mobs."]
	quest.29213AC500A39A04.title: "Devil Familiar"
	quest.29A7297004BECA7E.quest_subtitle: "Shiny Chest"
	quest.29EF96BD531FE5F0.quest_desc: ["Need the weather cleared? Then look no further than The Occult. With the catalyst of crops, a Djinni is summoned to clear the skies."]
	quest.29EF96BD531FE5F0.title: "Clear Skies Ahead"
	quest.2A0422E6DF854E64.quest_desc: [
		"&o&6The Void Blossom&r is another rather unique enemy, being more plant than monster or man. It's said to be quite the rare site, only ever found underground near the bedrock of the world. There does, however, exist means to locate this wonderful specimen, and it all starts with &o&6a Lily of The Valley and an Amethyst Shard&r."
		"When fighting this void-powered plant, it will fight back with crystalized thorns penetrating the ground beneath you, as well as puffs of poison exploding in the air."
		"&6&oBe swift, be aware, and The Crystal Eye will be in your hands.&r"
	]
	quest.2A0422E6DF854E64.title: "A Crystal Bloom"
	quest.2A6F2C6150FE049A.quest_desc: [
		"Interacting with minions shows their inventory menu and accessory slots. From there you can order them to follow you, defend you, Defend the area, Stay, or Collect resources. Alternatively, you can edit their appearance and lock them from accepting global commands, which you can do by accessing the command menu (default R)"
		""
		"Minions start out weak, but can grow stronger with the usage of more enhanced moon charms. The tasks required to obtain these charms become available as you level up in your lord status."
	]
	quest.2A90B8D5B22C1CED.quest_desc: [
		"Organic Compost is a special block that can be left to decompose over time, resulting in Rich Soil. There are a few factors that can speed up this process."
		"Factors that accelerate the decomposition are nearby water sources, being exposed to bright light, and being surrounded by certain blocks like mushrooms, Podzol, Mycelium, existing Rich Soil, or more Organic Compost."
	]
	quest.2AC31E694EFB6EB3.quest_desc: [
		"In exploring the Ancient Cities of the old world, I've discovered scripts describing the creation of an ancient forge I have dubbed The Draconic Crucible. I've recreated it with &4&nAncient Dragonite Fragments found in the same Ancient Cities&r."
		"Being a forge, it requires a heavy amount of heat to operate. Blaze Powder has been an easily obtainable source of this, but I believe something could be &4&ncreated with Cindervane scales and coal&r."
		""
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/draconic-crucible.png width:520 height:369 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2AEACBC0748148A7.quest_desc: [
		"You've made your totem, now you must fill it. Fortunately, doing so is a simple matter. Merely killing mobs while a totem is either in your hotbar or equipped as a curio will fill the totem with that mob's energy. Different types of mobs have differing amounts of soul energy, with undead being one of the weakest, most likely due to their nature."
		"The Totem of Roots can hold a max of &o&6100 souls&r. Before continuing, I suggest you fill it, as we will be needing that energy very soon."
	]
	quest.2AEACBC0748148A7.title: "Extracurricular: On Gathering Souls"
	quest.2B0FCAC7E8CFFC40.title: "Waystone 2"
	quest.2B10426B62B49B13.quest_desc: [
		"Small Ships adds 4 different boats to the game for various purposes, but above all, transportation. To get started, you'll want three boats of the appropriate wood type. Some boats require chests as well."
		"Your ships will be able to hold some cargo, but putting too much in it could reduce its overall speed by up to 10%. To access the cargo from outside the ship, use it while crouching."
		"I don't want to overwhelm you, so I'll finish with telling you that a damaged hull can be repaired with wooden planks and iron nuggets."
	]
	quest.2B10426B62B49B13.title: "Small But Strong"
	quest.2B15416FD329E64F.title: "time 2"
	quest.2B4A600190F438AF.quest_subtitle: "Kill Sir Pumpkin heafd"
	quest.2B712988FC2E66C0.quest_desc: [
		"Now, I'm sure in your travels you've come across some items with rather unique properties. Found in chests or dropped by mobs, these special properties are known as &6&oAffixes&r."
		"Affixes come in various categories, each with many possible effects. &o&6Stat Affixes&r change attributes such as speed or health; &6&oDurability Affixes&r decrease the damage taken by an item, often through negating it; &o&6Effect Affixes&r give a wide range of unique abilities such as applying a potion effect when striking an enemy or making the attack AOE; and both &o&6Gem Sockets and Augment Sockets&r give you slots to put gems and augments into, but more on that later."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/affixes.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2B712988FC2E66C0.title: "Affix To This"
	quest.2BED66945BBA3836.quest_desc: [
		"There are two other components we will want to acquire. One of those is an &6&oempty focus&r. For now, the simplest method of obtaining one would be to use your totem and some amethyst. Once you have that, then we can begin."
		"[ \"Oh, and if you're struggling to find amethyst, \", { \"text\": \"I believe my cousin may be able to help\", \"underlined\": \"true\", \"color\": \"light_purple\", \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"24D05EE5346105AD\" } }, \".\" ]"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/empty-focus.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2BED66945BBA3836.title: "Your First Focus"
	quest.2C744F74C1147FF4.quest_desc: [
		"You've been given a few already, but let me tell you about Fishy Notes."
		"They're quite simple, really. Along with a silhouette of then fish in question, a note will tell you its rarity and any requirements needed to catch it."
	]
	quest.2C744F74C1147FF4.title: "Notes Torn By Waves"
	quest.2C9358C87170FB16.quest_desc: ["Finding, killing, making armor, making incubator, hatching egg"]
	quest.2CBE90561300741D.quest_desc: [
		"You tried entering the nether, huh? Sounds like you need a tablet?"
		"Hmm... I've got an idea. Perhaps you could try making some sort of pseudo portal. Like, an unstable one. Maybe then we'd be able to find that tablet."
		"An unstable portal. If I had to guess, it'd probably need &o&6some blocks from the portal frame, something that holds a lot of lost souls inside it, and some kind of igniter. Flint and steel probably isn't good to use for this.&r"
	]
	quest.2CBE90561300741D.title: "Well... That Didn't Work"
	quest.2CC64FEFCD8C3A22.quest_subtitle: "Diamond Chests"
	quest.2CF72976CE0FE008.quest_desc: [
		"Do you ever find yourself scouring the town to find that one specific villager you want to trade with? I, Professor Larch, know I do. And to that, I say, \"No more!\""
		"The &o&6Trading Post&r is a block that connects to all nearby villagers, allowing you to access any trade from it. What's best is that you can even filter and search for more specific desires."
	]
	quest.2CF72976CE0FE008.title: "Trading Central"
	quest.2D0037293AA421E0.quest_desc: ["Found as rewards and as loot, they are bound to you once equipped, only being removable by destroying the item. They take damage when you die"]
	quest.2D0037293AA421E0.title: "Acessories"
	quest.2D65D038AF3F9654.quest_desc: [
		"Tinker's Contruct allows you to create tools out of (Almost) Any Material! YOU have complete control over your tools! This Questline will guide you from basic tinkering to a Master Smith!"
		""
		""
		"Sit down, and let this old dwarf teach you how it's done."
	]
	quest.2D65D038AF3F9654.quest_subtitle: "A Blacksmith is Born"
	quest.2D65D038AF3F9654.title: "Patterns Matter"
	quest.2D6EB90AB01FC332.quest_desc: ["Those that traverse the icy mazes are said to lose their very minds as they are lost in its depths. It only makes sense that they would write down journal logs, kept safe in their &o&6shelters and cabins.&r"]
	quest.2D6EB90AB01FC332.title: "Finally, I have them all."
	quest.2D846DFCA9F7CE9B.quest_desc: [
		"The Gem Case is a container useful for storing all types of gems. In its UI, you can insert gems through the blue slot. Retrieving stored gems is as simple as clicking the gem you use to take out."
		"Gem Dust and Rarity Materials can be stored in the slots on the left of the UI. With them, you can easily upgrade a gem using the copies stored in the case."
	]
	quest.2D846DFCA9F7CE9B.title: "A Case for your Jewelry, Dear?"
	quest.2D8E30F73790F5C8.quest_desc: ["If you want to be sure your ship is safe and not going anywhere, I'd suggest a lead. Just like with animals, your ship can be tied to a fence post."]
	quest.2D8E30F73790F5C8.title: "Docking Station"
	quest.2DDC9022F2D0B78E.quest_desc: ["There are two possible \"upgrades\" for the furnace, each pertaining to a certain function. The &6&oSmoker&r is one of these upgrades, pertaining to cooking various meat and vegetables. With a Smoker, &6&oany raw foods you put in will be processed much quicker than a typical furnace&r, but you will not be able to put any other items in, such as stone or ores. For that, you need the other option."]
	quest.2DDC9022F2D0B78E.quest_subtitle: "I don't name my own lessons, okay?"
	quest.2DDC9022F2D0B78E.title: "Smoking Sexy Style"
	quest.2E156E0FF61C3646.quest_desc: ["Ichor is the Nether's own Earthslime counterpart. Found in large geodes scattered between the lava seas"]
	quest.2E156E0FF61C3646.quest_subtitle: "Tangy!"
	quest.2E17178A86A774BE.quest_desc: ["The fiery hook warms up the temperature of the water, making it good for when you're not in the warmest of areas."]
	quest.2E17178A86A774BE.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Firey Hook"
	quest.2E17178A86A774BE.title: "Nice and Warm"
	quest.2E272904A33ACAD5.quest_desc: ["Obtained from Maledictus"]
	quest.2E33FB46525688BA.title: "Candy Chaos"
	quest.2E39C6C7A1BE0560.quest_desc: [
		"Obtained from The Harbinger"
		"The Wither was a primal force of pure darkness and destruction. Why they would ever think to build another one is beyond me. It seems as tho we won't find an answer, however."
	]
	quest.2E39C6C7A1BE0560.quest_subtitle: "The Mech"
	quest.2EAEB8C2A9C94594.quest_desc: [
		"{image:modpack:textures/vizier.png width:160 height:90 align:center}"
		"Despite my love for the dark arts, I cannot say I am... pleased with the vizier. Though anybody wanting to learn more of the forbidden will inevitably come face to face with him. To call one as powerul &mand arrogant&r as him, one must make use of a scroll crafted with the illagers' prized totem. After that, it's only a matter of finding a dark manor, and &4you can tear his soul apart.&r"
		"Uh, excuse me, I got a bit sidetracked."
		"PS: Crowd control is your ally."
	]
	quest.2EAEB8C2A9C94594.quest_subtitle: "The Evoker's Chief"
	quest.2F2C58A19EE524BD.quest_desc: [
		"30 levels is all that's achievable using regular bookshelves. If you want to go further, &o&6you'll need to start crafting more special bookshelves&r."
		"&6&oHellshelves&r and &o&6Seashelves&r are special bookshelves made with materials from The Nether and The Ocean respectively. Hellshelves will give extra &oQuanta&r while Seashelves will instead give &oArcana&r."
		"&6&oUsing these bookshelves, you can reach enchantment level 45.&r"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/hellshelf_and_seashelf.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2F7A45A76EED6B35.quest_subtitle: "Get the Fel Lamp from Lord Pumpkinhead"
	quest.2FD5037D4E720043.title: "All The Utility"
	quest.2FF4A63F425B31BD.quest_desc: ["Straw can be obtained by using a knife while harvesting grassy crops such as wheat or rice."]
	quest.2FF4A63F425B31BD.title: "Rough and Course"
	quest.300DBCF9A7A1466F.quest_desc: [
		"Using blood infused iron, you can craft two weapons, the heartseeker and heartstriker. These require charging via a blood pedestal, as well as training, which is simply done by killing mobs."
		"The swords becomes faster the more trained you are with them"
		"The blood pedestal is used to charge vampire swords. It must be placed on top of a blood container to work."
	]
	quest.300DBCF9A7A1466F.title: "Beginner Weaponry: Vampire"
	quest.306086EE9B34A8CC.quest_desc: [
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Uh, hey, have you notic\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ed any \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"Malignant Flesh Ve\"},{\"italic\":true,\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"ins\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\" ap\"},{\"text\":\"pearing wh\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"en you pe\"},{\"text\":\"rform a sacrifice? They'r\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"e hard to m\"},{\"text\":\"iss. If you do, well... \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"you might want to get rid of them bef\"},{\"text\":\"ore they spread.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"B-but they aren't nece\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ssari\"},{\"text\":\"ly a \"},{\"italic\":true,\"text\":\"bad\"},{\"text\":\" thing. If y\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ou w\"},{\"text\":\"ait, let them \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"spread\"},{\"text\":\", you'll s\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ee all s\"},{\"text\":\"orts of new blocks. Fleshy ones. They make \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"for a gr\"},{\"text\":\"eat source of raw material.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I uh, think \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"rotten flesh\"},{\"text\":\" upsets the cradle. Uh, causes it to nearly always grow more veins.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/malignant-veins.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.306086EE9B34A8CC.title: "The Primal Spread"
	quest.3064519CF5EDABDD.quest_desc: [
		"A Foliot Transporter is a Foliot bound to a book of calling with the purpose of taking items from one inventory, such as a chest, and putting them in another inventory, such as that of a crusher spirit."
		"Shift Right Clicking the spirit will let you change its filter, which by default is set to only allow items added to its list, but that can be changed to the opposite if you desire. To set its inventories, right click the Book of Calling obtained by the ritual, then make sure you have either Set Extract or Set Deposit selected. After that, shift right click the container or mob you want the spirit to take from or give to. It should be known that for blocks like furnaces, it's important you right click the correct face. For example, right clicking the back of a furnace will have the transporter deposit items into the fuel slot of a furnace."
	]
	quest.3064519CF5EDABDD.title: "Transporting The Goods"
	quest.309BB2C3143443F6.quest_desc: [
		"[\"\",{\"text\":\"You want to get stronger, don't you? In that case, \",\"font\":\"alt\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"You want to get stronger, don't you? In that case, look to the Skill Tree tab in your inventory, or press the assigned keybind (Default K).\"}},{\"font\":\"alt\",\"text\":\"look to the Skill Tree tab in your inventory\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"You want to get stronger, don't you? In that case, look to the Skill Tree tab in your inventory, or press the assigned keybind (Default K).\"}},{\"text\":\", or press the assigned keybind (Default K).\",\"font\":\"alt\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"You want to get stronger, don't you? In that case, look to the Skill Tree tab in your inventory, or press the assigned keybind (Default K).\"}}]"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/skill-tree-tab.png width:150 height:90 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Within the Skill Tree, you will find a variety of abilities, or \\\"Skills\\\" if you'd like. When you level up, you'll gain \",\"font\":\"alt\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Within the Skill Tree, you will find a variety of abilities, or \\\"Skills\\\" if you'd like. When you level up, you'll gain Skill Points, which you can then spend on these Skills. Experience varies, but for the primary Skill Tree, it can be obtained through combat, enchanting, fishing, and mining.\"}},{\"text\":\"Skill Points\",\"font\":\"alt\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Within the Skill Tree, you will find a variety of abilities, or \\\"Skills\\\" if you'd like. When you level up, you'll gain Skill Points, which you can then spend on these Skills. Experience varies, but for the primary Skill Tree, it can be obtained through combat, enchanting, fishing, and mining.\"}},{\"text\":\", which you can then spend on these Skills. Experience varies, but for the primary Skill Tree, \",\"font\":\"alt\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Within the Skill Tree, you will find a variety of abilities, or \\\"Skills\\\" if you'd like. When you level up, you'll gain Skill Points, which you can then spend on these Skills. Experience varies, but for the primary Skill Tree, it can be obtained through combat, enchanting, fishing, and mining.\"}},{\"text\":\"it can be obtained through combat, enchanting, fishing, and mining\",\"font\":\"alt\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Within the Skill Tree, you will find a variety of abilities, or \\\"Skills\\\" if you'd like. When you level up, you'll gain Skill Points, which you can then spend on these Skills. Experience varies, but for the primary Skill Tree, it can be obtained through combat, enchanting, fishing, and mining.\"}},{\"text\":\".\",\"font\":\"alt\",\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Within the Skill Tree, you will find a variety of abilities, or \\\"Skills\\\" if you'd like. When you level up, you'll gain Skill Points, which you can then spend on these Skills. Experience varies, but for the primary Skill Tree, it can be obtained through combat, enchanting, fishing, and mining.\"}}]"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/skill-tree.png width:225 height:135 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.309BB2C3143443F6.title: "Skills and Thrills"
	quest.30ABD0E686F62848.quest_desc: [
		"I hear you. Even with a nice bag and some chests, the items just keep piling up. At some point, you need to get rid of them, so have you considered &o&6selling your goods?&r If you have, then I, Professor Larch, recommend investing in a &o&6shipping bin&r."
		"Opening the bin, you'll find its inventory is much like a chest. &6&oSimply put in what you wish to sell, and when the clock strikes midnight, you will be notified of your earnings, which you can pick up next time you open it.&r"
		"Note that &onot all items are sellable&r, and some items like common ingredients may require more than one to receive any profit."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/shipping-bin.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.30ABD0E686F62848.title: "Ship It Off!"
	quest.312B3C60B1D25B21.quest_desc: ["Minons will have 4 attribute: Inventory Size, Health, Strength, Resource Efficiency. When you level up your minion, they gain a skill point that you can spend to increase one of these attributes."]
	quest.319328B8B24413DB.quest_desc: ["If one wants to easily obtain a large amount of Otherstone, summoning an Otherstone Trader is essential. They will take one of any kind of stone and exchange it for 2 Otherstone, a very good deal."]
	quest.319328B8B24413DB.title: "Otherwordly Stones For Sale"
	quest.31B44D0B5AFCF8C4.quest_desc: ["Found deep in Dark Forests, a Woodland Mansion is home to many Illagers"]
	quest.31C99151EAD7A26F.quest_desc: [
		"If you've defeated a boss, you may notice the creation of a &o&6Boss Rift&r. These special rifts in space are activated by interacting with them, where they will gather energy before &6&oteleporting all nearby entities to the home of the player who interacted with it.&r"
		"I, Professor Larch, find it to be very useful when capping off a long trip with a rather large fight."
	]
	quest.31C99151EAD7A26F.title: "A Rift In Time and Space"
	quest.31E3A26AA76120EB.quest_desc: ["The heart of an Ignivorus burns hot even in death. To a dragon hunter, there is no greater trophy."]
	quest.31E5A46546ECB533.title: "Forged In Soulfire"
	quest.31F7CCE1B74248B2.quest_desc: ["Skyslime is the type of slime found upon the island's floating far above even the tallest mountains, known for it's pale blue color, unlike Earthslime, it's properties are more condusive to mixing into metal."]
	quest.31F7CCE1B74248B2.quest_subtitle: "Blue Slime"
	quest.322A153075BE46A9.quest_desc: [
		"Your handmade tools do not shatter in your hands when they break like normal tools, They simply become worn down and unusable. But! They can be repaired!"
		""
		""
		"In a Tinker's Station, combining the tool with the correct repair material (Whatever the head is made from) will repair it. You can also repair an item on the go with a repair kit."
	]
	quest.322A153075BE46A9.quest_subtitle: "But still Unbreakable!"
	quest.322A153075BE46A9.title: "Not Quite Mending"
	quest.325CB4FC73144494.quest_desc: ["Cobwebs can be placed in an Anvil with an enchanted item to remove its enchantments. Prismatic Cobwebs are crafted with prismarine shards, and do the same for curses."]
	quest.327017618D00C9D9.quest_desc: [
		"Hovering over your fishing rod, you'll notice &o&6 a slot in its tooltip&r, perhaps more depending on the rod. These are used to store &6&ovarious bait&r to aid you in your fishing journey, as they generally have effects that modify your stats outside of the fishing minigame."
		"Basic bait can be made with some compost and rotten flesh. It will increase the speed of your fishing similar to the &oLure&r enchantment."
	]
	quest.327017618D00C9D9.quest_subtitle: "Craft Bait"
	quest.327017618D00C9D9.title: "A Little Birdy Told Me"
	quest.33058894ACD9CB06.quest_desc: ["The Graveyard is where the Undertaker will bury your deceased citizens. When a citizen dies, a grave will spawn at the location of death. The Undertaker will attempt to recover the grave before it despawns. If successful, the Undertaker will return to the graveyard and attempt to revive the citizen. If the citizen cannot be revived, the Undertaker will bury them in the Graveyard. Another grave will be placed with the citizen’s name on it."]
	quest.33058894ACD9CB06.quest_subtitle: "Build a Graveyard"
	quest.331F467C59076F55.quest_desc: ["Mossbacks are a species of small amphibian dragons known for being generally weak and slow, serving mostly as annoyances to those travelling through the jungles they call home. While not being especially adept at fighting (or anything, for that matter), Mossbacks face little true hardship and their numbers are limited only by their laziness, as their natural toxic defense allows them freedom from any natural predators. Mossbacks possess a bladder-like organ in their throats that produce immense amounts of a somewhat weak poison, causing them to always be partially inflated and to leak noxious gasses when under any amount of physical pressure. &4&nThey are not only passive when met in the wild, but able to be picked up and thrown as a projectile.&r"]
	quest.3382A9EBAE939697.quest_desc: [
		"Fishing. It truly is something special, isn't it? Well, here you'll find there's much to do and much to find."
		"But all fishermen need one item. What is it? Why, a fishing rod of course! So, why don't you craft one, and we can get this aquatic show on the road? &6&oThe next slides will describe the base mechanics.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"When you go to cast your rod, you will be met with a meter. &6&oWhen casting your rod, you must hold down right click. The longer you hold it, the farther you will cast your rod.&r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Once you've caught a fish, you will be met with a &onew minigame&r. &o&6You must right click when the sliding bar is closest to the middle.&r"
		""
		"Your performance in this minigame will affect the chance of catching the fish, with &6&ochances increasing as you hit closer to the middle&r."
	]
	quest.3382A9EBAE939697.quest_subtitle: "Craft a basic fishing rod"
	quest.3382A9EBAE939697.title: "Getting Fishy"
	quest.341343B9369306A6.quest_desc: ["Dropped by Captain cornealia"]
	quest.341343B9369306A6.title: "A Captain's Helm"
	quest.342A1EF584823D2C.quest_desc: ["Okay this achievement is kind of a lie. It might be more analogous to “teach a man to fish”.  Regardless, the point is that if you teach your builder to make simple items that fit in a 2x2 crafting grid (like torches) they can craft the item themselves instead of asking for help."]
	quest.342A1EF584823D2C.title: "Never Craft Again"
	quest.349C149AE25E469C.quest_desc: ["Perhaps the most straightforward rituals, Summoning Rituals, well, summon a spirit from the Otherworld to do your bidding. For your first ritual, you summoned a Foliot Crusher, but there are plenty more such spirits can do."]
	quest.349C149AE25E469C.title: "Summoning"
	quest.34D66284E2A560FD.quest_desc: [
		"Fixed-Wing aircrafts such as the Biplane cannot hover and must build up lift through forward motion. When flying one of these aircrafts, &o&6The Space Bar will increase throttle&r, the power of your engine. &o&6Shift does the opposite, lowering throttle. To angle yourself upwards, hold S, and to angle yourself downwards, hold W. A and D will turn your vehicle left or right respectively.&r"
		"These aircrafts require a long strip of flat land to build up enough throttle to take off. You can see the throttle above your hotbar."
		"&6&oIn addition to this, you can load fireworks and use them to boost yourself, much like an elytra, using the designated keybind (Default B).&r"
	]
	quest.359B2C55DB0B7050.quest_desc: ["Our enchanting can reach even greater heights, but doing so will require a new type of shelf. Using deepslate, one can create a &o&6Dormant Deepshelf&r. This shelf on its own is nothing special. &6&oIt must be infused first.&r"]
	quest.359B2C55DB0B7050.title: "A New Challenger Has Appeared"
	quest.35C75C417084A27E.quest_desc: ["To become a Hunter, you must find garlic in the world, either from villages or in the wild. Combine is with a syringe to craft a Garlic Injection, then right click an injection chair, which can also be found in villages or crafted. You will become immune to Vampire's \"Sanguinare Vampiris\" bite."]
	quest.35F1010EA8C338CE.quest_desc: [
		"Ichor, Earthslime, Knowing these two, Then I would harbor a guess that there's a type of slime in the end. Bad Part? Iv'e personally never been, just heard stories, so where it can be found? You'll have to figure that out yourself."
		""
		""
		"Knowing the End? It might behave more like Skyslime."
	]
	quest.35F1010EA8C338CE.quest_subtitle: "End Slime"
	quest.35FF8397225F4952.quest_desc: [
		"When reforging is no longer enough, the energy of a &oNether Star&r allows for the creation of the &o&6Augmentation Table&r. Through this, you'll be able to take your item's existing affixes and reroll or upgrade certain ones for the cost of &6&oSigils of Enhancement&r."
		"When using the table, you will be shown a UI with two slots on the left: one for your item and one for your Sigils of Enhancement. Clicking the drop down menu in the middle will let you select a specific Affix, which you can then either upgrade or re-roll. When upgrading, the new stat will be shown on the left, and when re-rolling a list of possible outcomes will be shown on the left instead."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/augmentation-table.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.35FF8397225F4952.title: "Augmentation's Peak"
	quest.3607F8E9C8F3C7FF.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat cry-nrg.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"At the site of a large meteor, researchers were able to extract crystals that seemed to glow with energy. Large samples have been taken, and more continue to as more meteors are found."
	]
	quest.3607F8E9C8F3C7FF.title: "cry-nrg.jv"
	quest.360A8263D9C40DF2.quest_subtitle: "Hey there's a lot and some of them obscure; BITE ME"
	quest.360A8263D9C40DF2.title: "You Got (Most of them-)"
	quest.360E9E02A494217C.quest_subtitle: "Build Barracks Tower Inside the Barracks"
	quest.3695D8779498D171.quest_subtitle: "Hard and Squishy?"
	quest.36A6DDDCE75E7925.quest_desc: [
		"[With the addition of FTB Chunks, you have the ability to &o&6claim land&r. Accessing the menu through your inventory will bring you to a small map of the immediate area. Using the left mouse button will let you claim chunks, and the right will unclaim them.]"
		"[Claimed chunks have a number of advantages, with one of the biggest being the inability for mobs to grief them. Perfect for a house you don't want broken down.]"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/claim1.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/claim2.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.36A6DDDCE75E7925.title: "Home is where the claim is"
	quest.36BF42D396F66FE3.quest_desc: ["Acropolis floats high above the open sea, its citizens evolved to live without the water, yet still forever attached to it. At its pinnacle sits &6&oScylla, The Storm Empress&r. In your search for power and the Legendary Eyes, you will need to conquer this floating city."]
	quest.36BF42D396F66FE3.title: "A Sanctuary Of Storms"
	quest.36C4FFB47FCE8671.title: "Make a Neollager"
	quest.36F0F40F5D746782.quest_desc: ["Tales speak of warriors who turned their pain into strength, but not many speak of those who do so out of revenge. Turning their lost health into something more, something truly damaging."]
	quest.36F0F40F5D746782.title: "Revenge Served Frozen"
	quest.36F7B644F6DCB1BA.quest_desc: [
		"The dummy is a great way to test new weapons and abilities in a safe controlled manner. Once placed down, it will not be destroyed by your attacks, and will even display your damage dealt along with DPS."
		"If you do find yourself wanting to move, simply crouch and hit the dummy to break it."
	]
	quest.36F7B644F6DCB1BA.title: "Can we get much higher?"
	quest.37043064988891A4.quest_desc: [
		"&o&6Spice of Life: Ringo Pie Edition&r is a mod that incentivizes eating a variety of different foods, encouraging the player to cook up meals more than a simple steak or loaf of bread."
		"While not required, eating a diverse amount of food and &6&okeeping one's diversity level high will grant the player a variety of useful buffs, from extra health to more speed&r."
		"Your active diversity level and eaten foods can be viewed through the food book."
	]
	quest.37043064988891A4.title: "Travel Meals Don't Need to Be Simple"
	quest.370F8CDB9335BC67.title: "Darkened Steel"
	quest.3742CEF52C525920.quest_desc: ["The Scythe of Nightmares has a powerful lifesteal and wither effect strengthened by wearing a full set of Nightmare Armor"]
	quest.3776262630099D76.quest_desc: ["Found as rewards and as loot, they are bound to you once equipped and take damage when you die"]
	quest.3776262630099D76.title: "Acessories"
	quest.377A0D66D50B77FC.quest_desc: [
		"&oTomes&r are a special type of book that's limited in what it can be enchanted with based on the specific type, &osave for the scraping tomes&r&o."
		"&6&oFor example, a Tome of Helmets can only be enchanted with helmet enchantments.&r The same with weapons and weapon enchantments."
		"The Tome of The Others can be enchanted with any enchantments that don't fit in other lists."
	]
	quest.377A0D66D50B77FC.title: "One Tome At a Time"
	quest.37A7B469D081A654.quest_desc: [
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"You got th\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"e st\"},{\"text\":\"uff? Great job, you'r\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"e a n\"},{\"text\":\"atural.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Alright, no\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"w y\"},{\"text\":\"ou should be ab\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"le to \"},{\"italic\":true,\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"t\"},{\"italic\":true,\"text\":\"ake some cla\"},{\"italic\":true,\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ws a\"},{\"italic\":true,\"text\":\"nd meat\"},{\"text\":\", and com\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"bin\"},{\"text\":\"e them to make a \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"Primordial Cradle\"},{\"text\":\".\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/primordial-cradle.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I fe\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"el like \"},{\"text\":\"I'\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"m fo\"},{\"text\":\"rgetting some\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"thi\"},{\"text\":\"ng... Ri\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ght!\"},{\"text\":\" \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"The Primord\"},{\"italic\":true,\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"ial C\"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"ore\"},{\"text\":\"! You'll need one of tho\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"se fo\"},{\"text\":\"r th\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"e cr\"},{\"text\":\"adle.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/primordial-core.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.37A7B469D081A654.title: "Primordial"
	quest.37BE190EE466D697.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade the Town Hall to Level 5"
	quest.37C14B09CE0D87C5.quest_desc: ["They say the depths have a way of changing life, making it... evolve. Some say this is what happened to the &o&6Angler Fish&r of the Ice Maze. Larger, sharper, more hostile, they are no longer like their more passive sisters on the outside. The venom of their fangs are said to make for some truly &6&oterrible&r equipment."]
	quest.37C14B09CE0D87C5.title: "Evolution's Toll"
	quest.37E43341FA234E84.quest_desc: [
		"The Flower Shop is where your Florist will grow flowers for your colony, if given compost and an axe. "
		""
		"One important factor to know is that the flower shop has a daily flower limit based on the hut level. Level 1 has a daily max of 4, level 2 has 8. At level 5 it’s daily max is 20. "
	]
	quest.37E43341FA234E84.quest_subtitle: "Build a Flower Shop"
	quest.37EFF85CF52A3935.title: "8x Gold Ingots"
	quest.38452E4AC25370A3.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat bat-lrg.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"A larger battery, capable of charging advanced tools for much longer than its predecessor. Like its predecessor, however, &lits charge is limited&r."
	]
	quest.38452E4AC25370A3.title: "bat-lrg.jv"
	quest.384F40B2B8912122.quest_desc: [
		"The Missionary is said to be a spirit created by the Lord of Chaos himself and scattered throughout the overworld. I'm afraid their seal won't last forever, and they'll find a way to return once again."
		"The Missionary is a powerful foe with strong control over the undead. Though primarily support, that does not stop it from attacking you itself."
	]
	quest.384F40B2B8912122.title: "A Collector of Sorts"
	quest.385C574E48EB6DE7.quest_desc: [
		"Placeholder"
		"By having a werewolf attack you and infect you with &oLupus Sanguinem, then sleeping while infected. When you wake up, you will be a werewolf.&r"
		"Werewolves are unique in that they only show their true strength at night and that they are only treated as a werewolf while transformed. In human form, you are treated like you aren't in any faction."
		"As a werewolf, you'll take reduced damage and can pierce armor with your attacks. Different forms gained later on will increase your abilities."
	]
	quest.3873AB1F19921EF0.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you've obtained an empty focus, perhaps multiple, it is time to combine it with your earlier magic fabric, some wooden planks, and 2 pieces of Lapis Lazuli. In doing this, you will craft your main tool, the &o&6Dark Wand&r."
		"This will server as your primary method of casting magic. In the future, you may wish to upgrade it, but that is out of the scope for these first lessons. Once fitted with a &ofocus&r, you need but hold the wand in your hands and right click, as if using any other tools or weapons."
	]
	quest.3873AB1F19921EF0.title: "A Wand Chosen By The Wizard"
	quest.38A80A30CD4BD3F4.quest_desc: ["An &oAncient&r rod, you can see what fish is currently hooked when using it."]
	quest.38AF1FEE0E819D16.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ext_stl_wpn.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Researchers and forges worked to put together a sword using the unknown metal, ch-101, informally referred to as Extraterrestrial Steel. The sword's irradiating effect was contained, only truly affected those it damaged. A hammer was also forged, and proved to be rather powerful."
		"In addition to its raw strength and irradiating effects, the weapons &lbypassed the natural armor of technoflesh organisms&r."
	]
	quest.38AF1FEE0E819D16.title: "ext_stl_wpn.jv"
	quest.38E49C8AA7FD4DA3.quest_desc: ["Swords and axes too slow for you? Daggers and Knives provide excellent fast damage. While on their own they may not seem too impressive, their true power comes to light when dual wielded."]
	quest.38E49C8AA7FD4DA3.quest_subtitle: "Stabby stab"
	quest.38E49C8AA7FD4DA3.title: "Say hello to my little friends"
	quest.39129615A6470D5C.quest_desc: [
		"The lunchbag is useful, but perhaps you want to store more meals and snacks inside it, and the 5 slot limit just isn't enough."
		"Well, fortunately for you, &o&6the lunchbag can be upgraded to a satchel, giving it 4 additional slots&r."
	]
	quest.39129615A6470D5C.title: "A Food Carrying Fiend"
	quest.39594A99C94BFE80.title: "Carry-On Focuses"
	quest.396D173C835EC97C.quest_desc: ["The Maw Hopper acts mostly like its traditional counterpart, but with some key differences. The first is that, unlike a regular hopper, &6&othe maw hopper will transport up to 16 of a single item at a time&r. The other difference is that, unlike a regular hopper, the maw hopper can be connected to elongate it and move in different directions, much like a pipe."]
	quest.397D7A84533F7361.quest_desc: ["The Warship is a massive vehicle that is undettered by winds but consumes fuel rapidly. To combat this, it has three fuel slots. Up to 4 people can ride it, with one having access to the gunner slot to use available weapons."]
	quest.397D7A84533F7361.title: "To War"
	quest.39807177697E390F.title: "Go Get Your—Nevermind"
	quest.39F18BD5E09298CE.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ext_stl.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"A rather large sample of the unknown metal was brought in to be investigated. Research showed more similarities to our own steel ore, however its structure does not appear to resemble an alloy of any kind known to us. We expect more samples in the future as more meteor showers occur."
	]
	quest.39F18BD5E09298CE.title: "ext_stl.jv"
	quest.3A1BCAC06FC8322E.quest_desc: [
		"Obtained from the Ferrous Wroughtnaut"
		"NORMAL"
	]
	quest.3A26F553422DC48B.quest_desc: ["By right clicking a fully grown crop, you can instantly replant it. No more needing to break the entire thing and put it all back. Harvesting with a hoe will also bulk harvest in a 3x3 area, making it much more convenient for large farms."]
	quest.3A26F553422DC48B.title: "It's a Grower, Not a Shower"
	quest.3A6E403F44FFE7AA.quest_desc: [
		"Vestige"
		"You've done well to make it this far. My hope in your actions grows ever more with each block you break, each item you craft, each entity you interact with."
		"Things will only get harder from here. Time is something nobody can avoid, and the clock is forever ticking."
		"For now, celebrate as you venture forwards evermore."
	]
	quest.3A6E403F44FFE7AA.title: "Onwards"
	quest.3AAB0E864C590306.quest_desc: ["Frostmaws do not take up a traditional den or cave. Instead, they are found often in large and open snowy biomes."]
	quest.3AAB0E864C590306.title: "Frosted Furs"
	quest.3ACC16304CD0C121.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat jet_bot.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Created as part of the Techointegration Project, Jet Boots are unique in that they do not consume energy, instead relying on Blaze Fuel Cylinders to fuel its abilities."
		"When worn, the boots give a passive reduction to fall damage. Their active ability is a second, rocket powered jump. After performing such an action, the boots must cool down."
		"If out of fuel, the boots will refill automatically from any Blaze Fuel Cylinders the wearer posseses."
	]
	quest.3ACC16304CD0C121.title: "jet_bot.jv"
	quest.3AE1C3290500638F.quest_subtitle: "Reach 10 Citizens"
	quest.3B40A769EDB26EA2.quest_desc: [
		"Got your eye on a new recruit and need some hay bales? If you place a postbox outside your tavern you can request items from the warehouse and a courier will deliver them to the postbox."
		""
		"Similarly, if you have items you want taken to the warehouse, place them in a Stash and a courier will be along shortly to pick them up."
	]
	quest.3B40A769EDB26EA2.title: "Postbox and Stash"
	quest.3B7DF82593D5E9F1.quest_desc: [
		"I'm sure you've filled your pockets with all sorts of blocks and knick knacks. Well, do not fear, for I, Professor Larch, will teach you about &6&obundles&r."
		"Bundles are fantastic little pouches that can hold up to a stack's worth of items. &6&oTo store an item hover the bundle over it and left click, or do the opposite and click the bundle with an item. To retrieve an item, hover over the bundle and scroll to the item you wish to take, then right click.&r"
		"It should be known, however, that bundles have their limits. &6&oItems with stack sizes of less than 64 will take up more space in a bundle, such as a potion taking 4 of bundle's 64 slots due to its stack size of 16.&r A bundle can only carry one of any item that does not stack."
		"Bundles are very useful, and you can carry up to two on your person via the curios slots."
	]
	quest.3B7DF82593D5E9F1.title: "Extra Pockets"
	quest.3B8BF726CC11FBFB.title: "8x Copper Ingots"
	quest.3B91163DE3DA885C.quest_desc: [
		"Possibly one of the most dangerous jobs, especially early on. The Nether Miner travels to the Nether to mine resources. When the miner travels through the portal, there is a chance they may die. So choose your worker carefully."
		""
		"The portal in the Nether Mine will transport players to the Nether. However, the Nether Miner does not actually travel into the Nether, nor do they actually mine any blocks in the Nether."
	]
	quest.3B91163DE3DA885C.quest_subtitle: "Build a Nether Mine"
	quest.3BEEBD80625364E4.quest_desc: ["With so much to do, even I, Professor Larch, struggle at times to keep track of things. Fortunately for people like us, there is the mighty &6&oClipboard&r. Using it is a simple matter and rather intuitive."]
	quest.3CCA251B73C9B4C6.quest_desc: [
		"{image:modpack:textures/void-blossom.png width:160 height:90 align:center}"
		"The Void Blossom is an interesting thing. It's less monster and more plant. Reminds me of the old Tremorzilla films, but we're getting off topic. This flower is said to be found at the bottom of the world in lush caves and jagged crystals. They say a special flower made from amethyst can lead you to these caverns."
		"PS: I say you keep your distance. Thorns aren't pretty up close."
		""
		"&lDifficulty: &2Medium&r&r"
	]
	quest.3CCA251B73C9B4C6.quest_subtitle: "The Crystal Flower"
	quest.3CDD48DCA161A352.quest_desc: [
		"The tower of &6The Night Lich&r is a large and forboding. While one may discover it naturally along their travels, an easier way of locating one would be to use Soul Stars, dropped from killing undead mobs. Do be aware, however, that &6&oyou need 4 soul stars&r to place in each Chiseled Stone Alter, summoning the boss."
		"The Night Lich itself is a powerful sorcerer, attacking from afar with magic while levitating high off the ground, you would best be ready to match its projectiles with your own. Phantoms called upon by the lich will be brutal obstacles in your battle, but do not worry too much, for they are merely phantoms."
		"&6&oBe ready for a long ranged fight, take care of your surroundings, and the Night Lich will die once more. &r"
	]
	quest.3CDD48DCA161A352.title: "Cold as Death"
	quest.3D0C52219AD8860E.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat nrg_bar_gen.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Created as part of the Technointegration Project, The Energy Barrier Generator uses the same technology as the Barrier of Extraterrestrial Activity, compacted down into a wearable alternative. While it &lreduces incoming damage by 50%&r, doing so depletes a large amount of stored energy, with the consumption scaled to the damage reduced."
	]
	quest.3D0C52219AD8860E.title: "nrg_bar_gen.jv"
	quest.3D13CC5391A7277B.quest_desc: ["They say the piglins have developed a special type of shield. Though the secrets to crafting such an item are lost to us, that doesn't stop one from acquiring it through... &oother means.&r"]
	quest.3D13CC5391A7277B.title: "A golden shield?"
	quest.3D23AD9F4C0A2BE3.quest_desc: [
		"Just what is &o&6the Maw&r if not a trap of sharp teeth and malformed fins. The sightings of these creatures, and the findings of those slain, many find only their fins and bones to be of use, although some say they've heard &6&oechoes of those killed in the icey depths&r. Some sightings claim to see items within the mouths of the Maws, as if to lure in adventurers to a sharp and cold end."
		"It seems like The Maw is &6&onot the only source of these&r, however, and they may make for some useful crafting material."
	]
	quest.3D23AD9F4C0A2BE3.title: "Into The Beast's Maw"
	quest.3DFFC6565E661655.quest_desc: [
		"At this stage in the game, you've probably gathered a stash of items, yes? Well, rather than constantly breaking everything down, why not try transfering more notable affixes to newer or better gear?"
		"The Sigil of Transmutation takes &6&oall affixes, gems, and sockets&r from one source item and transfers them to another base item when all three items are set inside a smithing table. &4&lBe warned, the source item will be destroyed in the process.&r"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/sigil-of-transmutation.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3DFFC6565E661655.title: "Old Becomes New"
	quest.3E5ABF732BC0002B.quest_desc: [
		"The Nulljaw is a passive End-adapted dragon species known for its slow drifting behavior and unusually quiet temperament. Unlike many dragon species, Nulljaws spend the majority of their existence suspended high above the End's landscape, traveling in loose airborne groups across void-touched regions. Due to their calm nature and persistent aerial drifting, sightings of Nulljaw groups are often associated with silence, low visibility conditions, and unusually still atmospheric environments within the End. &4&nIt is always passive.&r"
		"Nulljaw can be tamed by &n&4feeding it Chorus Fruit&r, which can be found in the End Barrens. Simply hold it out to lure Nulljaws close for taming."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/nulljaw.png width:300 height:89 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3E5ABF732BC0002B.quest_subtitle: "Tame a Nulljaw"
	quest.3E5ABF732BC0002B.title: "The Gap Between Stars"
	quest.3E70BA3755614508.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat flmr-16.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Utilizing the best in Blaze Fuel and Heat Protectant Metal, the FLMR-160 Flamethrower is capable of releasing high energy bursts of flames capable of burning even the most heat resistant creatures. Its extremely high temperature leaves those affected with immense burns, making them more susceptible to future fire based damage."
	]
	quest.3E70BA3755614508.title: "FLMR-16 \"Flamethrower\""
	quest.3E90E0D630633F39.title: "Stormy Summons"
	quest.3EDF20DB417E51C2.title: "1x Minor Potion of Healing"
	quest.3EED08264DB9E447.title: "Find the werewolf heaven"
	quest.3F2169DF8F96D8A3.quest_desc: [
		"Unlike many other aircrafts, The Gyrodyne is powered by the player's own body. When first taking off, you will be prompted to hold W to build up power. Once power has reached 100%, you  can control the aircraft like any other rotary vehicle."
		"Being that it is muscle based, flying will gradually drain your own hunger, so keep an eye out."
	]
	quest.3F2169DF8F96D8A3.title: "Push the pedal to the floor"
	quest.3F23F48FE24ECE5C.quest_desc: ["When roaming the frozen tundra, and especially high in the mountains, Powder Snow can be a deadly trap. Without specialized gear or leather boots, one will find themselves sinking in its cold grip, and quickly feel their temperature drop. It's best to get out fast unless you wish to freeze to death."]
	quest.3F23F48FE24ECE5C.title: "Watch Your Steps In The Snow"
	quest.3F3F6F3926110E42.quest_desc: ["While not decreasing speed as much as the copper line, The Golden Fishing Line also increses luck when fishing."]
	quest.3F3F6F3926110E42.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Golden Fishing Line"
	quest.3F3F6F3926110E42.title: "Gonna be gonna be Golden"
	quest.3F77375A5E0F0FFA.quest_desc: ["I do not know how this is obtained, but you got it. Maybe you can let me know in the mod comments."]
	quest.3F77375A5E0F0FFA.quest_subtitle: "IDK"
	quest.3FC61B65DA8C7080.quest_desc: [
		"Hey, you did it. Yo&ku ma&rde &6&oa proper serum&r. Serums aren't&k as st&rable as potions, not bein&kg held toge&rther through traditional magic. &o&6As a result, you won't be able to drink a serum or throw it at someone&r."
		"Instead, you&k'll want t&ro craft a &o&6Bio-Injector&r. Think of it like a &obig&r needle. &o&6To open its inventory, press the main-hand action key (Default: V)&r. After that, you can&k s&relect the seru&km yo&ru want to load into it. From the&kre&r, it's as &ksi&rmple as right click&king a&r mob to inje&kct the se&rrum into it, or hol&kding&r shift and right c&klickin&rg to inject the serum into yourself."
		"{image:modpack:textures/bio-injector.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3FC913EFE89A720B.quest_desc: ["An &oAncient&r rod, you can see what fish is currently hooked when using it."]
	quest.3FD815F712CCA0ED.quest_desc: [
		"If you would rather upgrade yer chests without spilling yer shit all over the floor, you'll need to make these upgrades, which allow you to right click a chest with it in your hand to upgrade it to the next tier. (You'll need TWO for double chests!)"
		""
		"This one specificly, is to turn basic Vanilla chests into Sophisticated Storage Chests."
	]
	quest.3FD815F712CCA0ED.quest_subtitle: "No Mess!"
	quest.3FE36789CB4C89C0.quest_desc: ["&6&oThe Ferrous Wroughtnaut&r offers a unique challenge. Located underground in buried chambers, it dons impenetrable armor not even the strongest blade can pierce. Or perhaps not, for there remains a single blade, a crack in its armor, from a past fight. &o&6Wait for it to reveal its weak point and then strike, and you may claim the Armored Eye&r."]
	quest.3FE36789CB4C89C0.title: "Knight Burried in Earth"
	quest.3FF41B2811BC191C.title: "Adept Nether Ritual"
	quest.405C9061EDF15427.quest_desc: [
		"The penultimate enchanting power, &6&oinfusing Dragon's Breath is no simple task, requiring very specific amounts of Eterna, Quanta, and Arcana, along with access to Level 80 enchantment power&r."
		"By using Infused Dragon's Breath, one can craft &6The Endshelf&r. With this shelf, along with its upgraded form, &6&oThe Pearlescent Endshelf&r, &6&oone can reach Level 90 enchanting&r."
	]
	quest.405C9061EDF15427.title: "The Eternal Shelving"
	quest.407C7E8C9ED8229E.quest_desc: ["Fallen Chaos Knights are revenants of servants of chaos, serving their masters until their dying breath. They are a force to be reckoned with, but killing one is rewarding, giving you the smithing template for Dark Metal Armor"]
	quest.40E25305BFD59E52.title: "Dawnbreak"
	quest.40E6822922724098.quest_desc: [
		"Power is seeked by all, and many find ways to achieve it. Typically, multiple gems can create a concotion of unique effects when inset together, but for some, a simpler approach is preferred."
		"If you are such a person, then your future lies with the &6&oSigil of Prismatic Conversion&r. When put in a smithing table with &6an item that has no gems inset inside it&r, all present sockets will combine into one &6&oCatalyst Socket&r. This single socket will be stronger depending on the number of Gem Sockets used to create it, and will apply that strength to whatever gem is inset in it."
		"[catalyst-socket]"
	]
	quest.40E6822922724098.title: "The Catalyst of Power"
	quest.4124EA310604F4D0.quest_desc: ["Now this is where we get interesting. This scroll will let you teleport to &oany&r known waystone, almost like you're using one yourself. It'll even negate the experience cost for you. One use though, so make it count."]
	quest.4124EA310604F4D0.title: "Warp Scroll"
	quest.415E54E23D13D76F.quest_desc: ["The ultimate form of the Rectification bookshelf is the Shelf of End-Touched Rectification. The Rectification is even further increased."]
	quest.41D0937E584D2393.quest_desc: ["The Tome of Extraction is the ultimate form of a Tome of Scrapping, and the upgraded form of the Tome of Superior Scrapping. &6&oWhen used, it transfers all enchantments of an item, but does not destroy the original item.&r"]
	quest.41D0937E584D2393.title: "Extraction Team"
	quest.41D1F6B3F2D922FE.quest_subtitle: "Brew all elixirs"
	quest.41D1F6B3F2D922FE.title: "The Mad Alchemist"
	quest.41E213E02CC541E2.quest_desc: ["Created from tossing a diamond into Spirit Fire, Spirit Attuned Gems are used in a variety of recipes, the most notable being Spirit Attuned Crystals. Like candles and skulls, these are used in the creation of certain pentacles used during rituals,"]
	quest.41E213E02CC541E2.title: "Bring In The Crystals"
	quest.4208293A3F93DF21.quest_desc: [
		"There are some substances that require a hotter temperature to melt down then lava can provide. In these instances, your sights must turn to the living constructs of fire that reside within the nether, Their blood does nicely."
		""
		""
		"Slaying Blazes with a Cleaver has a chance for them to drop their heads, which can be melted down into Blazing Blood. (There are probably better ways to get it however...)"
	]
	quest.4208293A3F93DF21.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Blood"
	quest.4208293A3F93DF21.title: "Better then Lava"
	quest.42C0216DD176D468.quest_desc: [
		"Moops are curious fish with simple minds and complex evolutionary abilities, known to be found in rivers. Being about the size of Salmon, Moop are easily identifiable by their tan colours and yellow stripes. The most well-known trait of the Moop to ecologists and Dragon Researchers is the unique blend of proteins and bacteria in their bodies that halts the growth of Dragons that eat them. "
		"When a Raw Moop is fed to a baby dragon, it will cause them to permanently cease growing. This is a useful tool for keeping your dragons cute and space-efficient. "
	]
	quest.42EA735FD945A117.quest_subtitle: "Make a Focus Bag"
	quest.42EA735FD945A117.title: "Bag For Your Troubles"
	quest.430475E11D259B74.quest_desc: [
		"The Stone Smeltery is where the Stone Smelter will smelt cobblestone into stone, stone bricks into cracked stone bricks, clay balls into bricks, clay blocks into terracotta, terracotta into glazed terracotta, all types of stone into all types of smooth stone, and logs into charcoal. They can also pop chorus fruits! "
		""
		"Be sure to teach the Stone Smelter recipes needed by your colony. Also, be sure to set a fuel type. "
	]
	quest.430475E11D259B74.quest_subtitle: "Build a Stone Smelter"
	quest.4363881A9797B749.quest_desc: ["Nightmare armor is strong armor that when worn as a full set will give certain bonuses to specific weapons. They hardest component to obtain is the Nightmare stalker's skull"]
	quest.4363881A9797B749.title: "The Costume of Terror"
	quest.43AE403E62C96F66.quest_desc: [
		"If you plan to get anywhere with this kind of power, you will require plenty of &6&oGem Dust&r. As the name implies, this dust is sourced by &6&ocrushing the gems&r found scattered around the world. The best, albeit least efficient, way to do this is with&6 the natural force of a falling anvil&r."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/gem-dust.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.43AE403E62C96F66.title: "Ashes to Ashes, Dust to Dust"
	quest.43D8B9DE51674200.quest_desc: ["It's hard to say who these ancient relics once belonged to, be it pirates or settlers, monsters or men. What's certainly the truth, however, is that these wrecks have valuable loot inside, including a &6&oBuried Treasure Map&r. This map will lead you to riches beyond your imagination, the most notable being the treasured &6&oHeart of The Sea&r, a rare item used as a crafting ingredient for numerous special items."]
	quest.43D8B9DE51674200.title: "A Remnant of The Sea"
	quest.43DB027C382D0466.quest_desc: ["The Economy Plane has better fuel consumption than its alternatives, but in doing so, sacrifices speed and all slots other than simple upgrades."]
	quest.43F02218C2BBA0ED.quest_desc: ["To any mad enough to enter the graveyard of frost, heed this warning. As the oceans freeze over, and the gods play with its shape, its form, combat the cold with leather, or else meet a sub-zero end like the pirates before thee."]
	quest.43F02218C2BBA0ED.title: "Overdue Hand-Me-Downs"
	quest.4423745A40F6AC11.quest_desc: [
		"Certain actions such as killing animals, villagers, or babies will gain you points in a particular stat: naughtiness. Reaching certain values, you will hear the laugh of Krampus."
		"Naughtiness can be reduced through \"good\" actions such as using bonemeal on plants or taming animals."
		"The evilometer lets you track your naughtiness"
	]
	quest.4479AB901F8621D9.quest_desc: [
		"So, you wish to learn the art of occultism? You wish to summon demons to do your bidding? Very well. I will teach you what I know."
		"&o&6Occultism&r is a mod based around drawing pentacles and sacrifcing items to summon demons for a variety of different tasks. It allows for a unique form of automation utilizing mobs and not blocks. The mod also features ways to get specific drops earlier than usual."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To begin, you will want &oDemon's Dream&r, a new crop that forms a base for future actions. Seeds can be found by breaking grass."
	]
	quest.4479AB901F8621D9.title: "Occult Beginnings"
	quest.44977686A91D674C.title: "Find All of Alex's Caves"
	quest.44A41664198FD457.quest_desc: [
		"&6&oQuanta is the stat that affects the randomness of your enchantments&r. A range is created based on your level and Quanta. The higher your Quanta, the larger this range is. This can be seen as both a good and bad thing, as you'll have access to stronger enchantments, but the strength will also become less consistent."
		"Quanta can be increased by stronger bookshelves or &o&6by placing skulls near the enchanting table.&r"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/quanta.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.44A41664198FD457.title: "Quanta"
	quest.44A93A794D4165FC.quest_desc: [
		"As you explore, you will find floating island's high in the sky, these are Skyslime Islands!"
		""
		"Slime has many uses in smithing. Though it's most known for it's utility in making Slime Alloys"
	]
	quest.44A93A794D4165FC.quest_subtitle: "Gross, But Useful"
	quest.44A93A794D4165FC.title: "Slimy Goodness"
	quest.44FC5F13D63E4BD2.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat tdn_str.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Created as part of the Techointegration Project, the Tendon Strengthers are a set of mechanical exoskeletal legs that can &lincrease the wearer's speed by 10%&r. When sprinting, they provide a boost to muscle and pushing force, allowing the wearer to &ljump 50% higher&r."
		"Being that they are mechanical in nature, they require energy to function."
	]
	quest.44FC5F13D63E4BD2.title: "tdn_str.jv"
	quest.452157A246B3BF7C.quest_desc: [
		"The Afrit Crusher is faster than its Djinni counterpart and can give up to 4 of a raw ore's corresponding dust, and can do so quickly to boot."
		"Abras' Conjure"
	]
	quest.452157A246B3BF7C.title: "Grit From Afrit"
	quest.4529EF7EA98B474C.quest_desc: ["With the Crucible, I've managed to alloy together Dragonheart Chunks and Worldroot Ingots. This material is much stronger than its components. I believe it will prove a useful material for some rather powerful armor and weapons."]
	quest.4529EF7EA98B474C.title: "Dragon and World Combined"
	quest.4532D8D7E4963F89.quest_desc: [
		"As a werewolf, you will receive buffs to your defense and attack, being able to pierce some armor in your base form. &oWhile you will be transformed automatically at night, you can also transform during the day, but you will be weaker, and can only stay in them for a limited time, shown by the red bar over your hotbar.&r In addition, you will only be able to consume meat."
		"Open the werewolf menu either by clicking the button in your inventory or through the keybind (Default P)"
	]
	quest.4537DD077CD404BF.quest_desc: [
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"You got \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"the f\"},{\"text\":\"lesh? Good, no\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"w you\"},{\"text\":\" ca\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"n r\"},{\"text\":\"eally begin. There are t\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"w\"},{\"text\":\"o mac\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"hine\"},{\"text\":\"s, a \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"Bio-Forge and a Decomposer\"},{\"text\":\". I can exp\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"lain m\"},{\"text\":\"ore onc\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"e y\"},{\"text\":\"ou have \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"th\"},{\"text\":\"em.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/bioforge-and-decomposer.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.4537DD077CD404BF.title: "Mechanical Meets Biological"
	quest.45547B4089A3D0F1.quest_desc: ["Obtained from Ignis"]
	quest.45AF68A92FF37768.quest_desc: ["It's said that long ago, the higher beings grew bored of the frozen seas that scattered the land, and chose to add new life to the barren areas in what's now considered the Ice Mazes."]
	quest.4654D02DBE4CCB87.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ful-blz.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Created by combining an energy crystal with blaze powder, &lBlaze Fuel&r harnesses the energy of The Nether itself to burn at extrodinarily high temperatures"
	]
	quest.4654D02DBE4CCB87.title: "ful-blz.jv"
	quest.47116E8A4D078C0B.quest_desc: [
		"Tales speak of a gem found in the deepest of the ocean, forged by frost and fear."
		"If you wander the maze in search of this &6&oAbyssal Amethyst&r, and hear vibrations under the icey ground below, beware, for &6&oThe Mother of The Maze&r has come for you. Powerful in her persuit, and said to be capable of breaking the very ice that separates you, killing her is said to be hard... but &6&operhaps not impossible&r."
	]
	quest.47116E8A4D078C0B.title: "Kill mother of maze"
	quest.47532F7269B287FF.quest_desc: [
		"So, you wish to become a sort of jeweler, now do you? Alright, in that case, I suggest you look into making a &o&6Gem Cutting Table&r. With it, you can combine &6&ocopies of gems&r, taking apart the bad and leaving only the good, higher quality behind. Along with this, &o&6Rarity Material&r is needed to reach the next stage, and &6&oGem Dust&r to fill in the cracks of the craft."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/gem-cutting-table.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.47532F7269B287FF.title: "Jeweler in Training"
	quest.4759A40CA643929B.quest_desc: ["Those commited may find themselves more interested in treasure than old clothing, and those before have certainly stashed such items away in pouches of their own. Armor, gold, gems, &6&operhaps even a map or two&r."]
	quest.4759A40CA643929B.title: "Treasure no longer needed"
	quest.4777E3CA84CDFCCB.quest_desc: [
		"If you've tamed any kind of dragon, you've likely wanted to travel with it. Unfortunately, this can prove difficult with some species. But fear not, for there exists a means to carry your scaly companion with you."
		"A Dragon Binder when bound to a tamed dragon will &6&ostore their very being inside it&r, allowing you to release it whenever and wherever you see fit. But these items are not simple to make. Each requires a &6&oDragon Binder Core&r, made from Worldroot, Echo Shards, and a &6&oDragon Seal Stone&r, found in chests of structures such as Ancient Cities and Strongholds."
	]
	quest.4777E3CA84CDFCCB.title: "To Bind a Beast"
	quest.47932CAA0EC704F4.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ch-007.jv"
		"Indentifier: ch-007 | Informal Name: Carcass"
		"-------------------------------------------"
		"After infecting a polar bear at site Remus, the resulting ch-007 showed to be passive at first. Unlike its cousin, ch-006, ch-007 did not outright attack researchers. Instead, it showed interest in infection, &lattempting to cover other creatures with a large volley of what appeared to be blood&r. When this did not work, or when presented with something immune to infection, its projectiles &ltook on a new, more directly dangerous form&r."
		"Over time, researchers began to notice growth in ch-007. While not immediately noticed, the timing was shown to line up with the deaths of other subjects. It appeared that &lwhen a technoflesh creature died near ch-007, it would increase in size and strength&r."
	]
	quest.47932CAA0EC704F4.title: "ch-007 \"Carcass\""
	quest.47B33098B502ED89.quest_desc: [
		"The Volitans is a highly territorial semi-aquatic dragon species adapted for environmental control, area denial, and prolonged territorial occupation. Volitans individuals are known for gradually altering surrounding environments through the accumulation of toxins and venomous biological residue. Volitans pursue prey over long distances. And they also establish dominance by controlling movement within their territory, forcing intruders into increasingly hazardous conditions through toxic spines, lingering breath attacks, and environmental pressure. Although often associated with toxicity, Volitans' activity is not inherently destructive. Once territorial disturbances cease, affected ecosystems frequently stabilize over time, suggesting the species alters environments as a defensive adaptation rather than out of indiscriminate aggression. &n&4If met in the wild, it will view a person as hostile.&r"
		"Before a Volitans can be tamed, &4&nit must first be subdued in combat&r. Wild Volitans become vulnerable only after their health is &4&nreduced to approximately 60 HP&r, causing the dragon to enter a stunned state. Once stunned, the dragon may be fed preferred foods such as &n&4tropical fish, pufferfish, raw cod, salmon, and Hearty Dragon Meal&r."
		"Feeding a Volitans does not guarantee successful taming. Failed attempts will restore a portion of the dragon's health, immediately ending its stunned state and forcing the player to subdue it again."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/volitans.png width:300 height:150 align:center}"
	]
	quest.47B33098B502ED89.quest_subtitle: "Tame a Volitans"
	quest.47B33098B502ED89.title: "Mors per Venenum"
	quest.4802FDF08E8A88E6.quest_desc: [
		"Apotheosis adds several mechanics to the game that work at allowing you to reach greater heights than ever before while staying close to Vanilla Minecraft."
		"The Chronicle of Shadows serves as the guide book for Apotheosis."
	]
	quest.482194464FFFE2DE.quest_desc: ["The Mummy familiar is a powerful combative spirit that will attack hostile mobs. Upgrading it increases the damage it deals."]
	quest.482194464FFFE2DE.title: "Mummy Familiar"
	quest.4892EFBE1C7AB547.title: "8x Emeralds"
	quest.48AC8545D66B71B7.quest_desc: ["Congratulations! Getting the builder upgraded is an important step. The Builder can only build or upgrade any other hut up to the level of their own hut. So, in order for the Builder to upgrade any building, the Builder’s Hut must be upgraded first. Then the Builder will be able to upgrade any other building(s)."]
	quest.48AC8545D66B71B7.quest_subtitle: "Level Up a Builders Hut"
	quest.48CC4DEF7370FC2F.quest_desc: ["Altar of Cleansing can be used to cure yourself of vampirism, but using it will kill you."]
	quest.48CC4DEF7370FC2F.quest_subtitle: "Optional"
	quest.48D9D8BC413CADEA.quest_desc: ["Fishing lines alter the difficulty of the fishing minigame. Although the basic line is purely cosmetic, it's needed to craft better ones."]
	quest.48D9D8BC413CADEA.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Fishing Line"
	quest.48D9D8BC413CADEA.title: "Line Em Up"
	quest.48DE59E5EA690CE1.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ptb_chr.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Due to the power hungry nature of the Advanced Series of items, technicians were tasked with creating a portable power source. The finalized design was a success. &lBy depositing batteries inside the charger's inventory, it will passively recharge any advanced items in inventory.&r"
	]
	quest.48DE59E5EA690CE1.title: "ptb_chr.jv"
	quest.48FD69C56789F0D9.quest_desc: [
		"Have you noticed the blue arrow next to your hotbar? One of the most important things to know about combat in this pack is the ability to &6&oroll&r&r."
		"Once assigned to any key in the controls menu (Default: R), pressing it will launch you in the direction you're moving, or forwards if you aren't. The meter will slowly recharge before allowing you to roll again. This is a very helpful skill, and can be key to avoiding some attacks."
	]
	quest.48FD69C56789F0D9.title: "On a roll!"
	quest.48FF58C2F6B54BB3.quest_desc: ["The Copper Fishing Line lowers a fish's speed, causing the slider in the fishing minigame to move slower."]
	quest.48FF58C2F6B54BB3.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Copper Fishing Line"
	quest.48FF58C2F6B54BB3.title: "Steampunk Era"
	quest.49033A134A6F1B8D.quest_desc: ["Astral dust is found in frozen chests"]
	quest.49033A134A6F1B8D.title: "Complete the set"
	quest.490628CE108A833A.quest_desc: [
		"The Courier runs back and forth from the Warehouse to all the worker huts in your colony, delivering materials to workers and putting finished products in the Warehouse. The level of the Courier’s Hut will dictate how many items the Courier can carry and the amount of requests they can keep track of at a time."
		""
		"Courier’s don’t just work on their own. You must build a warehouse, and assign the courier to work at a warehouse. "
		""
		"Note: If you have multiple Warehouses, Couriers will only see the items in the Warehouse they are assigned to. This is helpful in the late game when troubleshooting requests."
	]
	quest.490628CE108A833A.quest_subtitle: "Build a Courier Hut"
	quest.4919CA330CE83242.quest_subtitle: "Gold Chests"
	quest.493B9FC17C3CF3CA.quest_desc: [
		"The Rabbit Hutch is where the Rabbit Herder will raise and butcher rabbits. You will have to capture and bring in two rabbits to the Rabbit Hutch, as the Rabbit Herder will not catch and bring in any rabbits."
		""
		"The Rabbit Herder will only keep two rabbits alive per hut level, so at level 5 they will have ten rabbits in their holding pens."
		""
		"A rabbit may approach you if you hold a carrot or dandilion, but they won't follow you. Bring them back with a lead.  "
	]
	quest.493B9FC17C3CF3CA.quest_subtitle: "Build a Rabbit Hutch"
	quest.4947377B74C7D158.quest_desc: ["Hm? You recognize this tablet now, do you? Perhaps you have interest in the arcane arts. If so, you'll definitely be needing these. Not many ways to get some save for looting homes and old crypts."]
	quest.4947377B74C7D158.title: "8x Blank Runestones"
	quest.495F0F7106CC9D01.quest_desc: [
		"The Stegonaut is a heavily armored defensive dragon species known for its exceptional protective instincts, social imprinting behavior, and battlefield resilience. Stegonauts prioritize allied defense above direct confrontation, frequently positioning themselves between danger and bonded entities without requiring direct commands. Their immense durability and willingness to absorb incoming force made them highly valued companions for both riders and accompanying creatures. Stegonauts are particularly notable for their compatibility with allied mounts, pets, and cooperative combat behavior. &4&nIn the wild, they are notably peaceful.&r"
		"Stegonauts can be &n&4tamed through direct feeding using a single favored food item, such as raw cod, salmon, or hearty dragon meal&r. Due to the species' naturally social and imprint-driven behavior, successful taming relies less on subduing aggression and more on establishing immediate trust and recognition."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/stegonaut.png width:300 height:177 align:center}"
	]
	quest.495F0F7106CC9D01.quest_subtitle: "Tame a Stegonaut"
	quest.495F0F7106CC9D01.title: "My Sturdy Friend"
	quest.49793060345FB28C.quest_desc: [
		"The Cowhand’s Hut is where the Cowhand will milk, breed, and butcher cows for leather. The Cowhand will only keep two cows alive per hut level, so at level 5 they will have ten cows in their holding pens to breed and butcher."
		""
		"Note: &eYou must bring your own cows to the pen.&r"
	]
	quest.49793060345FB28C.quest_subtitle: "Build a Cowhand's Hut"
	quest.4987607027AD1D38.quest_desc: ["Just like Chests, Barrels can be upgraded in the same way. But also in a unique way too."]
	quest.4987607027AD1D38.quest_subtitle: "Barrel Time!"
	quest.498F02A60A22B5E1.quest_desc: [
		"I can't believe that worked. The tablet talks about the portals alright. I guess now we know how, all that's left is to try this one more time."
		"&0Let's hope it doesn't follow us.&r"
	]
	quest.498F02A60A22B5E1.title: "Welcome To Hell!"
	quest.4990D952610404AF.quest_desc: [
		"In addition to the primary three attributes is &o&6Rectification&r. This is an extra attribute that lessens the negative chances of &o&6Quanta&r. Put simply, &6&omore Rectification is always good and increases the consistency of more powerful enchantments.&r"
		"One way to increase Rectification outside of bookshelves is &o&6by placing Amethyst Clusters nearby.&r"
	]
	quest.4990D952610404AF.title: "Rectification"
	quest.49E5EB307780A00E.quest_desc: [
		"Some random guy stopped by a while back. Well, I say that, but only 'cause I heard footsteps. Opened the door to find this strange metal I'd never seen before and a note. I fashioned it into this pickaxe, and it's pretty good, but I won' lie, sometimes I feel sick when I'm near it."
		"I'll sell it 'o ya. Give you the note, too. Just... keep it away from me."
	]
	quest.49E5EB307780A00E.title: "Odd Pickaxe"
	quest.4A47FB945C0C4886.quest_desc: ["They say that long, long ago, the gods grew bored with the world they'd created. In search of something that may entertain them, the god of the storm transformed the deepest of the oceans covered with ice into a maze. Now a truly cursed place where those who venture in never return, it's said that even the water itself freezes you down to the very bone. Perhaps that's why so many wear leather."]
	quest.4A47FB945C0C4886.title: "Legends Carved in Ice"
	quest.4A5169146F81C5AF.quest_desc: ["Using a Sigil of Socketing, you can add tierless gem sockets to your items. Being that they are tierless, &6&oany gem can be inserted into them&r, provided they're compatible with the item type. These are also the only types of sockets that can later be &oAscended&r."]
	quest.4A5169146F81C5AF.title: "Socket Rocket?"
	quest.4A58FF0B04179B25.quest_desc: ["Mushroom Colonies are a renewable source of mushrooms created by placing a mushroom on rich soil. As the colony grows, extra mushrooms can be sheared off, and will regrow in time."]
	quest.4A58FF0B04179B25.title: "Fungus Amongus"
	quest.4A65E698C5C2306C.quest_desc: ["The Beaver familiar gives its owner increase speed when breaking wooden blocks. In addition, it will cut down any newly grown trees, provided the tree is small enough. When upgraded, it can give its owners snacks by right clicking."]
	quest.4A65E698C5C2306C.title: "Beaver Familiar"
	quest.4A725E741485566D.title: "Very Very Interesting"
	quest.4A73DC6507969015.quest_desc: [
		"Interacting with minions shows their inventory menu and accessory slots. From there you can order them to follow you, defend you, Defend the area, Stay, or Collect resources. Alternatively, you can edit their appearance and lock them from accepting global commands, which you can do by accessing the command menu (default R)"
		""
		"Minions start out weak, but can grow stronger with the usage of more enhanced moon charms. The tasks required to obtain these charms become available as you level up in your lord status."
	]
	quest.4A79D125A5C0F8F7.quest_desc: ["The helmet is only obtained by killing Captain Cornelia"]
	quest.4A79D125A5C0F8F7.title: "1000 dpeths under the sea"
	quest.4B341E2EB276866A.quest_desc: ["The Headless Ratman familiar will steal the heads of mobs killed nearby and give its master increased damage against that mob. When brought down to 50% of its health, the rider will die, but can be \"rebuilt\" with 2 sticks, 2 wheat, 1 haybale, and 1 carved pumpkin."]
	quest.4B341E2EB276866A.title: "Headless Ratman"
	quest.4B605AD4992DD0F5.quest_desc: [
		"The Gauntlet Arena is a structure you want to be on the lookout for. Sadly I cannot help much in terms of locating it, though I've heard they aren't the hardest to find."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/gauntlet_arena.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.4B605AD4992DD0F5.title: "Talk To The Hand"
	quest.4BCD060E27C56554.quest_desc: [
		"At the very top of the crusher hierchy is the Marid Crusher, boasting incredible speeds and crushing ores into six of their respective dusts."
		"Summoning one requries the usage of Fatma's Incentivized Attraction, so it is not a ritual for the unexperienced."
	]
	quest.4BCD060E27C56554.title: "Pinacle of Crushing"
	quest.4BFAEB671E0D2029.quest_subtitle: "Motherslime"
	quest.4BFB2D892CC29D6D.quest_desc: ["To mine otherworld materials, one must make a pickaxe of said materials. Iesnium is the go-to material, but to obtain it, you need to make an Infused Pickaxe first."]
	quest.4CE580B31A397745.quest_desc: ["Long guarded by the draugr that roam it, The Frosted Prison is a gargantuan structure housing the cursed soul of &6&oMaledictus.&r If you aim to conquer it and claim the Legendary Eye in his posession, then come prepared, less you meet a similar demise."]
	quest.4CE580B31A397745.title: "Cursed Crypt"
	quest.4D279009D425E84B.quest_desc: ["Can be used to locate budding amethyst."]
	quest.4D54B17785EC3EC0.quest_desc: ["Dragons are powerful creatures that come in many shapes and forms. Saint's Dragons aims to add variety within these powerful beings. Unlike other dragon based mods, dragons do not spawn in nests or structures. They are instead found in the wild, roaming, or remaining in their territories. While most are neutral, some prpesent a dangerous threat, so be on guard, and be prepared."]
	quest.4D54B17785EC3EC0.title: "Dragon Encounter 2"
	quest.4D61009737D94BDA.quest_subtitle: "Reach 25 Citizens"
	quest.4D867CCB572BFFA9.quest_desc: [
		"To obtain Shub Niggurath, one must first use a golden apple on a chimera familiar to seperate the goat from its body. Then once in a forest biome, the goat must be right clicked with black dye, flint, and an eye of ender. Doing so will convert it to Shub Niggurath."
		"Shub Niggurath summons its children to fight enemies. When upgraded, a warning bell is given to it, and hitting it will ring the bell, attracting nearby enemies."
	]
	quest.4D867CCB572BFFA9.title: "Shub Niggurath"
	quest.4D88C96EE88FCB2A.title: "I am Become Death"
	quest.4D92CD853B2371EB.quest_desc: ["The Nether isn't just a barren wasteland, you know. There's many different biomes and ecosystems, with different resources scattered about. There's a few that I find to be more common, so perhaps you could try to visit them all."]
	quest.4D92CD853B2371EB.title: "The Hottest Places to Tour"
	quest.4D9DC4973FD340E5.quest_desc: [
		"The Combat Academy is where your Knights in Training will train to become Knight. This also allows them to level up without a risk of dying to mobs."
		"The Knights in Training require a sword and shield to practice. They will attack the practice dummies, a pumpkin on top of a bale of hay."
		""
		"Tip: Consider setting the hiring mode to automatic so new recruits or kids growing up will automatically start training if not already attending school"
	]
	quest.4D9DC4973FD340E5.quest_subtitle: "Build a Combat Academy"
	quest.4DD7E2BD8508A117.quest_subtitle: "Build one of every herder hut."
	quest.4DEEB71D2AB760AE.quest_desc: ["The &o&6Storage Sac&r acts like a mix between a shulker box and a bundle. It can be placed down and picked up like the former, and its inventory can be accessed through your inventory like the latter. It can hold up to 15 stacks."]
	quest.4DFD059C412284D5.quest_desc: [
		"You've done well and gotten your bearings, but it's likely beginning to get dark, no? In this case, you'll want to keep your surroundings lit. This will go a long way in keeping hostile mobs at bay."
		"I, Professor Larch, recommend &o&6torches&r as the quickest and easiest method. A stick and some sort of coal is the easiest way to craft them. &6&oIf you've not gone underground yet, charcoal can be made by burning wooden logs.&r"
		"Something you will immediately notice is that holding items like torches visibly light the area around you without needing to be placed. Do note that this only helps you, and will not prevent things such as mobs."
	]
	quest.4DFD059C412284D5.title: "Light em up up up"
	quest.4DFFAE7DF0E17F96.quest_desc: [
		"As a vampire, you won't die immediately. Instead, when taking fatal damage, you will enter a Downed state. Waiting long enough, you will be able to resurrect yourself, and your blood bar will be converted to health. Afterwards, you will receive a potion effect, during which you cannot revive."
		"YOu can still be killed outright by fire and holy water, and vampire hunters often carry stakes to finish you off."
	]
	quest.4E01F448897FC3F6.title: "Bleeding The Bleeding Bolt"
	quest.4E17A7CEDA5CA534.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ext_stl_ing.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Researchers managed to gather enough of the unknown metal to forge into an ingot. The heat appeared to have set off some sort of chemical reaction. Those working on the project have been recorded as feeling sick. For safety reasons, they have since been quarantined."
	]
	quest.4E17A7CEDA5CA534.title: "ext_stl_ing.jv"
	quest.4E3580D10FB8FC76.quest_desc: ["Each gives a different full set bonus"]
	quest.4E3580D10FB8FC76.title: "Helm of The Blinding Abyss"
	quest.4E763FD9BA473520.quest_desc: [
		"The Ignivorus is a colossal fire-adapted dragon species known for its overwhelming physical presence and extreme thermal output. Native primarily to the Nether, Ignivoruses are capable of drastically altering their surroundings through prolonged exposure alone, often rendering occupied regions permanently hostile to other lifeforms. The Ignivorus relies on sustained pressure, environmental dominance, and absolute escalation once engaged in combat. Its immense resilience and refusal to retreat have made it one of the most feared apex predators documented. &4&nAny meetings will likely be hostile.&r"
		"Before an Ignivorus can be tamed, &4&nit must first be subdued in combat&r. Wild Ignivoruses become vulnerable only after their health is &4&nreduced to approximately 100 HP&r, causing the dragon to enter a stunned state. Once stunned, the dragon may be fed preferred foods such as &n&4raw cod, salmon, beef, and Hearty Dragon Meal&r."
		"Feeding an Ignivorus does not guarantee successful taming. Failed attempts will restore a portion of the dragon's health, immediately ending its stunned state and forcing the player to subdue it again."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/ignivorus.png width:300 height:199 align:center}"
	]
	quest.4E763FD9BA473520.quest_subtitle: "Tame an Ignivorus"
	quest.4E763FD9BA473520.title: "Scorched Earth"
	quest.4E8F017564A2C581.quest_desc: ["A human heart is dropped by vampire hunters. It is used as a crafting material, an item for leveling up, and as food to replenish one's blood bar."]
	quest.4EA4C799624AA35F.title: "8x Diamonds"
	quest.4EB7EBA9F1F56744.quest_desc: [
		"To summon The Leviathan is by no means an easy task. It will require an Abyssal Sacrifice, crafted using &o&6rare materials and items plucked from the bodies of the city's residents&r. Of all the ingredients, the two that stand out are &6&oThe Athame and Coral Chunk&r."
		"The Athame is a holy dagger held only by Deepling Priests and Warlocks, used in abyssal rituals. Coral chunks can be ripped off of a dead Coralssus, akin to golems and powerful mounts."
	]
	quest.4EB7EBA9F1F56744.title: "Sacrificial Blessings"
	quest.4EB82837E3678D45.quest_desc: [
		"The &6&oBlazing Hellshelf&r is an upgraded Hellshelf that &6&ooffers higher stats in exchange for lowering the amount of clues you can see&r."
		"This can be rectified by using the Hellshelf of Sight"
	]
	quest.4EC31168490064D6.title: "A fine addition to my collection"
	quest.4EE7637130ABFB0D.title: "Blackened Steel"
	quest.4EE9E84C828A9D70.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat bat_pnl.jv"
		"-------------------------"
		"With batteries capable of containing the extraterrestrial energy created, the next step was to connect them with basic electronics to be used in more complex creations."
	]
	quest.4EE9E84C828A9D70.title: "bat_pnl.jv"
	quest.4EEF0962CC249F30.quest_desc: [
		"Starving colonists will eat just about anything, including raw food and rotten flesh. Yuck! "
		""
		"When citizens are hungry, they will come to the Restaurant and the Cook will give them food. (assuming you have food to give them) Consider building a Fisher’s Hut, or a Cowhand’s Hut. "
		""
		"Note: Make sure to choose a fuel for your cook to use. Some popular options are charcoal, sticks, and planks, although anything with a burn time will work. "
	]
	quest.4EEF0962CC249F30.quest_subtitle: "Build a Restaurant"
	quest.4FC86601AD55B185.quest_desc: ["Not guaranteed, it makes illagers and villagers drop their emeralds"]
	quest.4FDACAE8F84DA3BD.quest_desc: [
		"{image:modpack:textures/umvuthi-throne.png width:160 height:90 align:center}"
		"&eUmvuthi, The Sunbird.&r I'll be frank with you, I don't like this guy. All these masks and cronies of his. But if you're in the savana, be sure to keep an eye out for an Umvuthana Grove. Maybe you have the strength it takes to slay this bird of terror and claim its Guardian Eye"
		"PS: Watch out for the laser."
	]
	quest.4FDACAE8F84DA3BD.quest_subtitle: "The Sunbird"
	quest.503C5A0CE113962C.quest_desc: ["Is the builder going too slow? With this hammer equiped and the right resources in your inventory, you can help the builder out. Simply click anywhere in the hut being built to place blocks for the builder. "]
	quest.503C5A0CE113962C.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Hammer"
	quest.5050429C5EBE871F.quest_desc: ["The familiar ring is used to store familiars. When worn, it can often grant the effect of the stored familiar to its wearer. In addition, if another player unleashes the familiar, they will begin to serve them."]
	quest.506D131D4A0F6CE8.title: "Make a Totem of Souls"
	quest.507322CB01827F36.quest_desc: ["Cobalt is a rare ore, well known for it's bright blue hue standing out against the firey backdrop of the nether. It is a strong metal on it's own, but can be improved even further, IF you're willing to excavate around the boiling lava seas..."]
	quest.507322CB01827F36.quest_subtitle: "Nether Iron"
	quest.507322CB01827F36.title: "Blue Metal"
	quest.508F4A0DC217F01F.quest_desc: ["Instead of Using three whole Diamonds to make a pick, you can add one to your iron pick, making it diamond tipped. This gives it the same properties as a vanilla Diamond Pick, being much more durable and being able to mine things like Obsidian! "]
	quest.508F4A0DC217F01F.quest_subtitle: "Cheaper, Better, Stronger"
	quest.508F4A0DC217F01F.title: "Diamond Tipped!"
	quest.510E0EB270B43037.title: "MMO"
	quest.513C7D4E29043CD5.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat &kReanimator&r.jv"
		"cat: &kReanimator&r.jv: Permission denied"
		"kane@remus~$ sudo cat &kReanimator&r.jv"
		"[sudo: authenticate] Password:"
		"------------------------------"
		"Created as part of the Techointegration Project, the Reanimator has the ability to save its user from lethal damage by expelling all stored energy, entering a temporary cooldown afterwards. After usage, it must be recharged full before possible activation."
	]
	quest.513C7D4E29043CD5.title: "&kReanimator&r.jv"
	quest.51489406A1269085.quest_desc: [
		"Feeling lonely in your travels? Perhaps a companion is what you need. For many, this means a pet, though for some it means... other entities."
		"However, I, Professor Larch, am not one to judge another on their tastes. I will, however, suggest a wolf as a companion. They are very loyal creatures, and iconic for a reason."
	]
	quest.51489406A1269085.title: "Need a friend?"
	quest.51505202836EF091.title: "Time 4"
	quest.517C023BA8F2CE58.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat xry_ggl.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Created as the first in the Techointegration Project, The X-Ray goggles were created in response to CH-006's camouflage abilities. &lIn addition to improved vision in the dark, the goggles also highlight an entity's weak spots, making them take more damage from the wearer's attacks.&r"
	]
	quest.517C023BA8F2CE58.title: "xry_ggl.jv"
	quest.51AB4D8CC9052211.quest_desc: ["You've obtained some Demon's Dream. Good. Now we will want to &o&6combine it with a book&r and obtain &n&6The Dictionary of Spirits&r. This tome serves as both a guide and a tool for rituals."]
	quest.51AB4D8CC9052211.title: "The Book of Demons"
	quest.51E87962019534D5.quest_desc: [
		"Alloys are typically much stronger then traditional metals, surpassing even Diamond, and at times, Netherite. Just be careful, the Smelter will alloy any metal that CAN ALLOY, wether you want it to or not."
		""
		"Be Polite, Empty your Smelters, Avoid Making 10 stacks of Rose Gold. "
	]
	quest.51E87962019534D5.quest_subtitle: "Mixing Metals"
	quest.51E87962019534D5.title: "Alloy Time!"
	quest.51FDF5A788044E71.quest_desc: ["Whether you did so slowly over time or consciously to summon him, accumulating 100 naughtiness points will summon Krampus himself, a very strong spirit. If not killed, he will appear to judge you with every future naughty action you take until he is slain."]
	quest.52453550206EC770.quest_desc: ["The Dyer's Hut is where the Dyer will craft dyes and dye other items, including red nether bricks and dark prismarine. They won't dye concrete or concrete powder, though."]
	quest.52453550206EC770.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Dyer's Hut"
	quest.52B0A510B06AF3A0.quest_subtitle: "Soft Chest"
	quest.52DA17035C75DEBE.quest_desc: ["By combining crushed obsidian and end stone, you can create purple chalk, the second strongest chalk"]
	quest.52DACA3870E942B9.quest_desc: [
		"To combat The Storm Empress, one must simply find her anchor at the peak of Acropolis. But be prepared, as &6&oher heavy strikes and ability with electrocution&r will live up to her title."
		"Scylla's anchor is her primary weapon, capable of grabbing foes from afar. She can also send out torrents of water, &6&omaking her enemy wet and amplifying her electrical attacks&r, such as a spear of lightning that bypasses armor."
		"To fight one such as her is never an even match, magical serpents being summoned to aid Scylla in your defeat."
		"&6&oIndeed, be aware of the water, be careful of the anchor, and you may yet live to see another day.&r"
	]
	quest.52DACA3870E942B9.title: "Storm's End"
	quest.532C02B55492142D.quest_desc: ["A simple aircraft in design, the Biplane is designed to move fast. Its storage allows for great use in supply runs or ventures where items need to be brought along."]
	quest.532C02B55492142D.title: "The Brothers' Creation"
	quest.5356973CA8AF15BB.quest_desc: ["Of all the slimes, Earthslime is the most well known, being bright green and the slime itself being found in many places of the world. Though hardened crystals can be found underground in geodes. much like ameythyst."]
	quest.5356973CA8AF15BB.quest_subtitle: "Green Slime"
	quest.536A723164A346B6.quest_desc: [
		"The first part of the main progression steps are as follow:"
		"(reveal if you want to be spoiled)"
		""
		"||1. Explore ancient cities to find Ancient Dragonite Fragments"
		"2. Craft a Draconic Crucible (the new main crafting station of the mod)"
		"3. Mine the new Worldroot Ore in deep deepslate layers"
		"4. Obtain blaze powder to use as fuel for the Draconic Crucible (this is a tier 2 fuel item), or alternatively, tame a Cindervane and harvest its scales to craft Searing Coals (also tier 2 fuel item)"
		"4. Smelt the new Worldroot ores in the Draconic Crucible (require tier 2 fuels)"
		"5. Craft Worldroot tools (they're better than diamond but weaker than netherite)"
		""
		"The rest i'll let other players figure out||"
	]
	quest.537A8F99CC3F525D.quest_subtitle: "Hire 8 Guards"
	quest.538F30201366232F.title: "Fus Ro Dah!"
	quest.53A09EAB4421492A.quest_desc: ["Tier 1 Tools are equivlant to wood or stone vanilla tools, and can be made purely on the Tinker Station without worrying about liquid metal. \"Materials and You\" explains what you can use for what part. Bone and Flint are common and flimsy, but are often better then dull old stone."]
	quest.53A09EAB4421492A.quest_subtitle: "Primitive, Shmimitive"
	quest.53A09EAB4421492A.title: "Tier 1 Tools"
	quest.53A31A5C0C000C7B.quest_desc: [
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"H\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ell\"},{\"text\":\"o? Ah, fi\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"nally, \"},{\"text\":\"contact. I was beginning to l\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"os\"},{\"text\":\"e \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ho\"},{\"text\":\"pe. Listen, I d\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"on't kn\"},{\"text\":\"ow how muc\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"h longe\"},{\"text\":\"r there \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"is f\"},{\"text\":\"or me, so I'll \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"keep\"},{\"text\":\" it brief.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"I've m\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ade\"},{\"text\":\" breakthroughs on life, its \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ver\"},{\"text\":\"y nature. But n\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ow I'\"},{\"text\":\"m lost. I need \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"you\"},{\"text\":\" to take in w\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"hat\"},{\"text\":\" I've learned, c\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ar\"},{\"text\":\"ry it on.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"text\":\"Please.\"}"
	]
	quest.53A31A5C0C000C7B.quest_subtitle: "{\"text\":\"Can you hear me?\",\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\"}"
	quest.53A31A5C0C000C7B.title: "What is this? Some kind of device?"
	quest.53F8923B85A8A9CC.quest_subtitle: "Hire 80 Guards!"
	quest.542299DFDB714816.quest_desc: ["The Blacksmith Familiar has a chance of repairing its master's tools when stone is picked up. In addition, giving it iron ingots or blocks will allow it to upgrade another familiar, providing them with addition effects."]
	quest.542299DFDB714816.title: "Blacksmith Familiar"
	quest.54434A0CA6214A3A.quest_desc: ["Unlike other tomes, the Tome of Scrapping serves a unique purpose. &o&6When placed in an anvil with an enchanted item, it will take half of the item's enchantments.&r The original item is lost in the process."]
	quest.54434A0CA6214A3A.title: "Scrap It"
	quest.5482C9C8A1CF524C.quest_desc: ["The Nether is home to some of this world's hottest... most volitile substances."]
	quest.5482C9C8A1CF524C.quest_subtitle: "Treated with Hellfire"
	quest.5482C9C8A1CF524C.title: "Hotter Yet Hotter"
	quest.54B5AFEFE66E574B.quest_desc: ["Rain has an interesting effect on fishing, huh? Well, it's not the only one. But weather can be unpredictable. That's where the &6&oWeather Radio&r comes in to save the day. Once placed down, standing nearby will let you see the coming forecast on the bottom left corner of your screen."]
	quest.54EDC18D9EC77ADA.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat fla_spw.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"The Flame Spewer is capable of releasing high amounts of superheated energy from the Blaze Fuel Cylinder held within. Unlike the Flamethrower, its stationary positioning allows it to never run out of fuel."
	]
	quest.54EDC18D9EC77ADA.title: "fla_spw.jv"
	quest.550F3C0585F44DCC.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat sta_crg_stn.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Due to the increase energy requirements of the advanced tools, a new source of power was required. To this end, the mechanics, chemists, and technicians worked to develop the Station"
	]
	quest.550F3C0585F44DCC.title: "sta_crg_stn.jv"
	quest.551ADB23A1679792.quest_subtitle: "Better Barrels"
	quest.5554564CABF86018.quest_desc: ["Now this is where we get interesting. This scroll will let you teleport to &oany&r known waystone, almost like you're using one yourself. It'll even negate the experience cost for you. One use though, so make it count."]
	quest.5554564CABF86018.title: "Warp Scroll"
	quest.55851524FDDB6959.quest_desc: ["The Cookery is where the Chef prepares meals for your citizens. When other buildings request food, the Chef will cook it. Pair the Cookery with your Restaurants to automatically keep them stocked with fresh meals."]
	quest.5635D89E2594043D.quest_desc: [
		"Now you've got the basics down."
		"To level up to level 4, one must fill this altar with several bottles of blood.&r The first time, you need 4000mb, or 40 units of blood. The numbers increase from there, to 70 units, then 100."
	]
	quest.5635D89E2594043D.title: "Lie in The Blood Where You Bathe"
	quest.56B565694503D9C4.title: "Waystone 5"
	quest.56BECC7019FEC95F.quest_desc: [
		"The Cindervane is a highly migratory draconic species known for its exceptional endurance and long-distance flight capability. Unlike territorial apex predators, Cindervanes prioritize survival, mobility, and environmental adaptation over prolonged combat engagement. Historically, many ancient civilizations are believed to have relied on established Cindervane migratory routes when constructing trade paths, evacuation corridors, and long-range messenger networks. Cindervanes are also domesticated for the purpose of transportation rather than combat mounts on a daily basis. Their tendency to disperse eggs across wide regions rather than defend centralized nesting grounds has led many researchers to classify the species as ecological carriers rather than territorial rulers. Although not specialized for sustained combat, Cindervanes remain highly dangerous when cornered. &n&4Wild Cindervanes are not hostile unless provoked.&r"
		"Similarly to domesticated wolves and cats, Cindervanes can be tamed through &4&ndirect feeding with preferred foods such as raw chicken, cod, salmon, and Hearty Dragon Meal.&r"
		"Due to their naturally cautious behavior, taming attempts may require multiple feedings before successful domestication occurs."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/cindervane.png width:300 height:180 align:center}"
	]
	quest.56BECC7019FEC95F.quest_subtitle: "Tame a Cindervane"
	quest.56BECC7019FEC95F.title: "Destruction Commence"
	quest.56C9557D933F0045.quest_desc: [
		"The Foundry gives byproducts the the Smeltery cannot. Smelting Iron will now make a small amount of Steel due to the high tempurature. Cobalt, Diamiond, and many more. The Foundry Also will NOT Alloy ores, making it perfect for bulk smelting without worrying that your metals will mix."
		""
		"If you'd like to make alloys, it might be best to keep the smeltery around."
	]
	quest.56C9557D933F0045.quest_subtitle: "Improved, Maybe"
	quest.56C9557D933F0045.title: "The Foundry"
	quest.56C9F3BA861F9CA8.quest_desc: ["A rather unique ability, the Twilight hook inverts the time preference of a fish, letting you find night fish in the day and day fish at night."]
	quest.56C9F3BA861F9CA8.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Twilight Hook"
	quest.56C9F3BA861F9CA8.title: "Forest Magic"
	quest.57100F16C9395F28.quest_desc: [
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Aside from a few decorative blocks, Bloomberries can be used for one particular, beautiful thing. \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"The Primordial Infestation effect\"},{\"text\":\". Using these berries for potions or a serum will grant this wonderful boon. Under its effect, you'll speak the Primordial Tongue. It will come naturally to you. Ah, a true gift~\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Even more, your death \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"will spread the flesh further\"},{\"text\":\". Even deceased, you will continue to breathe new life.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
	]
	quest.57100F16C9395F28.title: "A Wonderful Infestation"
	quest.57383C95CC6678D3.title: "16x Grout"
	quest.57B0727D357856C6.quest_desc: [
		"The aptly named &6&oDraconic Crucible&r is a powerful workstation crafted with Ancient Dragonite Fragments, a long forgotten material found in Ancient Cities, Nether Fortresses, and Bastions. The Crucible requires strong sources of heat such as &6&oBlaze Powder or Searing Coals&r to function, but can create some spectacular items."
		"Or you can use it as the world's most badass furnace, I guess. "
	]
	quest.57B0727D357856C6.title: "Doom's Furnace"
	quest.57C889EC980D33D9.quest_desc: ["I can finally top playing in the dirt (as much) and hand off my farming duties to someone else. I should probably have the farmer start with carrots since they don't need to be cooked, too..."]
	quest.57C889EC980D33D9.quest_subtitle: "Build a Farm"
	quest.57E6AD8682F2624A.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat bat-adv.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"A rechargeable battery, the extraction team found several on the persons of deceased researchers and tecnicians from Site Romulus. There were no traces of prints describing their creation, but also nothing to suggest they were created on-site. &lIt is possible other facilities may have these.&r"
	]
	quest.57E6AD8682F2624A.title: "bat-adv.jv"
	quest.5827E9110E4B19F9.quest_desc: ["I hope your citizens apprcaite all that you do for them. Spoiler alert, they don't thay are probably still complaining abount not enough guards, poor housing conditions, or refusing to eat the slop you put in front of them. (only commoners eat steak...)"]
	quest.5827E9110E4B19F9.quest_subtitle: "Build a Level 5 Mystical Site"
	quest.583A7AA84FEC027F.quest_desc: [
		"Before anything can be built, you need a Builder. The Builder must build their own Builder’s Hut before building any other huts, and they cannot build or upgrade a hut to a higher level than their own hut level. "
		""
		"The builder is arguably the hardest working citizen in your colony. (Second only to you). You are not limited to just one builder. As your colony grows, you may need multiple builders to keep up. "
	]
	quest.583A7AA84FEC027F.quest_subtitle: "Say that 10 times real fast! "
	quest.583A7AA84FEC027F.title: "Build the Builder Building"
	quest.584B0BD24BD79AEA.quest_desc: ["Once you've gotten enough naughtiness, two Krampus Henchmen will spawn and attack. Use this as your warning."]
	quest.585EFD3486B4D863.title: "A Special Shade of Green"
	quest.58697C4CF815054A.quest_desc: ["The Fleshkin Chest is like a regular chest for the most part, though it features less storage, only holding 42 stacks of items. Where it differs from a regular chest, however, is in its &odefense mechanism&r. You see, by default, &o&6only the player who placed the chest down will be able to open it. All other players will be attacked, instead. A player can be given permission by right clicking the chest with said player's tier 3 essence&r."]
	quest.5884738C49CA8E9B.quest_desc: ["Obtained from The Netherite Monstrosity"]
	quest.5884738C49CA8E9B.quest_subtitle: "The Monstrosity"
	quest.58A91870FFA1A844.quest_desc: ["To kill an Ignivorus is by no means an easy task. The monster is large, powerful, and merciless. However, it makes for some rather wonderful prey. A satisfying kill, rewarding one with even more powerful loot. The Ignivorus's wing hide, teeth, and most powerful of all, its heart are exceptionally tough. Even after death, an Ignivorus's heart runs hot, perhaps enough to use as fuel."]
	quest.58A91870FFA1A844.title: "True Dragon Slayer"
	quest.58B0624C9BBA1796.quest_desc: [
		"Requires you to have the demons dream effect when cutting down the tree"
		"Due to a bug, HT's Treechop will not drop otherworld logs. You must be crouching to chop the tree down normally."
	]
	quest.58C4A3B1A0BFD749.quest_desc: ["The End seems to contain a rare blood red material found on the bottomside of its islands. Due to its color and location, I've decided to call this material &4&nDragonheart&r. It is incredibly tough, requiring a pickaxe as strong or stronger than Netherite."]
	quest.58C4A3B1A0BFD749.title: "Dragonhearted"
	quest.58DC57C5FB7FE225.quest_desc: ["Once you've hit max level at 14, you can start to increase your age rank. You can do this by killing mobs with your bite attack. To check your progress on increasing your rank, interact with the stone altar fire bowls. As your age increases, you get more bite strength, damage, health, time to spend in your werewolf form during the day, and healing from your bite attack. However, you will also take more damage from silver oil and hunters, as well as having harsher prices from villagers."]
	quest.58E6B0A4E1DEA998.quest_desc: [
		"You'll find many a guide book in your adventures. Even with quests, sometimes you want a bit of more traditional reading. But carrying all those books around can be a hassle. Luckily for you, I, Professor Larch, know of a quite... &6&oEccentric Tome&r."
		"&6&oYou can combine this tome with any of your guide books in a crafting grid, and it will be added to the tome's chapters.&r From there, you simply right click with the tome to select the book you'd like to read. Hitting the air with the book in hand will return it to the tome.&r"
		"I suggest you make your own, then if you'd like, I've gone ahead and put something together for you to trade."
	]
	quest.58E6B0A4E1DEA998.title: "The Book of Babel"
	quest.592B100EDEFA0F5A.quest_desc: [
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"Great, you deci\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ded to le\"},{\"text\":\"arn. Alright, the\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\" fi\"},{\"text\":\"rst thing you'll nee\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"d is a\"},{\"text\":\" \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"Flesh Plunderer.\"},{\"text\":\" It's a s\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ick\"},{\"text\":\"le of sorts, \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"made fr\"},{\"italic\":true,\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"om bon\"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"e and raw meat.\"},{\"text\":\" I... wish I could tel\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"l yo\"},{\"text\":\"u \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"mo\"},{\"text\":\"re on how to mak\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"e on\"},{\"text\":\"e.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"It's a crucial tool needed to g\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"athe\"},{\"text\":\"r impo\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"rta\"},{\"text\":\"nt items fro\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"m mob\"},{\"text\":\"s that they otherwise w\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ould no\"},{\"text\":\"t usually dr\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"o\"},{\"text\":\"p. Just... make one, th\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"en go and k\"},{\"text\":\"ill a bunc\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"h of m\"},{\"text\":\"obs, especially pred\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"ato\"},{\"text\":\"rs, the ones with sharp claws and fangs.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/flesh-plunderer.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.592B100EDEFA0F5A.title: "A Fleshsickle"
	quest.5932AE4458E58E8A.quest_desc: ["Some fish can only be found underground or in very deep waters. For these, a &o&6Depth Meter&r is a valuable tool. Holding it in your hand, offhand, or in the Informational curios slot, the current depth will be visible in the bottom left corner of the screen."]
	quest.5981B3DEDD0B3827.quest_desc: [
		"&6&oSoul Energy&r is the driving force of the dark arts, so naturally, your first step as a fledgling caster is to harness this energy for yourself. To do this, a &o&6totem&r will be required. The craft the &6&ototem of roots&r, &oectoplasm&r is required. There are many ways to obtain it, but for yourself, I suggest seeking out a &4&owraith&r."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/wraith.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5981B3DEDD0B3827.title: "Fetch Me Their Souls!"
	quest.59B393F49F76FE66.quest_desc: ["I'll uh... I'll be real with ya for a momen'. I... do not remember where this thing came from. I just found it while cleaning. It's certainly a good tool, don't get me wrong. But something about it just feels... off."]
	quest.59B393F49F76FE66.title: "Eerie Pickaxe"
	quest.59E5F8A65B826B42.quest_desc: [
		"You may quickly notice that combat here is a little... different than average worlds. The first thing you'll likely notice is the moveset of your weapon. Indeed, each weapon has its own set of attacks and combos, from large sweeping motions to powerful slams. Even the simple knife is deadly when dual wielded."
		"This chapter aims to teach you about combat and its changes, to help you in your future endeavours."
	]
	quest.59E5F8A65B826B42.quest_subtitle: "Fighting 101"
	quest.5A11292F3000B167.title: "Cut up an orchid"
	quest.5A11A2FC20E5CE2A.quest_desc: [
		"The Barracks is the ultimate protection for your colony. The Barracks Towers (unlike the normal Guard tower) will employ and house one Guard for every level built, for a total of 5 Guards per Barracks Tower!"
		""
		"In the later game you will likely want two barracks chock full of &mexpendable&r brave souls."
		""
		"Tip: At level 3, you can hire spies for 5 gold per raid, these spies will go out into the world and if barbarians are spotted, the spies will tell you exactly where the barbarians are."
	]
	quest.5A11A2FC20E5CE2A.quest_subtitle: "Build a Barracks"
	quest.5A97C15CA4463102.quest_desc: [
		"Affixes will certainly not be the only item you come across in your travles. What is that shine in the dungeon's chest? The shimmering from within your enemy's bag? Why, it a &o&6Gem&r of course."
		"Gems are items that can add various effects to items they are slotted into. They can be found in several states, each with a corresponding rarity. These are &8Cracked&r, &2Chipped&r, &9Flawed&r, &5Normal&r, &cFlawless&r, and &6Perfect&r."
		"&6&oNot all gems work with all item types.&r You may find one that can only be used on armor, or perhaps everything but swords. In addition, &6&omost slots you'll find on Affixed items will be tiered&r, and will only accept a gem &6&oof the same or lower rarity&r."
		"If all of these match, then inserting the gem is as simple as putting both the item and the gem inside a &o&6smithing table&r."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/gems.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5A97C15CA4463102.title: "Shine Bright"
	quest.5AA9BF164EF88E5F.quest_desc: ["The seed pouch is a useful tool that acts like bundle for seeds and other plants such as saplings. Able to hold up to 10 stacks of a single seed, you can use it on soil or dirt and it will plant its contents as if you were holding them. What's more, any seeds you pick up will be immediately put inside the pouch if there's room."]
	quest.5AA9BF164EF88E5F.title: "A Sorta Seed Bank"
	quest.5AFA8806FF39B731.quest_desc: ["The Hellshelf of Sight is a unique bookshelf that does not offer any boosts to the primary attributes. &6&oInstead, it increases the amount of clues you can see when enchanting.&r"]
	quest.5B76548804FFB620.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ch-005.jv"
		"Indentifier: ch-005 | Informal Name: Blood Spreader"
		"-------------------------------------------"
		"After being infected during an accident with ch-004, Dr. ███'s pet wolf was infected. Immediately following this, the wolf was quaranteened, and ch-005 later emerged."
		"ch-005 is more in line with the other subjects, showcasing a strong defense to traditional weaponry."
		"Dr. ███ fell into hysterics trying to get to the subject. His actions resulted in its escape, and the site was put into immediate lockdown. Following extraction showed the location itself greatly infected and in ruin. The large amounts of ch-002 and ch-003 were either captured or disposed of, and any natural lifeforms were put down."
		"Reviewed security footage showed ch-005 attacking researchers, often retreating after each attack before returning. Reviewers noticed that &lwhen it attacked or took damage, ch-005 released what appeared to be blood clots.&r After a small collection had been left and not destroyed, &lit howled and the clots took on a life of their own as copies of the original&r. Designated ch-005-1, these copies were weaker than the original, but also showed the ability to leave blood clots, though it was unable to create more ch-005-1. &lThe ability seems to only be present in the original cs-005.&r"
	]
	quest.5B76548804FFB620.title: "ch-005 \"Blood Spreader\""
	quest.5B841122EFD8854C.quest_desc: [
		"Whether you've wanted to take an existing piece of armor to the next level or add on to a freshly forged weapon, at one point or another, a &o&6Simple Reforging Table&r will be something to look at crafting."
		"Using it, you will be met with three slots. The Reforging Table works much like an enchanting table. In the center goes the item you wish to reforge, the bottom right holds your &6&oSigils of Rebirth&r, think of it as your Lapis Lazuli, and the top left holds the rarity material corresponding to your desired rarity. The base table can only reforge items up to &9&oRare&r For more than that, you'll need to upgrade it."
		"With all items in place, you will be presented with three options, again like an enchanting table. Each option &6&oconsumes experience, Sigils of Rebirth, and Rarity Materials&r. No option is inherently better than the other, so pick your favourite, and you can always reroll again."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/simple-reforging-table.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5B841122EFD8854C.title: "Given New Purpose"
	quest.5B9D08BF34A3396B.quest_desc: [
		"We all need sleep, and that includes our little, or big, friends. A &6&opet bed&r will act the same way for your pet that your own bed does for you, &6&oletting them respawn if they die&r."
		"I, Professor Larch, find this to be a true life saver. You'll know your pet has claimed the bed when Zs appear over their head. Do note the pet will only respawn at dawn."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/pet-bed.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5B9D08BF34A3396B.title: "Pets Need Sleep, Too "
	quest.5C13443DAF789830.title: "8x Iron Ingots"
	quest.5C4476807C0C4A7B.quest_desc: ["Now this is where we get interesting. This scroll will let you teleport to &oany&r known waystone, almost like you're using one yourself. It'll even negate the experience cost for you. One use though, so make it count."]
	quest.5C4476807C0C4A7B.title: "Warp Scroll"
	quest.5CC74FC9F8E587B1.quest_desc: ["The Drakkar is a massive viking-style ship for up to 11 passengers, with slow speed and average strength, but the ability to break through the ice of frozen waters. Up to 10 shields can be added to its side for increased defense."]
	quest.5DB70BF3CCF1E5C9.title: "Custom Order Coming Up"
	quest.5DFEA58465571979.quest_desc: [
		"More recent than the alchemist set is the Warrior Set. This armor is stronger than its sibling, almost on par with Diamond Armor, and grants special bonuses when fully worn."
		"Through the helmet, you can weaken your foes with a deafening roar. The chestplate, trade speed for raw power. The leggings, dash through the air in a tornado of flesh and bone. And the boots, land gracefully from tall heights."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/warrior-set.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5DFEA58465571979.title: "A Warrior's Plate"
	quest.5E209C436D651716.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ext_bar.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Using the energy of extraterrestrial crystals and phantom membrane, technicians were able to create a barrier generator that protected the site and its surroundings from meteor showers."
	]
	quest.5E209C436D651716.title: "ext_bar.jv"
	quest.5F5DB67F6A470C73.quest_subtitle: "Hire 30 Guards"
	quest.5FF18EB0CE40B71B.quest_desc: [
		"So, you've been introduced to a world of creativity and challenges. I, Professor Larch, welcome you with open arms."
		"Now then, let's get you fitted with the basics, shall we? As a wise man once said, it all begins with a tree, then an upgrade. We'll get started on that first one now."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/tree-chopping.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
		"When you go to cut down a tree, you'll likely notice something. Indeed, not all trees are chopped at the same speed. Some may take longer than others. But, as long as you keep going, all trees, big or small, will fall. After they do, you'll be given their blocks and any other items from them at the base of the stump you destroyed. Quite convenient. But do be aware that felling a tree will use the same durability as if you had destroyed all the blocks manually yourself."
	]
	quest.5FF18EB0CE40B71B.quest_subtitle: "Chop a tree (You don't need an axe)"
	quest.5FF18EB0CE40B71B.title: "How much wood"
	quest.5FFB17F64270A154.title: "Vault of Enchantments"
	quest.602B6817D394000D.quest_desc: ["There's the question, that in this world and all that it contains, all the weapons forged from nothing, can even bone be turned into a weapon. Perhaps something sharp may do the trick, if not on land, then certainly in the sea. &6&oUnder the water, such a serrated blade is sure to do more harm.&r"]
	quest.602B6817D394000D.title: "A Serrated Sword"
	quest.606A9C8CAB93DE34.quest_desc: ["A &oPlain&r rod, fishing luck is increased in sunlight."]
	quest.60894743B2741EC1.quest_desc: ["A planter can be used to farm any plant or crop without requiring water. It is also unable to be trampled like Rich Soil"]
	quest.60894743B2741EC1.title: "Decoration for The Rich"
	quest.60926B401C87CB94.quest_desc: ["A parrot familiar is no different from a regular tamed parrot, and its main use, besides company, is to aid in the summoning of a Drikwing. There are two ways of obtaining a parrot. Using string, the parrot is summoned as a bound familiar, but using an egg, it is summoned untamed."]
	quest.60926B401C87CB94.title: "Parrot Familiar"
	quest.60C544DE193C1953.title: "Expert Nether Ritual"
	quest.610AEA5B82729D80.quest_desc: [
		"To think the ancient beings were responsible for the scourge of the overworld. I suppose that happens when you try to play god and revive the dead."
		"I wonder... could we recreate such a feat with &6some soul filled blocks and skulls of our own&r? Perhaps there are clues in the fortresses."
		""
		"{image:minecraft:textures/painting/wither.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.610AEA5B82729D80.title: "A Force Of Corruption"
	quest.61758C232C6FC42C.quest_desc: ["Requires Haunting Scroll"]
	quest.61C405313FC828E3.quest_desc: ["Bobbers are purely cosmetic in nature, but definitely give your fishing rod some personality. They can all be crafted with a slime ball, wooden planks, and an item specific to the bobber itself."]
	quest.61C405313FC828E3.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Bobber"
	quest.61C405313FC828E3.title: "Bob and Wave"
	quest.61D9F90B24B0679C.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ext_stl_tol.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Researchers and forges worked to put together a complete set of tools using the unknown metal, ch-101, informally referred to as Extraterrestrial Steel. Like the weapons also forged, the metal proved effective in &lbypassing the natural resistance of technoflesh organisms&r."
		"The tools themselves prove powerful, easily matching diamond tools in strength but not in durability."
	]
	quest.61D9F90B24B0679C.title: "ext_stl_tol.jv"
	quest.6282BFF8E9934E2A.quest_desc: [
		"The Leviathan and Scylla are two sides of the same coin. It is said that the Sunken eye was shattered by the pair long ago, and now each hold a shard. You will need to combine both to restore the eye to its former glory."
		"The Leviathan is found within The Sunken City, a place one could easily call the abyss. "
		"&bScylla&r, known also as the Storm Empress, is found in the hovering lands of Acropolis. A mighty place, found high within the clouds. An Eye of Storm may be capable of leading one to this mighty palace. True to her name, lightning is Scylla's ally, and your biggest enemy. Be wary of her attacks, as some may be able to pierce through even the toughest armor. Do this, and the shard she holds will be yours."
		""
		"Obtained from The Leviathan or Scylla"
	]
	quest.6349B7742FE88ADF.quest_desc: ["The Shelf of Hellbound Rectification is an upgraded form of the Shelf of Seabound Rectification &6&othat further increases the Rectification attribute&r."]
	quest.634ACDA4857B1A62.quest_desc: [
		"The result of waiting for compost to decompose is Rich Soil, a very powerful block for growing plants. Any plant or fungi placed on rich soil will have its growth accelerated, with mushrooms resulting in something very unique."
		"Unlike normal farmland, rich soil cannot be hydrated by methods such as rain, and require nearby water. Also unique to it, rich soil cannot be trampled by mobs or by blocks like pumpkins and melons."
	]
	quest.634ACDA4857B1A62.title: "Pay to Play"
	quest.639F18460A94F794.title: "Archwood"
	quest.63FE95E91D565AE0.quest_desc: [
		"Rolling is great for avoiding many attacks, but there are times you simply need to take the blow. In these cases, a shield is your best ally. Simply holding one in your hands will decrease the damage you take from incoming attacks."
		"But simply holding a shield is one thing. It's another to &6&oblock&r&r with it. Blocking with a shield will completely negate most attacks. Be careful, however, as weapons such as axes may damage your shield, disabling it for a small period of time."
	]
	quest.63FE95E91D565AE0.title: "Block the haters"
	quest.64084A2EAFBE2B7F.quest_desc: ["Nobody is truly alone in the world. Why, just look at the many settlements, villages, dotted around the world. I, Professor Larch, am amazed at the varrying style and scale some of these villages have. They tend to have Waystones, so you don't need to worry too much about the closest one being far, far away."]
	quest.64084A2EAFBE2B7F.title: "Villages to Venture"
	quest.646B634356763676.quest_desc: ["An &oHeroic&r rod, you can sometimes catch extra loot with it."]
	quest.6494A9980556064A.quest_desc: [
		"The Dimensional Mineshaft is a portal housed by a Djinni with access to an uninhabited dimension with a plethora of materials. Due to its small size, humanoid beings cannot enter it, but spirits can use the usage of a lamp."
		"Lamps with spirits housing them can be inserted into the mineshaft through its top, and materials and findings can be extracted through its sides."
	]
	quest.6494A9980556064A.title: "Miner Spirits"
	quest.64CACC32F8670740.quest_desc: [
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"So, you \"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"prob\"},{\"text\":\"ably don't want to b\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"e const\"},{\"text\":\"antly giving the ma\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"chines meat fo\"},{\"text\":\"r nutrients, right? Well, you have the Bio-Forge now, so you can make a \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"Digester\"},{\"text\":\".\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"The Digester\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\" is ra\"},{\"text\":\"ther simple. You put any\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\" sort of \"},{\"text\":\"organic material like meat or plants inside, and it'll convert them into \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"Nutrient Paste\"},{\"text\":\". This is a great sou\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\"rce of n\"},{\"text\":\"utrients, and\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\" when compr\"},{\"text\":\"essed into \"},{\"italic\":true,\"color\":\"gold\",\"text\":\"Nutrient Bars\"},{\"text\":\", can\"},{\"font\":\"biomancy:caro_invitica\",\"text\":\" be a\"},{\"text\":\" very good option for food.\"}],\"text\":\"\"}"
		"{\"text\":\"I don't remember the last time I've had anything else.\"}"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/digester.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.64CACC32F8670740.title: "Nutritious and Delicious"
	quest.64DB6AB811975E9A.quest_desc: [
		"Familiars are like pets, but rather than being tamed, they are bound to your very being. They give their owner buffs, and at times will fight for them. These buffs often require the familiar be close to their owner."
		"When hurt, familiars can be healed with Demon's Dream, Demon's Dream Essence, or Otherworldly Essence"
	]
	quest.64DB6AB811975E9A.title: "Familiars"
	quest.6582DCB124CE4A9F.quest_desc: ["{\"font\": \"alt\",\"text\":\"I won't let you, not yet.\"}"]
	quest.6582DCB124CE4A9F.title: "You Won't Die"
	quest.65D23E7683812E26.quest_desc: [
		"What kind of a leader are you?! Your citizens are so hungry, they are eating rotten flesh! &eAre you eating rotten flesh?&r Can you spare some bread or apples for the colony? "
		""
		"It is strongly suggested that you build a restaurant and any of the 5 herding huts or a fisher’s hut. If you have those buildings already, check that buildings have the resources they need to work."
	]
	quest.65D60C5290E5786B.quest_desc: [
		"to level up you need to place a Stone Altar with 4 Stone Altar Fire Bowls (in a 3 block radius). You must lit the fire bowls with a torch or flint and steel. After that you can insert Liver \\& Cracked Bones into the altar. To start the ritual you must right-click the altar with Flint \\& Steel or a (Soul) Torch."
		"For level 2, 3 livers and 2 cracked bones are required, and you must have killed 50 mobs."
	]
	quest.65D60C5290E5786B.title: "Learn about the altar"
	quest.65D9302038D75A53.quest_desc: [
		"The Raevyx is a rare, combat-oriented dragon species known for its nomadic behavior, aerial agility, and calculated aggression. Unlike more instinct-driven dragons, Raevyxians exhibit complex emotional awareness and inherited social behaviors, making their upbringing and handling particularly important. &4&nIn the wild, they will not actively target a person without reason.&r"
		"Before a Raevyx can be tamed, &4&nit must first be subdued in combat&r. Wild Raevyxians become vulnerable only after their health is &4&nreduced to approximately 60 HP&r, causing the dragon to enter a stunned state. Once stunned, the dragon may be fed preferred foods such as &n&4raw cod, salmon, beef, and Hearty Dragon Meal&r."
		"Feeding a Raevyx does not guarantee successful taming. Failed attempts will restore a portion of the dragon's health, immediately ending its stunned state and forcing the player to subdue it again."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/raevyx.png width:300 height:129 align:center}"
	]
	quest.65D9302038D75A53.quest_subtitle: "Tame a Raevyx"
	quest.65D9302038D75A53.title: "Bleeding Bolt"
	quest.663022ABC71F924C.quest_desc: ["The Chaos Component serves as a base for most elixirs, created with seeds of chaos and water"]
	quest.666AC968E52F94F6.quest_desc: ["Your bait can be improved, used to craft two special types. One of these is lucky bait. While it doesn't increase fishing speed, &6&oit provides a good increase in luck, akin to the Luck Of The Sea enchantment&r."]
	quest.666AC968E52F94F6.quest_subtitle: "Craft Lucky Bait"
	quest.666AC968E52F94F6.title: "One Day It'll Run Out"
	quest.66BA8C0F224F38F0.quest_desc: ["The Ancient Builders were said to have retreated underground long ago, building &6&osprawling cities within the Deepslate caves&r. How unfortunate, then, that in doing so, they flew too close to the sun and &6&oopened a gateway to The Otherside&r, welcoming in The Warden and its sculking mass. If you find such a relic, you are sure to obtain some truly wonderful loot."]
	quest.66BA8C0F224F38F0.title: "City of Sculk"
	quest.66E6F27F50A996CB.quest_desc: [
		"Certain enchantments can not typically be obtained through an Enchanting Table. These are &o&6Treasure Enchantments&r. You probably know about the most popular treasure enchantment, &oMending&r."
		"&o&6The Deepshelf of Arcane Treasures&r changes this, adding Treasure Enchantments to the list of enchantments one can obtain through the Enchanting Table. Do not celebrate too early, however, as many &o&4curses&r are also treasure enchantments, and will be added to the lists."
	]
	quest.671A213F5059C4E7.quest_desc: ["You're probably gonna be catching a lot of fish, right? With all the different sizes you'll get, you may want to nab yourself a Fish Satchel. Open and close it by using the item, or put a fish in by right clicking in the gui. Best part? &6&oWhile it's open, the satchel will automatically store any fish you catch.&r"]
	quest.671A213F5059C4E7.title: "Bags of Fish"
	quest.671F5E4584CD5C25.quest_desc: ["The Diamond Fishing Line massively lowers a fish's speed, causing the slider in the fishing minigame to move much slower."]
	quest.671F5E4584CD5C25.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Diamond Fishing Line"
	quest.671F5E4584CD5C25.title: "Diamonds Sparkling in The Sea"
	quest.6728C3AC474508DF.title: "time 1"
	quest.673800544C41DE7D.title: "Fog"
	quest.67E1F1698D957610.quest_desc: [
		"A difficult fight lies ahead of you to claim the Legendary Eye, for Maledictus can never truly be killed. Even so, his defeat at your hands will be all you need."
		"Maledictus is rageful, &6&ogetting stronger with each attack that hits its mark&r. At his rage's full potential, even simple strikes may become lethal to the unprepared. His mastery over &6close range maces, dexterous halberds, and long range bows&r will quickly become apparent. The bands around his arm indicate his attacks, with green being blockable, orange blockable but disabling shields, and red unblockable."
		"&6&oBe patient, be smart, and you will leave this room a champion.&r"
	]
	quest.67E1F1698D957610.title: "To Seal a King's Soul"
	quest.67E8B8DCFC93F832.quest_desc: ["The warehouse is completed. It might not seem like much, but you can't have much of a trade empire without a place to store things. "]
	quest.68500900087F92BC.quest_subtitle: "Teach a Carpenter to Craft a Door"
	quest.68DA08FB4647A681.title: "Kill supreme b0onescaller"
	quest.68FC81E133443E76.quest_desc: [
		"The Library is a way for you to raise your adult citizens’ Intelligence skill, which influences skill increases once employed. A citizen will randomly level up their Intelligence as long as they’re assigned to the Library. Paper and books help Library Students increase their skills faster."
		""
		"Being a Library Student is a full-time job, and a student cannot be employed simultaneously at any other hut."
		""
		"Tip: Consider setting the hiring mode to automatic so new recruits or kids growing up will start school automatically."
	]
	quest.68FC81E133443E76.quest_subtitle: "Build a Library"
	quest.69248DB421B51F6E.quest_desc: ["Your bait can be improved, used to craft two special types. One of these is magnetic bait. It increases fishing speed like your basic bait, but &6&oalso greatly increases the chance of fishing up a crate&r."]
	quest.69248DB421B51F6E.quest_subtitle: "Craft Magnetic Bait"
	quest.69248DB421B51F6E.title: "Quite The Magnetic Personality"
	quest.696BDC29ACCBBE29.quest_desc: ["Just make sure you have unlocked the research \"Raising the Dead\"..."]
	quest.696BDC29ACCBBE29.quest_subtitle: "Give the Undertaker a Totem"
	quest.69BEEF688AA76D82.quest_desc: ["A Dolphin is an interesting creature. Swimming alongside one will grant you the Dolphin's Grace, speeding up travel drastically. What's more, if you feed a dolphin a fish and gain its favor, it will lead you directly to a shipwreck"]
	quest.69BEEF688AA76D82.title: "Grace of Dolphins"
	quest.69D9D1F047C4B892.quest_desc: [
		"Diving into the Deep Dark is no simple task, but you've achieved it. Even moreso, you have likely discovered an Ancient City. &6&oBut to slay its ultimate protector, The Warden, is no simple task.&r That said, the rewards are great indeed."
		"&6&oThe Sculkshelves&r are upgraded forms of Deepshelves utilizing the tendrils of a Warden, &6&oallowing one to reach enchantments of Level 80&r."
	]
	quest.69D9D1F047C4B892.title: "Behold Its True Power!"
	quest.69EAF1072D492F1A.quest_desc: [
		"The Ancient Tome is a glowing book that’s dropped by raiders during raids. If you have the Ancient Tome in your inventory, it will glow when there is going to be a raid that night. "
		""
		"In the later game, the Enchanter can convert Ancient Tomes into enchanted books. "
	]
	quest.69EAF1072D492F1A.quest_subtitle: "Keep one in your hotbar"
	quest.69F42AC6CA4A0032.quest_desc: ["The Greedy familiar will pick up nearby items for its master. When in a Familiar Ring, it increases its holder's pick up range. In addition, it can ride a Dragon Familiar, giving the dragon the same abilities. When upgraded, it can be given a block to search for more of the same block."]
	quest.69F42AC6CA4A0032.title: "Greedy Familiar"
	quest.6A3B7FC7807367FE.quest_desc: ["If you're truly into fishing, you're going to want a &6&oFishing Journal&r. This beauty of a tracker takes note of every fish you've caught, along with the conditions required to catch more. What's even better, &6&oyou'll find the details of all previously read Fishy Notes&r. No need to carry around so many papers when you've got it all sorted out in here."]
	quest.6A3B7FC7807367FE.title: "Notetaker"
	quest.6A60B76053393288.quest_desc: ["The Smeltery is where the Smelter will smelt ores into ingots. The higher the level of the Smeltery, the more furnaces the Smelter will be able to use. A higher level will also have a higher chance to double and even triple the ingot output per block of ore."]
	quest.6A60B76053393288.quest_subtitle: "Builder a Smelter"
	quest.6A9B9DB71F967F74.quest_desc: [
		"You may be wondering, \"If I need to constantly eat a variety of foods, won't that fill up my inventory?\" And you would be correct. That's where the &o&6lunchbag&r comes into play."
		"Crouching and right clicking will open the bag's menu, wherein you can place up to &ofive different foods&r. From there, the bag can be used as a food item itself. When eating from the bag, &o&6it will automatically pick a food from its contents that best keeps your diversity level high&r."
	]
	quest.6A9B9DB71F967F74.title: "Don't Forget Lunch!"
	quest.6B0CE8AD86991E28.quest_desc: [
		"The Composter’s Hut is where the Composter will turn organic materials into compost, which can be used by the Farmer or Florist to fertilize crops or flowers. "
		""
		"Note: You must configure the composter’s hut with the items you want composted before the composter will compost. &7&oThis sounds similar to a woodchuck tongue twister.&r"
	]
	quest.6B0CE8AD86991E28.quest_subtitle: "Build a Composter Hut"
	quest.6B26495A9E7D77FC.quest_desc: ["Here's a bed, you will probably need more."]
	quest.6B26495A9E7D77FC.quest_subtitle: "Have a Baby"
	quest.6B2AC9F66E18B5C6.quest_desc: ["A rather simple weapon, merely poisoning those hit."]
	quest.6B43C3734794C3D7.quest_desc: ["The Quadrocopter is a small aircraft designed to aid in building. It is unique in that it does not follow the same side to side controls that other rotary aircrafts do. Instead, holding A and D will simply move you to the left and right respectively. Turning is done via the mouse like normal gameplay."]
	quest.6B4B90EFD206B3A9.title: "Reach level 14"
	quest.6B733345FAD245D0.quest_desc: ["So the satchel is nice, but you want even &omore&r storage from your meals. Well, there is one last upgrade. By turning your satchel into a Picnic Basket, it gains 5 additional slots for food&r."]
	quest.6B733345FAD245D0.title: "Going Somewhere?"
	quest.6B80B2314CC47FD6.quest_desc: ["A level 3 smeltery applies Fortune II when smelting ores! "]
	quest.6B80B2314CC47FD6.quest_subtitle: "Fortune II"
	quest.6B9B91887BF3FB7B.quest_desc: ["Obtained from an Ancient Remnant"]
	quest.6B9B91887BF3FB7B.quest_subtitle: "The Remnant"
	quest.6BB0C51EE8CA5966.quest_desc: [
		"At the Mine, the Miner will mine for ores and materials. Once they are hired, the Miner will first create a shaft downward to a specific depth depending on the level of the Mine. Once the main shaft is completed, the Miner will then branch out. While mining, sometimes the Miner will get lucky and get an ore block instead of a basic stone block. &7&o(magic!)&r&r"
		""
		"Tip: The miner fills holes and gaps with a Fill Block, cobblestone by default. However, the fill block can be changed in the Miner’s Hut settings. If you have a forester and lots of wood, consider using wood planks. Or perhaps now you will have a use for all that deepslate."
	]
	quest.6BB0C51EE8CA5966.quest_subtitle: "Build a Mine"
	quest.6BE3A91F70079E4E.title: "1x Potion of Fire Resistance"
	quest.6C751E7948299C82.quest_desc: ["A &oGuardian&r rod, fishing luck is increased in the rain."]
	quest.6CC8ABE47CE50400.quest_desc: [
		"Use to get essences from mobs or yourself. Essences are used for other blocks and flesh chests"
		"ENchanting with surgical precision increases the tier of the essence."
	]
	quest.6D0FB5D28DED4EB6.quest_desc: ["So, you're not quite fond of the Scroll Affixes you've given your items? Well, you can certainly remove them."]
	quest.6D3D534CCE38C433.quest_desc: ["With smelted Worldroot, Echo Shards, and a Dragon Seal Stone I found within ancient cities, I've crated a core that, in theory, may be able to bind a dragon. I just need to find a way to add further connection to a particular species."]
	quest.6D56AD1BEC644A10.quest_desc: [
		"The Archery is where your Archers in Training will train to become Archer. This also allows them to level up without a risk of dying to mobs. "
		""
		"The Archers in Training require a bow to practice. They will shoot at the practice targets, a target block"
		""
		"Tip: Consider setting the hiring mode to automatic so new recruits or kids growing up will automatically start training if not already attending school. "
	]
	quest.6D56AD1BEC644A10.quest_subtitle: "Build an Archery"
	quest.6D9C812CBC680546.quest_desc: [
		"If you're reading this, then you've gotten yourself a fair bit of wood. If not, stop reading ahead, and go back and get some."
		"Now then, provided you've gotten the wood you were supposed to, I, Professor Larch, implore you to &6&ocreate a crafting table&r. You likely know how to make one of these, but if you don't, &o&6Just Enough Items, or JEI, can tell you virtually any recipe.&r Just go over to the right side of your screen. The bar at the bottom can be used to search for particular items."
	]
	quest.6D9C812CBC680546.quest_subtitle: "Craft The Crafting Table To Craft More"
	quest.6D9C812CBC680546.title: "Let's (Mine)craft!"
	quest.6DEED125538775FD.quest_desc: [
		"All good pets need a fitting name! While name tags get the job done, they aren't exactly accessible. To remedy this, we can craft a &6&ocollar tag&r. Not only does this act as a cheaper alternative to name tags, they can also be &oenchanted&r to give your pet a boost. I, Professor Larch, am rather fond of the Charisma enchantment. Crouching will let you see the enchantments on your pet's current collar tag, and exchanging them is as simple as interacting with a second tag."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/collar-tag.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6DEED125538775FD.title: "Do They Have A Name?"
	quest.6E2846C32B27E04F.quest_desc: ["Wild Crops are naturally spawning plants that provide the seeds and starter materials needed to begin farming Farmer’s Delight crops. Seven different variants can be found across the Overworld, each in specific biomes: &aWild Cabbages on beaches&r, &eWild Onions in plains and forests&r, &cWild Tomatoes in hot deserts and savannas&r, &6Wild Carrots in most biomes&r, &eWild Potatoes in forests&r, &cWild Beetroots on beaches and deserts&r, and &7Wild Rice growing in rivers and swamps&r."]
	quest.6E2846C32B27E04F.title: "The Seeds of Our Youth"
	quest.6E4F3993219B451E.quest_desc: ["A step towards remote access, by shift right clicking a storage actuator, the wormhole is bound to it, and placing it down will allow access to said actuator through it. Be warned, however, that breaking it will no give the wormhole back, so be careful when choosing where to put one."]
	quest.6E709CA5EA306336.title: "Hunter of Souls"
	quest.6ED45E65608B8164.quest_desc: [
		"Before the warriors, there were alchemists. Once known as devotees of the primordial ways, their time has been lost. Still, the armor remains, a memorial of what once was."
		"The Bio-Alchemist Armor will give you increased resistance of acid and success with the usage of serums and injections."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/alchemist-set.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6ED45E65608B8164.title: "An Alchemist's Robes"
	quest.6EEA012FA11C7C08.quest_desc: ["Once you have found the location for your colony, you will likely want to build either a supply camp or supply ship. You can choose one but not both. Either will provide you with some basic supplies to help you get started in the early game. &o&7(bed, food, basic tools and armor, starting resources, etc.)&r&r It’s beneficial to place your supply camp or ship near your colony as you will be traveling back and forth to it frequently in the early game. &eClose, but not in the way close.&r"]
	quest.6F0F1C8DF581DC8C.quest_desc: ["Immersive Aircraft adds a variety of flying vehicles to your arsenal. For starters, you're going to want an advanced engine. All but one of the vehicles use one."]
	quest.6F0F1C8DF581DC8C.title: "To Power a Flying Wonder"
	quest.6F26060A50069BF2.quest_desc: [
		"Hooks generally alter the types of fish available to you, allowing you to find certain ones when not quite meeting their conditions naturally. &6&oSome are required to fish in specific areas&r."
		"The basic hook, however, is purely cosmetic."
	]
	quest.6F26060A50069BF2.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Fishing Hook"
	quest.6F26060A50069BF2.title: "Are You Hooked Yet?"
	quest.6F740DA7B65AAEF6.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ind_adj_wrn.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Since its invention, researchers on site near always carried with them the Industrial Adjustable Wrench. It has let them repair certain damaged objects, as well as tweak, disable, or enable specific machinery, including golems."
	]
	quest.6FB8ADE0C08B5542.quest_desc: ["A &oBee&r rod, you can put many types of bait on it."]
	quest.6FCC21B481AA7424.quest_desc: [
		"It is time. Prepare yourself, for Ignis is one who demands upmost respect from his challengers. &o&4Do NOT underestimate his power.&r"
		"Good luck, friend."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/altar-of-fire.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6FCC21B481AA7424.title: "The Immortal Flame"
	quest.6FD4FFBFF9D3EB62.title: "A Tip of The Hats"
	quest.700207112B8CB1E9.quest_subtitle: "The Best Chest"
	quest.701FB25B9128CD42.quest_desc: ["The Cthulhu familiar grants its owner Water Breathing when nearby or in a ring. When upgraded, it also acts as a mobile light source."]
	quest.701FB25B9128CD42.title: "Cthulhu Familiar"
	quest.707A51B4CC38F5F1.quest_desc: ["Iesnium looks like Netherrack at first, but with otherworld goggles, it can be seen and mined with an infused pickaxe. The material is very spiritually charged, and used in many expert recipes and rituals."]
	quest.708195DB8305AD2B.quest_desc: ["The chakram is said to be hard to master, but its passive damage can be very helpful for those keeping their distance."]
	quest.708195DB8305AD2B.title: "Toxic Circles"
	quest.708BF47743F07494.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ch-006.jv"
		"Indentifier: ch-006 | Informal Name: Prowler"
		"-------------------------------------------"
		"At site Remus, researches managed to infect a horse through contact with a ch-001. It seemed to be curious, and that intelligence was shown when it had been thought to have escaped. Upon entering its containment, however, ch-006 revealed itself, &lhaving turned invisble to the naked eye&r, and struck a powerful blow to one of the armed researchers, &lseemingly reducing their armor's strength&r."
		"ch-006's body contains canisters with a substance similar to that of ch-001's projectiles, &lapplying the same neurotoxin effect to another when slashed with its claws or tail&r."
	]
	quest.708BF47743F07494.title: "ch-006 \"Prowler\""
	quest.70A04C140ADBC630.quest_desc: ["Taverns are small buildings offering rest and food via the villagers housed there. Most notably, however, they are a source of structure maps, each showing the location of a specific structure. For an explorer, there's no better method, except maybe special eyes."]
	quest.70EA49198D23A24A.quest_desc: [
		"The End Portal is locked behind 12 magical blocks, each requiring more than a normal eye of ender can give. Instead, one must obtain 12 of the 16 legendary eyes. It does not matter which eyes you obtain, so long as you have 12."
		"This will serve as a log of the eyes you've collected on your journey."
	]
	quest.719D4457588528C8.quest_desc: ["The cog is a medieval trade ship suited for cold waters and up to 5 passengers. It does its job well enough, and might be all you'll really need, with average speed and decent strength."]
	quest.71A3C142D8A78EF7.quest_desc: [
		"When you level up as a vampire, you gain skill points that are used to gain various perks. It must be know, though, that you will not be able to obtain each and every one."
		"In addition, as you grow stronger, so does your weakness to the sun. At level 2, it will weaken you; at level 3, you will grow nauseus; and at any levels above, you will take damage."
	]
	quest.71A3C142D8A78EF7.title: "Learn Skills and Sun Weakness"
	quest.71C633AEF69F91A6.quest_desc: ["Possession Rituals involve the, well, possessing of different creatures to allow for easier obtaining of rarer drops. You've likely already performed one to kill a possessed endermite and obtain end stone used for chalks."]
	quest.71C633AEF69F91A6.title: "Possession"
	quest.71FCF06A98CC66D7.quest_desc: [
		"With so many colonists working for the greater good it can be difficult to know who needs what. The clipboard is an easy way to see all the requests your workers have."
		""
		"&eSneak + right-click&r on your town hall block to register the clipboard."
	]
	quest.7211E9ED86A677EE.quest_desc: [
		"The potion effect &o&4\"Sanguinare Vampiris\"&r is what converts you. &oSaid effect comes from the fangs of a vampire, either from being attacked by one, or by using their dropped fangs on yourself.&r &o&4If not cured, the effect's duration reaching 0, will turn you.&r"
		"Being a vampire seems to have some nice advantages. It seems &o&4most undead will ignore you unless attacked&r. You no longer need to breathe underwater, but it weakens you."
	]
	quest.7211E9ED86A677EE.title: "Infectious"
	quest.725FBF759BC307C8.title: "Diggy Diggy Hole 2"
	quest.72C749AD9F1C634E.quest_desc: [
		"Citizens will go to the Residence they are assigned to at night to sleep. The Residence is also a way to get more citizens for your colony. Every residence level adds another bed. More beds means more citizen capacity."
		""
		"It’s worth considering residence locations and the citizens they house. Workers get grumpy when they have to travel long distances to work. Try to move citizens into homes close to where they work. "
	]
	quest.72C749AD9F1C634E.quest_subtitle: "Build a Residence"
	quest.72FFC043391FC449.quest_desc: ["For more advanced rituals, you'll need gold chalk. This is crafted like white chalk, and processed through the same method of throwing the impure chalk into spirit fire"]
	quest.72FFC043391FC449.title: "Chalk 2.0"
	quest.731B4F00F1A94F19.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat nrg_glv.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Created as part of the Techointegration Project, the Energy Glove is capable of storing up energy within itself, allowing a user's critical attacks create an electrical surge, stunning entities hit and charging the user's other electronic devices."
		"Due to its heavy firepower and small form factor, the glove must recharge after every usage of its surge."
	]
	quest.731B4F00F1A94F19.title: "nrg_glv.jv"
	quest.732DDBE332DE607F.quest_desc: ["Ars Noveau is a magic mod focused around spell creation and automation"]
	quest.7344913F87F8F4A3.title: "Taking Prisoners"
	quest.7360CC59A2A52088.quest_desc: ["Worldroot, being as powerful as it is, proves to be stronger than Diamond tier tools, but not quite at the level of Netherite. Regardless, it is a powerful asset."]
	quest.7360CC59A2A52088.title: "Tools Rooted in Strength"
	quest.73837610E788A3CD.quest_desc: [
		"Legends tell of Ancient Builders who once created these temples, back before the sea rose to drown it. A mix of biological and magical, the Guardians that roam its surroundings fend off would-be-intruders with concentrated prismatic light. It's best that you don't let them win any staring contests."
		"The Ocean Temple is a structure worth its troubles. Rewarding with riches and Sponges from the 3 Elder Guardians, as well as a bountiful supply of Prismarine Shards and Crystals. Indeed, you don't want to miss this."
	]
	quest.73837610E788A3CD.title: "The Sea's Temple"
	quest.741E225D8F31C175.quest_desc: ["You can use a blood grinder to extract blood from items, but it will be impure, and undrinkable at first"]
	quest.743D7D9204915A13.quest_subtitle: "Burry Your First Citizen"
	quest.7494BD5420DD948B.title: "Diggy Diggy Hole 0"
	quest.74B74B738FDAA691.quest_desc: [
		"bishop@romulus:~$ cat ext_stl_smp.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"___Report Date: 1982-06-25___"
		"An unknown metal was taken from sites of meteor showers alongside small rocks and a living specimen. Analysis of small samples revealed a structure similar in shape to that of steel. Properties have yet to be fully analyzed. A larger sample may be required."
	]
	quest.74B74B738FDAA691.title: "ext_stl_smp.jv"
	quest.74C114D0C0D4D374.quest_desc: ["Remember in the beginning how it seemed that everyone was sick with Influenza and you had to keep feeding everyone carrots and potatoes? With the hospital built, they can go see the doctor and get cured by the Healer. You or the colony still needs to supply the ingredients."]
	quest.74C114D0C0D4D374.quest_subtitle: "Build a Hospital"
	quest.750F9DC2755C097F.quest_desc: [
		"When you open a crafting table for the first time, you'll be met with some new values. These are Eterna, Quanta, and Arcana. They are your primary attributes, and values you'll learn more of as you progress."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/enchanting.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.75599A9909C7A8C8.quest_desc: ["Citizens need to eat in order to work. Until you have a restaurant and a steady supply of food, you will need to put a few pieces of food in their inventory. They’ll eat when they are hungry."]
	quest.75599A9909C7A8C8.title: "Another Mouth to Feed"
	quest.758F00009EFA6E27.quest_desc: ["So if you've seen the flesh spread long enough, you've probably come across some &o&6Gastric Acid&r, right? This stuff is highly corosive. While a bucket works when it's spilled on the ground, you can &o&6use an organic vial on the orifice that produces it&r to gather it in a more portable form."]
	quest.75ADCF86A6F6B50C.quest_desc: ["The Guardian Familiar is summoned with a random number of limbs. Upon its user taking fatal damage, it will sacrifice one of its limbs to prevent the user's death. Once all limbs are used up, the familiar dies. A blacksmith familiar can repair a single limb, bringing it back."]
	quest.75ADCF86A6F6B50C.title: "Guardian Familiar"
	quest.75B955D121D3B267.quest_subtitle: "Three Stack"
	quest.75CBFD0F90772359.quest_desc: [
		"Cliches aside, the tavern should be a high priority building in the early game for several reasons. A tavern can house four colonists. Exactly the number that spawned when you created your village. "
		""
		"After completing the tavern, visitors will stop by to hang out in hopes of being recruited into your colony. You can recruit these visitors by giving them the items they request. "
		""
		"You may want to check out their stats before recruiting a visitor because nobody wants to pay too much for a rubbish colonist."
		""
		"&o&8PRO TIP: You can tell a lot about a potential recruit by looking at their boots. Fancy boots, better stats.&r&r"
	]
	quest.75CBFD0F90772359.quest_subtitle: "Build a Tavern"
	quest.75CBFD0F90772359.title: "You All Meet In a Tavern..."
	quest.75F46ED3CD1FE1A7.quest_desc: [
		"With this, we have come to the end of our introduction. The Dark Arts will now open for you. Many powerful artifacts and spells lay there, waiting to be discovered. &8Necromancy&r, &2Nature&r, &1The Abyss&r, &bWinds&r, &eStorms&r, &dGeomancy&r."
		"With so many options, what will &oyou&r choose? I look forward to finding out."
	]
	quest.75F46ED3CD1FE1A7.title: "A Dark Graduation"
	quest.75FCBE55E779DB8B.quest_desc: ["Because the blood from a blood grinder is impure, it must be filtered through a blood sieve to become drinkable. Placing it with a blood case below and a case above with pure blood will let it act like a hopper"]
	quest.7636F7B646A967FD.quest_desc: ["The Shelf of Seabound Rectification is a unique bookshelf that does not increase any of the three primary attributes. &6&oInstead, it raises Rectification by a large amount.&r"]
	quest.76E6E295FDCA2A3D.quest_desc: ["An elegant solution for the need to eat Demon's Dream in order to get the Third Eye effect are Otherworld Goggles. Before you obtain these, however, you must craft Lenses"]
	quest.76E6E295FDCA2A3D.title: "Seeing Things a Bit Clearer"
	quest.7727C53B1B821455.quest_desc: [
		"Have you heard about illagers? Strange cousins to the villagers, and much less peaceful. You might come across a group of pillagers, but beware the one with a banner, for it will give you a nasty omen with its dying breath."
		"&6&oVillage raids&r begin when a player with the Bad Omen effect enters a village. Waves of illagers will come seeking naught but destruction and death, and you'll need to help fend them off. Doing so has its rewards, as you'll be seen a hero in the eyes of the traders. I, Professor Larch, have received many a discount and gift for doing such a feat."
	]
	quest.7727C53B1B821455.title: "Village Defense Squad"
	quest.774A7D8001A081E3.quest_desc: [
		"You've reached level 45, good. Now it's time to learn about &6&oInfusing&r."
		"Infusing is essentially enchanting a block, typically a bookshelf. Unlike regular enchanting, &o&6infusing requires specific amounts of Eterna, Quanta, and Arcana&r. Usually you only need to have at least the required amounts, but there are some cases where you must have less than a specific amount."
		"&6&oUsing Infused Bookshelves, you will be able to reach Level 54 enchantments. But there is more to be done with them.&r"
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/infusing.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.774A7D8001A081E3.title: "Potential Unleashed"
	quest.7756E05A9E7AB29F.quest_desc: [
		"Some say Worldroot is the remnants of an older existence, before the world grew to where it is today. Some say it was from a time where man and monster worked as one. Whatever their origin, &6&oWorldroot remains a powerful material&r."
		"Found embedded in Deepslate and close to the bedrock of the Overworld, Worldroot is especially tough, &6&orequiring at least a diamond tier pickaxe to mine&r. This toughness seems to transfer over to smelting as well, as only the power of a &6&oDraconic Crucible&r can turn this ancient essence into usable ingots of history."
	]
	quest.7756E05A9E7AB29F.title: "Ingots of Origin"
	quest.777005851A20471C.quest_desc: ["Ships are separated by temperatures. While you could use the same boat everywhere, sailing in the appropriate biomes give a 10% speed boost in the right waters and a 10% speed &odecreease&r in the wrong waters."]
	quest.7790867215971C3C.quest_desc: ["Not one for mining, ay? Well, I'd say it can be worth the trouble most times, but if you need a little push, I can cover ya, for a fee of coure."]
	quest.7790867215971C3C.title: "16x Cobblestone"
	quest.779A26C471E80278.quest_desc: [
		"Tier 4 Tools are Netherite Equivilants or better, and while Tier 5 exists within the world, I am afriad I have now taught you all I know, You have the makings of being a better Smith then even this old dwarf."
		""
		"Now, Get out there, and show the world your creations!"
	]
	quest.779A26C471E80278.quest_subtitle: "You HAVE, Earned the Rank of Master"
	quest.779A26C471E80278.title: "Tier 4 Tools"
	quest.77CF8C796B164B27.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ful-cry.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Researchers noticed the energy crystals had an affinity towards colder climate. When fully encased, they resulted in what's now known informally as &lCryogenic Fuel&r, a deathly cold substance."
	]
	quest.77CF8C796B164B27.title: "ful-cry.jv"
	quest.78025406C5AF87EA.quest_desc: [
		"Obtained from fishing"
		"{image:aquaculture:item/treasure_chest width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.781F913DAC8B393B.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat ext_act_rdr.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"In order to better understand and obtain sample data, the site technicians and scientists created a radar capable of putting out a redstone signal when detecting extraterrestrial movement in the sky, effectively &ldetecting meteor showers&r."
	]
	quest.781F913DAC8B393B.title: "ext_act_rdr.jv"
	quest.78646EB5642CD915.quest_desc: ["To make harvesting Otherwood easier, one can summon a Foliot Sapling Trader, who will take an ordinary oak sapling and exchange it for a Stable Otherworld Sapling. These saplings will grow into trees that do not require the Third Eye effect to break and will even give normal Otherworld Saplings."]
	quest.78646EB5642CD915.title: "Otherworldly Trees For Sale"
	quest.786D983E45D03A2F.quest_desc: [
		"&o&4Faction controlled villages&r are protected and occupied by one of the three factions. While exploring, you may find a village already with a fragile totem. If not, you can make a base and head yourself."
		"When claimed by a faction, all workstations and beds will be claimed by that faction. Right clicking a totem head not belonging to you will start &oa raid&r in which some of the attacking faction will spawn and try to take out the current possessors."
		"Right clicking a village totem not belonging to you will start &oa raid&r wherein the attacking faction will begin spawning and must be fought off by the defending faction. Raids can also occur randomly, or by entering a village with the Bad Omen effect from another faction."
	]
	quest.786D983E45D03A2F.title: "Village of Vampires"
	quest.7870800C28A7E199.quest_desc: [
		"The Chicken Farmer’s Hut is where the Chicken Farmer will raise chickens, collect eggs, and butcher chickens for food. You will have to capture and bring in two chickens to the Chicken Farmer’s Hut, as the Chicken Farmer will not catch and bring in any chickens."
		""
		"The Chicken Farmer will only keep two chickens alive per hut level, so at level 5 they will have ten chickens."
	]
	quest.7870800C28A7E199.quest_subtitle: "Build a Chicken Farmer's Hut"
	quest.78D798DD080DD1E4.quest_desc: [
		"The Atroxiia is an ancient cryomancy-adapted lindworm species inhabiting frozen mountain ranges, glacial valleys, and polar frontiers. Rather than overwhelming prey through relentless pursuit, Atroxiia establish dominance by exerting precise control over the terrain itself, reshaping the battlefield through specialized cryomantic abilities channeled primarily through the tail. Their composed temperament, territorial discipline, and unusually regal demeanor have inspired countless legends depicting them as forgotten monarchs or divine guardians of winter, though such accounts remain unverified. Despite their measured behavior, an Atroxiia becomes exceptionally dangerous once provoked, relying on calculated force rather than prolonged aggression. &4&nAny meetings will likely be hostile.&r"
		"Before an Atroxiia can be tamed, &4&nit must first be subdued in combat&r. Wild Atroxiia become vulnerable only after their health is &4&nreduced to approximately 60 HP&r, causing the dragon to enter a stunned state. Once stunned, the dragon may be fed preferred foods such as &n&4raw cod, salmon, beef, porkchops, mutton, chicken, and Hearty Dragon Meal&r."
		"Feeding an Atroxiia does not guarantee successful taming. Failed attempts will restore a portion of the dragon's health, immediately ending its stunned state and forcing the player to subdue it again."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/atroxiia.png width:481 height:113 align:center}"
	]
	quest.78D798DD080DD1E4.quest_subtitle: "Tame an Atroxiia"
	quest.78D798DD080DD1E4.title: "The False Pharaoh"
	quest.7911F84EA2E2FDA6.quest_desc: [
		"kane@remus:~$ cat mtn_sns.jv"
		"------------------------------"
		"Utilizing cybernetic optics found in the mouths of [REAPER], researchers were able to create a new type of sensor that can detect entities within 15 blocks of its field of vision, and let out a redstone signal of corresponding strength."
	]
	quest.7911F84EA2E2FDA6.title: "mtn_sns.jv"
	quest.7980B96B5E47711B.quest_desc: ["The galley is a naval warfare ship suited to warm waters. It's got average speed and strength, but can carry up to 9 passengers."]
	quest.79AEECE2AD7C75C1.quest_desc: [
		"Technically not a familiar, the Demonic Wife and Husband are bound to their partner through a marriage contract."
		"If given a raw food item, they will cook it. If given a potion, they will grant the effect to their partner for a greater period of time. In addition, they will fight alongside their partner."
	]
	quest.79AEECE2AD7C75C1.title: "Demonic Husband"
	quest.7A7BB1012C68BD96.quest_desc: ["Briggs are large medieval trade ships suited to cold waters. Their increased size makes it good for transporting a lot of cargo and up to 11 passengers. It's speed and strength are both good as well."]
	quest.7A7BB1012C68BD96.title: "Brigg"
	quest.7AB7E23B8A7D40FA.title: "Lakes and Rivers"
	quest.7B1E7D944854185E.quest_desc: [
		"All Tools can be modified and all materials have it's own modifier that effects the tool, and effects each kind of tool differently."
		""
		"For Example: Adding Redstone to your pickaxe gives it Haste! Which allows you to mine faster much like the Efficency enchantment!"
	]
	quest.7B1E7D944854185E.quest_subtitle: "Craft a Modifier Worktable"
	quest.7B1E7D944854185E.title: "Adapt, Modify, Overcome"
	quest.7B36440BC7FD9165.title: "Thunderous Applause"
	quest.7B396A381FC50D4E.quest_desc: [
		"To call forth &4&oIgnis&r, one must first claim the ashes of an Ignited Revenant. These monsters are powerful guards of the Burning Arena, wielding several shields to protect them. But, just like your own shields, &6&oan axe can make quick work of them&r."
		"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/ignited_revenant.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7B396A381FC50D4E.title: "Ashes From Ashes"
	quest.7B5E2CD676A1A1C4.quest_desc: ["The Baker will craft bread dough, cookie dough, cake dough, and raw pumpkin pie, then bake these in a furnace to create bread, cookies, cakes, and pumpkin pies. They will only do this upon request, whether from the Cook, the postbox, or as a minimum stock in the Warehouse."]
	quest.7B5E2CD676A1A1C4.quest_subtitle: "Build a Bakery"
	quest.7B7F34E2C34E28FA.quest_desc: [
